geez/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vageez","id":37623247,"login":"vageez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIzMjQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/runtime-module-composition.dev/commits/400ec9fae419731530ad60f10f10d69e0dc864d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:43:36Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-23T01:43:36Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"message":"Reframe existing-app guide as a peer path, not a migration afterthought\n\nRenamed \"Migrating an Existing App\" to \"Decoupling a Slice from an\nExisting App\" and moved it from an implicit migration narrative to a\nthird parallel entry point on the Quick Start landing page, alongside\nReact and Vue — someone with an existing app can now identify that\npath as directly as picking a framework.\n\nSoftened the closing section: staying on createInjectedModuleBoundary\nindefinitely is presented as a legitimate destination (isolating a\nslice for its own release cadence, ownership, or risk profile), not\njust a stepping-stone before a larger migration. Added a worked\nexample based on a real host integration, kept intentionally minimal\n(no feature flag, no incidental props, no extra deps) so the pattern\nreads clearly on its own.\