ser","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/rmc-toolkit/commits/8a605c657020f716290010b3723a4bff31e0a601/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T05:10:57Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T05:10:57Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"message":"Address code review feedback on DynamicModuleBoundary DI fix\n\n- Add a comment mapping the React.createElement nesting in\n  createDynamicModuleBoundary back to its equivalent JSX shape, clarifying\n  that ErrorBoundary''s `children` prop is a deliberate JSX-children\n  substitute (needed to satisfy createElement''s overload resolution), not\n  an accidental extra prop.\n- Add a comment explaining ErrorBoundary is intentionally redefined on each\n  createDynamicModuleBoundary call (it extends the injected React.Component,\n  so it can''t be hoisted out without a second DI parameter), and that this\n  has no meaningful cost since these factories run once per host app at\n  module scope.\n- Rewrite the index.test.tsx comment that referenced \"see self-review\" (not\n  accessible to a future reader) to state directly, as a static fact, that\n  create-dynamic-module-boundary.ts has no runtime \"react\" import, and that\n  this test instead proves the DI parameter is wired through end-to-end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b10f736b043e1a25e5ed4c35f8801eac5c3cbedb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/rmc-toolkit/git/trees/b10f736b043e1a25e5ed4c35f8801eac5c3cbedb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/rmc-toolkit/git/commits/8a605c657020f716290010b3723a4bff31e0a601","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_ur