23247,"login":"vageez","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIzMjQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vageez","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/rmc-toolkit/commits/ffac2aa1aa07814afca89ce2a498987b5661c2be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T05:05:23Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T05:05:23Z","email":"37623247+vageez@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Angelo Vagenas"},"message":"Fix DynamicModuleBoundary''s two-React-instances bug via dependency injection\n\nApplies the same DI pattern already used for createReactAdapter:\nDynamicModuleBoundary is now produced by a new createDynamicModuleBoundary(React)\nfactory that takes the host app''s own React instance as a parameter instead of\nimporting \"react\" as a runtime value. The factory implementation lives in a new\n.ts (not .tsx) file, create-dynamic-module-boundary.ts, and avoids JSX syntax\nentirely in favor of explicit React.createElement calls, since JSX with\n\"jsx\": \"react-jsx\" would auto-inject an unreconcilable runtime import of\nreact/jsx-runtime -- the same bug one level down.\n\nindex.tsx is renamed to index.ts since it no longer contains JSX or a runtime\nReact import, and now just re-exports both factories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ac321f5901b21caad1fcf70eaf2e44d92573ec8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-module-composition/rmc-toolkit/git/trees/ac321f5901b21caad1fcf70eaf2e44d92573ec8b"},"url":"https://api.github.