"tseitzin"},"authoredDate":"2026-07-04T01:10:21Z","committedDate":"2026-07-04T01:10:21Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"tseitzin","providerType":"User"},"email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:36:20.154Z","repositoryId":1288793305,"sha":"3a8b63e73e6c25aa71a7c5967f427dee4e0e7581"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T23:36:20.154Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c06fa2bab3738b67f51380c9af2a4a1dc01eb644/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T19:43:07Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T19:43:07Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"fix(scan): strip NUL from EXIF, and report progress when a scan fails\n\nA massive import died after indexing 11,500 photos, on a Postgres\nDataError: UntranslatableCharacter, \" cannot be converted to text\",\nraised by an ImageDescription reading \"SAMSUNG DIGITAL CAMERA\" followed\nby NUL padding.\n\nPostgres stores no NUL in text or jsonb at any position, and one that\nslips through fails the whole 500-row INSERT batch, which fails the scan.\n_coerce_json_value tried to handle this by stripping NUL, but strip only\ntrims the ends: the camera pads the fixed-width ImageDescription with\nNULs and *then* spaces, so the last character was a space and nothing was\nremoved. End-trimming is the wrong tool anyway — a NUL in the middle of a\nvalue is just as fatal and no amount of trimming reaches it. Both string\npaths now remove every NUL wherever it sits; _clean_str had the same\nlatent hole for embedded NULs, and camera_model is a text column that\nrejects them too.\n\nVerified by reverting the fix under the new tests: the Postgres\nround-trip and embedded-NUL cases fail against the old code and pass\nagainst this one. The round-trip is asserted against a live database on\npurpose — the old code produced a perfectly valid Python string, and only\nPostgres objected.\n\nThe second half is why nobody found out. The failed scan''s span reported\nfiles_found=0, files_added=0, errors=0 for a run that had indexed 11,500\nfiles, because add_attributes was only called on the success path. So the\n\"Scan hit file errors\" trigger — watching aperture.errors > 0 — stayed\nsilent through a crashed import. Counts are now written on the failure\npath too, especially there: a crash after 11,500 files and one after none\nare very different problems, and a span reporting zeros for both is\nuseless exactly when it is needed.\n\nThe trigger has been widened in Honeycomb to fire on error.type existing\nOR aperture.errors > 0, so a crashed scan pages as loudly as an\nunreadable file.\n\nRe-running the import after the fix: 27,910 files walked, 11,148 added,\n282s, 99 files/s, completed. The 12 remaining errors are six genuinely\ntruncated JPEGs, each present in two directories.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"51e52665965965b6224663fc067c3f4f78f648bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/51e52665965965b6224663fc067c3f4f78f648bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/c06fa2bab3738b67f51380c9af2a4a1dc01eb644","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c06fa2bab3738b67f51380c9af2a4a1dc01eb644","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGMwNmZhMmJhYjM3MzhiNjdmNTEzODBjOWFmMmE0YTFkYzAxZWI2NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12","sha":"c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12"}],"sha":"c06fa2bab3738b67f51380c9af2a4a1dc01eb644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c06fa2bab3738b67f51380c9af2a4a1dc01eb644"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-13T19:20:15Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-13T19:20:15Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"perf(obs): drop CORS preflights, bound the GPS backfill chunk\n\nA week of real use put ~2,700 CORS preflight spans in Honeycomb — about\n9% of everything sent. The frontend is a separate origin, so the browser\nsends an OPTIONS before most mutations; each produced a server span plus\nan ASGI http send child, and none of it can answer a question.\n\nDropping the server span alone was not enough. The SDK still makes a\nrefused span current as a non-recording parent, so its children are\nsampled independently and would have outlived it as rootless fragments.\nThe sampler now inherits a dropped parent''s decision, which settles every\ndescendant at once, and is renamed to SpansWorthKeeping since it no\nlonger only concerns parented client spans. Verified against the running\napp: five preflights now produce zero spans while five real GETs produce\ntheir full traces.\n\nThe GPS backfill measured 13.4s in a single request. The caller already\nloops on a cursor and reports progress, so the resumability a background\njob would add is already there — what was wrong is the bite size. 1,000\ncandidates per request froze the progress bar for 13s, made Stop take\nthat long to be noticed, and risked a client timeout. 200 keeps a chunk\nnear a couple of seconds and costs only round trips. Recommending a\nbackground job was the wrong call: it would have been a table, a\nmigration, job wiring and a UI for a one-off operation that is already\nincremental.\n\nAlso records why a VACUUM FULL was needed. Autovacuum reclaims dead rows\nbut does not shrink the file: 26,117 row updates from marking grew the\nphotos heap to 3,706 bytes/row while the row count fell, and every\nendpoint drifted with it — /api/stats P50 14ms to 80ms across the week.\nDead tuples stayed near zero throughout, so this was the table carrying\nits high-water mark, not autovacuum failing. 0.59s to run, 33 MB to\n13 MB, /api/stats back to 19.8ms.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ce0496a0adbd30fb21d10f3bdeb09ac94540de42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/ce0496a0adbd30fb21d10f3bdeb09ac94540de42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGM5NDRjZDNhNTRlM2Y1Mzk1MTkzYWM1ODJlYjExMTNhYjI3NDdlMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e","sha":"36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e"}],"sha":"c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c944cd3a54e3f5395193ac582eb1113ab2747e12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T01:02:00Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T01:02:00Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"fix(library): selecting every camera now returns every photo\n\nTicking all 13 cameras on a 5,938-photo library returned 5,455. The 483 photos\nwhose EXIF names no camera — texts, screenshots, downloads — could not be\nselected at all, because two things conspired:\n\n- the facet query excluded camera_model IS NULL, so no checkbox was ever\n  offered for them;\n- the filter used camera_model IN (...), and NULL never matches IN, so no value\n  could have included them anyway.\n\n\"Select all\" therefore meant \"all photos that have a camera\", which is not what\nit looks like. The file-type filter has no such gap because ext is never null,\nwhich is why this only ever affected cameras.\n\nAdds a blank-valued facet, rendered as \"No camera\" and sorted last, plus an\nIS NULL branch in the filter. Blank is safe as a wire value because a real\ncamera model never is — _no_camera() folds blanks into the same bucket, so\nnothing can be both a camera name and the sentinel.\n\nDeliberately not inferring where these photos came from. The provenance is\nlargely recoverable (a message-export filename identifies 3,367 photos with no\nfalse positives against the audit log), but source and camera are independent\naxes: 3,013 photos have both a camera and a texted filename, and 129 camera-less\nphotos are not texted. Labelling this facet \"from a text message\" would be wrong\nin both directions. A source filter is its own feature.\n\nVerified against the live library: facets now sum to 5,938 and selecting every\ncamera returns 5,938. Both halves of the fix are mutation-tested — reverting\neither one fails three tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"147bba175121a46b08567cb730dfdb7d73ca7970","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/147bba175121a46b08567cb730dfdb7d73ca7970"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDM2NDgxZjk0MWM3ZDg0NjRjYzVjMDc5M2Q3OTdiZjBkODg4NDcwNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb","sha":"94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb"}],"sha":"36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/36481f941c7d8464cc5c0793d797bf0d8884705e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T00:35:51Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T00:35:51Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"feat(organize): show where the library lives and warn before splitting it\n\nOrganizing 4,954 photos into one folder while 984 were already organized in\nanother left the same date structure in two places. Nothing in the app compared\nthe chosen destination against where the photos already were, so the split was\nonly discoverable afterwards by browsing the folder tree — and because the new\nyears sat two levels below a root instead of one, they were collapsed out of\nsight and the run looked like it had failed.\n\nAdds GET /api/organize/layout: active photos grouped by the destination they\nwere organized into. A date tree reports its destination rather than each of\nits year/month folders, otherwise one library reads as a hundred locations.\nFolders that are not date buckets report themselves, which is how photos left\nloose by a skip_duplicates run show up.\n\nReuses the generated `directory` column and ix_photos_status_directory, so the\naggregate is index-only and the regex runs over distinct directories rather\nthan every row — measured at 1.4 ms over 5,938 photos, and it scales with\nfolder count, not library size.\n\nThe Organize page now lists those locations before a destination is chosen, and\nthe destination card warns when the choice would leave the library in more than\none place, offering to switch. A warning, never a refusal: a second location is\noccasionally deliberate, and this is how the codebase already treats the\nanalogous \"destination inside a source folder\" case. A first run with no saved\npreference now defaults to where the library already lives instead of guessing\nfrom folder names.\n\n/layout is declared before /{run_id} — FastAPI matches in order and would\notherwise parse \"layout\" as a run id and 422. A test pins it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"86c23c2e7ad0b6e44a5ac700d8d8842f5f45c544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/86c23c2e7ad0b6e44a5ac700d8d8842f5f45c544"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDk0YjZkYjg2ODc2NGI1MGMyNmYyNmNkMTNkYmRhZWEwZWZiODJjZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695","sha":"07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695"}],"sha":"94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/94b6db868764b50c26f26cd13dbdaea0efb82cdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:04:25Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T01:04:25Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"style: ruff format the new duplicates tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f132804ad8f35c1235ea7203602eef309aaa6b36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/f132804ad8f35c1235ea7203602eef309aaa6b36"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDA3YTZmMDEyYWZlZjExYTdlYzAyZDg2NzAzNjEzYmFjZjVlYjc2OTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418","sha":"8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418"}],"sha":"07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/07a6f012afef11a7ec02d86703613bacf5eb7695"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:53:01Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:53:01Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"feat(duplicates): a page for groups already reviewed\n\nDeciding on a duplicate group left it on the Duplicates page with a changed\nbadge, so the queue filled up with work already done. With 259 groups and a\n50-per-page fetch, decided groups were also consuming slots ahead of ones\nstill needing a look.\n\n/duplicates now lists only pending groups and empties as it is worked through.\nEverything already dealt with moves to /duplicates/reviewed and\n/duplicates/dismissed, linked from the bottom of the queue with their counts.\n\nTwo pages rather than one, because \"I decided which to keep\" and \"these were\nnever duplicates\" are different answers: the first writes per-photo decisions\nand lands on status=reviewed, the second is a group-level dismissal with no\ndecisions at all. They share one view component and differ only by the status\nthey request, passed as a static route prop.\n\nNo backend change — status, limit and offset already worked; only the store\nnever sent them. Keeping one status per page also keeps offset paging correct,\nwhich merging two statuses client-side would not.\n\nThe Duplicates empty state now distinguishes \"nothing left to review\" from\n\"no duplicates found\"; claiming a library has no duplicates when it has 17\ndecided ones would be a lie.\n\nGuarded by a test that would have caught the bug this design creates: from a\npage listing no pending groups, the old startReview(groupId) — which filtered\nthe loaded list for pending — found nothing and silently did nothing. Reverting\nto it fails \"reopening a reviewed group starts a review of it, from this page\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"555e17df7a099efca4e7fd63cb8bde41252d1546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/555e17df7a099efca4e7fd63cb8bde41252d1546"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDhhY2NkNDVmMTY5MjcyZDYzODBkN2E0ZmZmNTIyYWMwYjQyYTI0MTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b","sha":"745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b"}],"sha":"8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/8accd45f169272d6380d7a4fff522ac0b42a2418"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:47:59Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T00:47:59Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"refactor(duplicates): extract the group card, add Load more\n\nGroundwork for splitting reviewed groups onto their own page. Lists the same\ngroups as before; only paging is new.\n\nThe list fetched 50 groups with no pagination UI, so with 259 groups in the\nlibrary most of them were simply unreachable — you could never see past the\nfirst page. Adds a shared LoadMore footer (\"Showing 50 of 242\") driven by a\nloadMore() that takes its offset from what is already loaded, so a group\nleaving the list cannot shift the window and skip a row.\n\nMutations now fold the group the API already returns back into the list\ninstead of refetching page one. Refetching would throw away every page loaded\nso far, and re-running an offset query against a list that just shrank is the\nclassic way to skip a row. applyUpdatedGroup replaces the group in place, or\ndrops it when it no longer matches the page''s filter — which is what will make\na reviewed group leave the Duplicates queue in the next commit.\n\nstartReview is now a thin wrapper over startReviewOf(groups), so a review can\nbe seeded from an explicit set rather than from whatever happens to be in the\nlist. reopen(id, andReview) uses the group returned by the reopen endpoint.\nWithout this, \"Review again\" from a page that lists no pending groups would\nsilently do nothing.\n\nDuplicateGroupCard takes the card markup and CSS out of DuplicatesView\nunchanged, with the actions as a slot: three pages will show the same card and\noffer different choices on it.\n\nBackend gets tests, no code — status and offset already worked, but\ntest_kind_and_status_filters_paginate never passed status despite its name, and\nthe whole feature now rests on it. Verified by mutation: disabling the status\nfilter fails test_the_group_list_filters_by_status.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae68577f0cd9ddb3cc6586128421a8606a370876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/ae68577f0cd9ddb3cc6586128421a8606a370876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDc0NWY4NzFjNDU4NDVkODkzY2RlMTVhN2Y2YTdlZmY1YjMwYjcyMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642","sha":"e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642"}],"sha":"745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/745f871c45845d893cde15a7f6a7eff5b30b722b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T01:52:23Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T01:52:23Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"docs(obs): record why there is no Collector, and stop the rule that would undo it\n\nAsked whether adding an OpenTelemetry Collector was the best-practice\nnext step. It is not, yet: a collector is for data processing, multiple\nsources, or multiple destinations, and this app has one service, one\ndestination, and redaction that happens at source with tests pinning it.\nMeasured volume is 146 spans per 24h against 20M events per month.\n\nRecorded as a decision rather than left as an absence, with the four\nconditions that would change the answer — a second instrumented app being\nthe strongest — and the note that deferring is cheap because the\ndestination is already an environment variable.\n\nAlso records the trap that would otherwise be found the hard way: a\nhostmetrics receiver inside Docker Desktop on macOS measures the Linux\nVM, not the Mac, so the CPU figures used to diagnose import throughput\nare not reproducible that way.\n\nThe more urgent half is the contradiction found while looking for\nsomewhere to put that. Telemetry recently moved from per-session to\nalways-on in backend/.env, because a flag re-typed on every uvicorn\ninvocation is one that gets forgotten and the failure is silent. README\nwas updated; CLAUDE.md and ARCHITECTURE.md still said the opposite — and\nCLAUDE.md is loaded as project instructions every session, so its rule\nwould have had a future session \"fix\" .env back to 0 and quietly end the\nmonitoring. Both now say the committed default stays 0 while a monitored\nmachine sets it in its own gitignored .env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f1366bf4059040bf54f47969860067ed27983b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/2f1366bf4059040bf54f47969860067ed27983b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGU2NmM1MDMyNjVmZDAyNzA0YTUxNjhjNDdjMDMyMzY4MDkyMjE2NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e","sha":"449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e"}],"sha":"e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e66c503265fd02704a5168c47c03236809221642"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T00:06:13Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T00:06:13Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"docs(obs): say when to put TELEMETRY_ENABLED in .env\n\nThe README told the reader to enable tracing per session so the safe\ndefault survives. That is right for a debugging session and wrong for a\nbackend that is actually being monitored: a flag re-typed on every\nuvicorn invocation eventually is not, and the failure is silent — the app\ngoes dark while looking healthy.\n\nRecords the two things a reader needs to know before relying on it:\nthere is no collector, so an unreachable endpoint drops the last few\nseconds of buffered spans, and traces are the only signal exported —\nlogs stay in LOG_DIR.\n\nThe committed default in .env.example is unchanged; a fresh clone still\nsends nothing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b2921f613539608bed301a27343502ac8b7ca3b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/b2921f613539608bed301a27343502ac8b7ca3b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDQ0OWI5YTQ5ODJiNDQ0OGNlMzgwMjI0MzhiYWE0ZjQ4N2UyYzU4MGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23","sha":"5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23"}],"sha":"449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/449b9a4982b4448ce38022438baa4f487e2c580e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:56:27Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:56:27Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"perf(scan): read files ahead of the decode pool\n\nA worker reads a file and then decodes it, so its core idles while the\ndisk works. A reader thread now pulls files into the page cache ahead of\nthe pool, bounded by a semaphore released once per completed photo —\nwithout the bound a large batch would evict the pages it just loaded.\nNothing crosses the process boundary: the payload is the page cache, not\na pickled buffer, which would cost more than the stall it removes.\n\nThe gain is real but modest, and much smaller than I first claimed.\nThree cold-cache A/B runs against the USB drive came out at 1.08x, 1.11x\nand 1.40x — positive every time, never negative, but not resolvable more\nprecisely: the drive''s own throughput wandered between 20 and 91 MB/s\nacross blocks of a single run, swamping the effect being measured.\n\nI had read the import numbers as reads and decoding being fully\nserialised (19.6 photos/s against 47 reading and 42 decoding, almost\nexactly 1/47 + 1/42) and predicted this would roughly halve import time.\nThat was wrong. A cold baseline run on a matched workload reaches close\nto the decode-only rate on its own, so most of the overlap was already\nhappening. Kept because the direction is consistent across every test\nand the mechanism is sound; SCAN_PREFETCH=0 turns it off.\n\nAlso records what the measurements did establish, which is worth more\nthan this change: SQL is 0.17% of an import and geocoding 17 ms, so the\ncost is process_file itself. Decode plateaus at 3.2x regardless of worker\ncount because an M3''s four efficiency cores contribute little, and the\ndrive delivers the same 115 MB/s to seven readers as to one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fe2e9b3583fffe43821033d3d34af12b20e217cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/fe2e9b3583fffe43821033d3d34af12b20e217cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDU0NTZjNDI2NDA0MjFlNWE4MmRiZGIyMDJlZjQ1NDcxYzMwMWNiMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a","sha":"3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a"}],"sha":"5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/5456c42640421e5a82dbdb202ef45471c301cb23"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:19:15Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T23:19:15Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"chore(obs): tooling to watch a large import\n\nA big import is the only time this app does sustained work, and the three\nplaces it can stall — the worker pool, Postgres, and the scan loop — are\nonly distinguishable while it runs. Afterwards there is nothing left to\nlook at.\n\nwatch_import.sh samples all three on one tick: files/sec from the scan\nrow, CPU and RSS per process, and Postgres commit/insert rates plus wait\nevents. A saturated pool reads as ~100% per worker; one busy process\nwhile the rest idle means the parent serialises the work, which is what\na bottleneck in the geocode or the DB writes would look like.\n\nimport_report.sh diffs the database around the import and, afterwards,\nattributes time to individual statements.\n\nThat attribution needs pg_stat_statements, which must be preloaded at\nserver start and cannot be switched on in a running one — so compose now\nloads it permanently rather than leaving it to be regretted mid-import.\nVerified the restart keeps the volume: 4,491 photos still there, and the\napp reconnected on its own through pool_pre_ping.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"52ad12b1144bfbb7585894e9b7cf14ced4f57a7c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/52ad12b1144bfbb7585894e9b7cf14ced4f57a7c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDNjYzdmNGFhZTZkMzhkZGMyZWE2YzY1YTI4YTc1MTdkMDYzNzM5OWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa","sha":"e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa"}],"sha":"3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/3cc7f4aae6d38ddc2ea6c65a28a7517d0637399a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:03:18Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T01:03:18Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"perf(db): make the folder and stats aggregates index-only\n\nGET /api/stats and GET /api/folders were four sequential scans of a 27 MB\ntable. Two of them derived regexp_replace(path, ''/[^/]*$'', '''') per row to\nfind a photo''s folder — a function call no index can serve, so both read\nevery heap page, exif blob and all.\n\nphotos.directory is now a stored generated column, indexed as\n(status, directory), so the derivation happens once at write time and\nboth queries walk the index without touching the heap. Generated by the\ndatabase, so an organize move updates path and Postgres refiles the\nphoto; it cannot drift, and hand-writing it is rejected.\n\nMeasured on 100k rows over 2,000 folders:\n  folder count  169.7 ms / 16,670 buffers -> 6.5 ms / 93\n  folder tree    88.9 ms / 16,704 buffers -> 9.1 ms / 93\nOn the real 4,491-photo library, end to end:\n  /api/stats     68.9 ms -> 13.9 ms      /api/folders  23.4 ms -> 11.4 ms\n\ncount(DISTINCT x) makes the planner sort every row; grouping in a\nsubquery and counting the groups gets the same answer from the index.\n\nix_photos_sha256 is widened to (status, sha256, size_bytes) rather than\nadded to — every sha256 lookup in the codebase already filters\nstatus=''active'', and carrying size_bytes makes the stats duplicate\npreview index-only too (1,024 -> 59 buffers, 7.47 -> 1.91 ms). photos\ncarries twenty indexes and each is written on every insert during an\nimport, so a swap is worth more than an addition.\n\nAutovacuum''s defaults do not suit an imported library: it triggers on\nupdates and deletes, so inserting tens of thousands of photos leaves the\nvisibility map stale and every \"index-only\" scan silently falls back to\nthe heap. Measured on the real library, a plain VACUUM turned\ncount(*) from a 1,024-buffer sequential scan at 7.07 ms into an 8-buffer\nindex-only scan at 0.41 ms. 0016 lowers the vacuum, insert-vacuum and\nanalyze scale factors on photos and does the one-time catch-up.\n\nexif storage is deliberately left alone. It was the third item on the\nlist — inline at ~1.3 KB, it made every sequential scan a third more\nexpensive — but the scans that suffered are now index-only and never\nread it, list queries already defer it, and a LIMIT-bounded index scan\nmeasures the same 98 buffers with or without it. Moving it out of line\nwould have bought nothing and added a TOAST fetch to the detail view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a8890b3016f73a9a0d751cf7fd0bcc10c3cf28d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/a8890b3016f73a9a0d751cf7fd0bcc10c3cf28d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGUzY2FmOTA3ZDE0MGVjY2M1YTRjMzk4NWI2MmJiNDY0NGNiZTE0ZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a","sha":"c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a"}],"sha":"e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/e3caf907d140eccc5a4c3985b62bb4644cbe14fa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T00:45:51Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T00:45:51Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"test(dedupe): cover the identity-collision guard, add coverage tooling\n\nThe bounded rebuild looks groups up by derived identity as well as by\nmembership, because a group can hold an identity a derivation is about to\nproduce without holding any of that derivation''s photos — a stale group\nwhose key photo left the active set. That guard protects the unique\n(kind, key) invariant and was the one branch of the new code no test\nreached; branch coverage of app/services/duplicates.py goes 96% -> 97%.\n\npytest-cov is added to requirements-dev so this is reproducible rather\nthan a one-off install. Branch coverage specifically: the dedupe passes\nturn on which side of a threshold a scan falls, and a line-covered branch\ncan still be untaken.\n\nAlso corrects the README''s backend test count, stale at 195.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"19d96992b978890f8a0f290479cb5b4b0afdf167","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/19d96992b978890f8a0f290479cb5b4b0afdf167"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGM3YjZmOGM4MDg0YTgwODMxODY3NTRlNWQ4NWYxMGUxYjdhNjkyOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339","sha":"9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339"}],"sha":"c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c7b6f8c8084a8083186754e5d85f10e1b7a6928a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T00:22:42Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T00:22:42Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"perf(dedupe): bound the post-scan rebuild to what the scan changed\n\nDeriving duplicate groups costs O(n^2/64) distance checks over the whole\nlibrary, and execute_scan ran it whenever a scan changed anything. So\nimporting 200 photos into a 100k library re-derived every group from\nevery photo: 29.7s of a scan that had nothing else left to do.\n\nrebuild_groups_for derives the same groups over a closed subgraph around\nthe touched photos, and the scan falls back to the full pass once it has\ntouched more than a quarter of the library. Measured, uniformly random\nhashes, importing into 100k: 200 photos 29.7s -> 0.25s, 1,000 photos\n30.3s -> 0.59s, 5,000 photos 32.6s -> 2.01s. Cost now tracks the import\nrather than the library.\n\nWiring the existing add_photos_to_groups in would have been the small\nchange, but it re-forms exact groups only — every imported photo would\nhave silently dropped out of \"visually similar\" until the next full\nrebuild. Deriving over a subgraph instead reuses the proven grouping code\nand keeps both kinds.\n\nCorrectness rests on the subgraph being closed, so it holds whole\ncomponents rather than just the new photos and their neighbours, and its\nscope is seeded from the neighbours: a new photo is in no group yet, so\nthe group it is about to join is reachable only through the neighbour it\njoins. Only in-scope groups may be deleted — the full pass deletes any\ngroup absent from its derivation, which here would be most of the library.\n\nThe first implementation selected neighbours by band equality alone and\nbenchmarked *slower* than the full pass. Band matching is a candidate\nfilter with a ~1/32 false-positive rate per pair: the band values of 200\nseeds cover most of each band''s 256 values, so nearly every photo matched\nand the subgraph became the whole library. The Hamming check now happens\nin SQL against the same indexed bands the lightbox uses.\n\ntest_bounded_and_full_rebuilds_agree is the load-bearing test; the rest\nname the specific ways a naive bounding goes wrong.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0867b34fe96ad517f681049312228fa4a5145d05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/0867b34fe96ad517f681049312228fa4a5145d05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDlkMjVmYTk1NzE1OWFkZDJmMjc1ZDNhMDMwMWZiNThmZmJiYzIzMzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd","sha":"c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd"}],"sha":"9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/9d25fa957159add2f275d3a0301fb58ffbbc2339"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T23:38:58Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T23:38:58Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"docs(obs): correct the scan span-volume claim with a measurement\n\nThe previous wording warned that a traced scan \"emits far more spans than\na browsing session\" and told the reader to watch their vendor quota. A\nmeasured no-change rescan of 4,491 photos across 4 roots cost 17 spans:\none coarse job span, 8 SELECT, 6 connect, 2 UPDATE.\n\nThe warning mistook library size for span count. Volume follows batches\nand roots because the scan deliberately takes a single span for the whole\njob and carries per-file totals as aperture.* attributes — the case the\ncode comment already made, and which the instrumentation honours.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b7ae6d325a5dd5b402ae07da41765d22b3d06e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/0b7ae6d325a5dd5b402ae07da41765d22b3d06e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGM5OTgxZDZjYjQwOTIzZTQyYjgwYzkwOGE0YmI5ZmU4N2RjYWIwZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0","sha":"0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0"}],"sha":"c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/c9981d6cb40923e42b80c908a4bb9fe87dcab0dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-06T23:31:14Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-06T23:31:14Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"feat(obs): trace SQL queries under the request that ran them\n\nA slow endpoint was previously one opaque block: only FastAPI was\ninstrumented, so /api/stats at 69ms said nothing about why. Query spans\nnow nest under the request, and the answer turns out to be a 33ms\ncount(distinct(regexp_replace(path))) — a per-row function call that\ncannot use an index and grows with the library.\n\nNaively enabling SQLAlchemy instrumentation would have broken the\n/health, /thumbnail and /preview exclusions rather than respecting them.\nThose requests get no server span, so each of their queries would have\nopened a trace of its own — one photo grid turning \"no spans for\nthumbnails\" into hundreds of rootless SELECTs, more volume than the\nexclusion ever saved. ParentedClientSpans drops parentless client spans,\nso a query is recorded only when it explains a recorded request. Server\nand internal spans are untouched, so a background scan still opens its\nown trace.\n\nQuery spans are safe to send onward because every value in this codebase\ntravels as a bind parameter: db.statement carries the placeholder, not\nthe photo path. That is load-bearing rather than incidental, so the test\npins it with an allowlist of span attributes — a raw f-string in a\nrepository, or an upgrade that starts attaching a connection string,\nfails a test instead of shipping paths to a third party. Verified\nend-to-end against a real export: zero spans contain /Users.\n\nAlso documents the observability story, which existed only in\n.env.example until now, and corrects the README''s \"no secrets exist in\nthis app\" — enabling tracing puts a vendor ingest key in backend/.env.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"18d6a04216635dc2c8dab58a48a51db3292a3414","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/18d6a04216635dc2c8dab58a48a51db3292a3414"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKDBjNDJmMThiMGY2YjExMWNiZTk1YzNhMDlmYWQyNzNiMmRiMWM4YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e","sha":"b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e"}],"sha":"0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/0c42f18b0f6b111cbe95c3a09fad273b2db1c8c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:44:32Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:44:32Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"feat(obs): first trace to Honeycomb, off by default\n\nAdds vendor-neutral OpenTelemetry tracing behind TELEMETRY_ENABLED, exporting\nOTLP over HTTP so the same spans reach Honeycomb or a local backend by changing\none env var. FastAPI is auto-instrumented; SQLAlchemy, job links and batch\nspans come later.\n\nTelemetry never carries filesystem paths, filenames, usernames or machine\nnames. That is enforced, not documented:\n\n- add_attributes refuses any path-like value on a custom span, so no call site\n  has to remember.\n- record_failure records the exception *type* only. span.record_exception would\n  attach a traceback with source paths, and an OSError message carries the\n  filename it failed on.\n- a server_request_hook rewrites the auto-instrumented URL attributes to the\n  path alone. GET /api/photos?folder=/Users/... otherwise puts a real path and\n  its meaning on a span we do not write. The hook runs after the instrumentation\n  sets those attributes, so it is the final word; it covers both the current\n  and legacy semconv spellings, and the legacy http.* set is what this version\n  actually emits.\n- the process and OS resource detectors stay off, so no hostname or command\n  line ships.\n\nVerified live: with a ?folder=/Volumes/... request, every URL attribute on the\nexported span reads \"/api/photos\" and no span mentions the path. Removing the\nredaction fails two tests, one of them end to end through the real\ninstrumentation.\n\nConfig splits deliberately: TELEMETRY_ENABLED/TELEMETRY_CONSOLE_EXPORT are\npydantic settings, while the destination stays in the SDK''s own OTEL_* vars.\nMirroring OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT into Settings would collide with the SDK\nreading it, and the semantics differ — the SDK appends /v1/traces to the env\nform but not to a constructor argument, so mirroring would post to the wrong\nURL. load_dotenv bridges .env into the process environment so one file\nconfigures both.\n\nsetup_telemetry runs in create_app(), not the lifespan hook: instrument_app\nadds middleware and FastAPI forbids that after startup. It is idempotent\nbecause set_tracer_provider silently no-ops on a second call while\ninstrument_app does not — it would double-count every request.\n\nconftest forces TELEMETRY_ENABLED=0 before the first app import, for the same\nreason it forces LOG_DIR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bca02001f1efd8dea31da606e1a81ab9a4cb69cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/bca02001f1efd8dea31da606e1a81ab9a4cb69cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGI3MGM5ZjA2ZGU3ZjRlY2M4OTdmMzE4NGMxOGFmOTVhYWM1MTFlMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb","sha":"cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb"}],"sha":"b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/b70c9f06de7f4ecc897f3184c18af95aac511e0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:20:52Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-05T00:20:52Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"feat(obs): persist application logs to a rotating file\n\nEvery log line lived only in the terminal running uvicorn: closing it, or\nletting --reload restart the process, destroyed the whole record of what the\napp had done. There was no file to open and nothing to grep.\n\nsetup_logging now also writes newline-delimited JSON to LOG_DIR (default\n~/.aperture/logs, 10MB x 5 files), readable with `jq`. LOG_DIR=\"\" keeps the\nold stdout-only behaviour.\n\nAdds a pure-ASGI RequestContextMiddleware that tags each request with an\nX-Request-ID, echoes it back, carries it into every log record for that\nrequest via a ContextVar, and logs method/path/status/duration_ms. Written as\nraw ASGI rather than BaseHTTPMiddleware because thumbnails and previews are\nstreaming file responses, which BaseHTTPMiddleware buffers.\n\nUnhandled errors now get a {\"detail\": ...} 500 like every other error, with\nthe traceback logged from the middleware — Starlette''s error middleware sits\noutside ours, so a handler there would have lost the request id.\n\nconftest sets LOG_DIR=\"\" before the first app import; it must happen there\nbecause app.db.session calls the lru_cached get_settings() at import time, so\nan assignment placed after that import silently has no effect and the suite\nappends to the real log. A test pins it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0eb6ce501408d3a933c8b522b8d56fe964086a0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/0eb6ce501408d3a933c8b522b8d56fe964086a0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGNmODc2MTFiNTA4NjdiNTFjODk1ZTg3ZDg4MjIyYTcxZjUzZWU4ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701","sha":"fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701"}],"sha":"cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/cf87611b50867b51c895e87d88222a71f53ee8eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:00:47Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T01:00:47Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"docs: record the measured accuracy of place names\n\nThe 13.5 km median quoted earlier came from the only photos that had\ncoordinates at the time — all of them in the White Mountains, which is the\nworst case. Across the full 4,500-photo library after the backfill, 84% of\nmatches land within 5 km and only 2 photos exceed 25 km. The spread is terrain,\nnot lookup error.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71b1a61d82584d5cd98322a2631c2ff5625c5150","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/71b1a61d82584d5cd98322a2631c2ff5625c5150"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGZlYzQyZWRhZjIzYmE0M2I4ZTc4ZGIwM2QwYzgyZWI0MjZkNzk3MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3","sha":"bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3"}],"sha":"fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/fec42edaf23ba43b8e78db03d0c82eb426d79701"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits/bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:56:24Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:56:24Z","email":"tseitzinger@gmail.com","name":"tseitzin"},"message":"fix(geo): backfill photos that already have coordinates\n\ngps_backfill_candidates selected only rows with null coordinates, so the photos\nindexed between GPS extraction (0012) and place names (0014) — which have\ncoordinates but no city — could never gain one. Scans skip unchanged files, and\nthe backfill was their only route. On this library that stranded all 385 photos\nthat had coordinates: the Library showed no place for any photo at all.\n\nCandidates are now \"no coordinates yet\" OR \"coordinates but never geocoded\".\nThe second case needs no file read — the coordinates are already known — so it\nis a tree lookup per photo, and works even if the file has since gone.\n\nReverting the query fails the two new tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"048e0248a8002bc92791dd709771315012388767","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/trees/048e0248a8002bc92791dd709771315012388767"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/git/commits/bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30446692?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin","id":30446692,"login":"tseitzin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDQ2Njky","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tseitzin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/bdb9581599184d09a8d03f31b4e17f9ff86e2aa3","node_id":"C_kwDOTNFs2doAKGJkYjk1ODE1OTkxODRkMDlhOGQwM2YzMWI0ZTE3ZjlmZjg2ZTJhYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tseitzin/photoapp/commit/c50daa3dda024f6a2525e6784339dd398906d178","sha":"c50daa3dda024f6a2525e6784339dd398906d178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tseitzin/photoapp/commits