.\nThis issue manifested itself in a failing e2e test after updating the versions of the core tooling and\nframework used in the project. More specifically, this fix restores the name prop for the user menu button,\nwhich was removed in a previous commit. It also adds a ts-ignore comment to the user menu button component to\navoid type errors.","tree":{"sha":"801c8f877758b3565428a143ff70f2b9e7b6c6f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jpomaloh202122/emrs/git/trees/801c8f877758b3565428a143ff70f2b9e7b6c6f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jpomaloh202122/emrs/git/commits/7d909c05e008b0420e7ead48642df11637c0d1bf","verification":{"payload":"tree 801c8f877758b3565428a143ff70f2b9e7b6c6f9\nparent 5c77a80793d4340e6bf03814f27e0e152acfb605\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1749191647 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1749191647 +0300\n\n(fix) Restore name prop for user menu button (#1388)\n\nThis fixes an issue affecting the user onboarding app where the user menu button was not getting triggered correctly.\nThis issue manifested itself in a failing e2e test after updating the versions of the core tooling and\nframework used in the project. More specifically, this fix restores the name prop for the user menu button,\nwhich was removed in a previous commit. It also adds a ts-ignore comment to the user menu button component to\navoid type errors.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJoQovfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaIsQAGqUOI9cUf27Dgj+HR4XnNtF\nD/Gd/Qti6FpJzV7cduQ+cbXz7yszH3NOqS/9ZAouirSx9aa84aIpEtmpB7ivO+yY\nU8qPvitumXJhrv0gKGn4kxN6uUwoEUJ7ccIVzMf+2zQoGC23PIvO4gZfs/I1B4rx\nmb4ZHDH2m+H6h41/L9+YtD3qiK2Is5hqyIZkUPhz7mipSj2GMHAHbqQ7jIsR7m8t\nJvsMtSpDYuIICNRZoMTcecotZFFk6AJQlwpKd03sQX2SYd4Tef0A0UiLlqPyhEeA\n5sbBY+hDeXB+/DeEYrcLpYS0BvB71Km7Ps3kthGH5X3sIIg6775Drdz9VhG85/Cc\nn17TYsOOmzk0GkWTOMogC78rDCCvgucg5WQrqS/oMRdyhx5BEXbNMSlikEW6hGLw\nZTwfkpmhLKYIZnYMBqEoEWXwzU80XaJHiuSMWWJZhgEIYi8xP1pKdsZVBDsZmfs2\nBW2lELOTCTCB0Y6Q5yxITM+1F