users/kdmccormick/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kdmccormick","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kushaledx/openedx/commits/b71d8a79c1c3df417fcd7c7513d033011c843724/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-08T15:02:37Z","email":"kyle@axim.org","name":"Kyle McCormick"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-08T15:02:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat!: Remove Unused Libraries v2 Import API & LTI Tool (#38297)\n\nThis removes two unused content_libraries features. Both were\ndeveloped during the ~2021 pre-alpha Blockstore Libraries days.\nThey were ostensibly ported during the Blockstore->Core\ntransition but they were untested and probably do not work any more.\nWe''re removing them now to avoid bringing them along for any more re-\nfactorings. The features:\n\n* The LTI 1.3 Provider Tool, which exposed library blocks via LTI, developed\n  originally for a HarvardX use case.\n* The Course Import API. This was developed by 2U in attempt to\n  move course content into V2 libraries, but only developers used it.\n  Please note that this is not the same as the Course Import feature which we\n  are building for Verawood--that is built on the modulestore_migrator API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ff4bbc5ff2129c6659ecd656d4bbb735b2a703d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kushaledx/openedx/git/trees/ff4bbc5ff2129c6659ecd656d4bbb735b2a703d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kushaledx/openedx/git/commits/b71d8a79c1c3df417fcd7c7513d033011c843724","verification":{"payload":"tree ff4bbc5ff2129c6659ecd656d4bbb735b2a703d5\nparent e14103c61c6850bce63540a0e28b0f95a368e08e\nauthor Kyle McCormick <kyle@axim.org> 1775660557 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775660557 -0400\n\nfeat!: Remove Unused Libraries v2 Import API & LTI Tool (#38297)\n\nThis removes two unused content_libraries features. Both were\ndeveloped during the ~2021 pre-alpha Blockstore Libraries days.\nThey were ostensibly ported during the Blockstore->Core\ntransition but they were untested and probably do not work any more.\nWe''re removing them now to avoid bringing them along for any more re-\nfactorings. The features:\n\n* The LTI 1.3 Provider Tool, which exposed library blocks via LTI, developed\n  originally for a HarvardX use case.\n* The Course Import API. This was developed by 2U in attempt to\n  move course content into V2 libraries, but only developers used it.\n  Please note that this is not the same as the Course Import feature which we\n  are building for Verawood--that is built on the modulestore_migrator API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp1m4NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAy3UQAD5Nligm7uJ6V7jRoyvFR/8T\nnfPReNM/oj1rmIcFMkrIrwMuPll+LffBj7kohNW7+EEhrOh2qrs/3n/xWcsn7j/S\nvU8os1Z8BR/x/Pu1lm9a8SoSfPkvSofd/SCaT6vRevXTvkbqJKwuHkCC98307FiG\n6Jv9ZPzK3CT+ahqzhwiRYoDN8lAzUUe8RWXz/+1s/AjCEWBhn5LKpKPiakMLUeZF\ndpVhY+Drem7dDRf4JdYdwKqepJa+153zFtKIP8nUbmXNf4wFq6RWlIdDufCp0fvM\ntwmr2TSo9ZAdt9rY7sYb6N/ISe0CXtdqolSxM0mWWFme9cukn/PYchzlwuckWND+\nX/hoPUzVdmDBBWqNhlV4ZO5wY+wRx0AT+e1IZw3RZoiPGc8ljytBvVLioMvmGvry\nrljNfLx0H1fi60tSE0P9ALFnOsKCIlSN5JvY3LHEqnjqXrlSLp9bemXB554KQN3O\nwhwwi46vihrzUc4l10G/x3PwZtS2OZ2QaC1R4f7G57C9GWQ4hVvVOrnQZYBEoLYm\nMemNiVruD7FxRL49RJ9d7Rhwxsf6FCcIy2C/Mr20ovPSHQhoZAShb9d7tzGlPK+K\nv3/LirPPch48fCVRHGDqOie2IVJBFWOeSDXFeb22st8KRVqsnpTJr2FHWJm0oxG+\nrx2CFcmhQZs2u3XXufgg\n=fe14\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-04T11:33:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"htt