 slice S10):\n\n- themes.ts no longer owns any token values: the theme surface maps the\n  provider''s ''dark'' | ''light'' prop onto @workspec/design''s console-dark /\n  console-light and re-exports TokenName / THEMES / themeStyle from there.\n- The provider binds the full WorkSpec palette inline on .ds-root via the\n  package''s themeStyle(), and carries the dual theme signal\n  (data-aesthetic=\"console\" + data-theme, plus the .dark class for\n  Tailwind''s dark: variant) scoped to its subtree.\n- styles.css drops the :where(.ds-root) fallback ramp, both [data-theme]\n  value blocks, and the shared token definitions: the inline binding\n  guarantees a bound theme wherever React renders, so the CSS-side palette\n  was redundant, not load-bearing. Every var(--ds-x) becomes the WorkSpec\n  var(--x) (verified 1:1 against @workspec/design tokens.json).\n- Adopt design-system components where they cover bespoke elements:\n  Button (all action buttons), Chip (chips + flags), Input/Textarea (catalog\n  cells, qty/amount boxes, rationale editors), Switch (catalog committed\n  toggle), Tabs (app view nav + catalog section nav), Card (DecisionCard\n  shell + ADR rail cards), Lbl (eyebrow labels). Bespoke CSS for those\n  roles is deleted.\n- The package now compiles its own Tailwind CSS from src/index.css: theme +\n  utilities layers only (NO preflight — the remote must never reset a host\n  page) plus a .ds-root-scoped preflight stand-in, with @source pointed at\n  the installed @workspec/design components (Tailwind v4 skips node_modules).\n  The lib build chains @tailwindcss/cli; the MF build adds @tailwindcss/vite.\n  The remote stays self-contained: the S6 constraint was never \"no\n  Tailwind\", only \"no dependence on a host''s Tailwind build\".\n- Readability pass per @workspec/design docs/contrast-audit.md: every\n  --ink-ghost usage on readable text/UI (section counts, group rows, n/a\n  cells, fixed tags, ''/mo'' suffixes, zero amounts, delete icon) moves to\n  the spec-correct text ink; eyebrow labels move to muted-foreground via\n  Lbl. Weak-pair usages that are upstream drift (ink-muted/fade, warn-as-UI,\n  on-accent-on-accent light) are kept and documented.\n\nThe committed pnpm-lock.yaml intentionally contains only the\nregistry-resolvable additions (tailwindcss, @tailwindcss/vite,\n@tailwindcss/cli): @workspec/design@0.1.0-alpha.0 is declared in\npackage.json but unpublished until Brett''s one-time first publish, so CI\nstays red at --frozen-lockfile until then (the documented gate); a plain\npnpm install + lockfile commit closes it after publish.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* feat(site): adopt WorkSpec tokens, fonts, and components on the product site\n\n- index.html sets both WorkSpec theme signals (data-aesthetic=\"console\" +\n  data-theme, and the .dark class) from prefers-color-scheme in a no-flash\n  inline script before first paint; main.tsx keeps them in sync when the OS\n  preference changes — always writing both signals together per the\n  dual-signal contract in @workspec/design docs/theming.md.\n- styles.css imports tailwindcss + the @workspec/design preset + fonts.css\n  and deletes the site''s own unprefixed page vars (--page-bg, --panel-bg,\n  --ink, --ink-muted, --line, --accent, --accent-ink, --code-bg,\n  --code-ink) in favour of WorkSpec tokens. Body copy that used the weak\n  --ink-muted moves to --ink-soft (AA-clean on every documented surface per\n  the upstream contrast audit). Chrome rules live in the base cascade layer\n  so component utilities always win (the documented unlayered-a-vs-utility\n  cascade bug).\n- Marketing CTAs and the demo bar adopt the design system''s Button (asChild\n  around the router Link for the CTAs); eyebrows adopt Lbl.\n- The demo keeps mounting DecisionApp from the PUBLISHED\n  @workspec/decision-ui, which still ships its own interim token layer —\n  the embedded studio picks up the migrated look when the packages\n  republish (same publish gate as the lockfile).\n- The hero screenshot (public/workspace.png) is re-captured post-merge\n  against the live deploy, not regenerated here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* refactor(studio): point the standalone shell chrome at WorkSpec tokens\n\nThe shell renders inside .ds-root, where the migrated provider binds the\nWorkSpec palette inline, so the host chrome reads var(--bg-soft),\nvar(--ink), var(--accent), … directly — the --ds-* names it referenced no\nlonger exist anywhere. Also corrects the mf-host smoke.css comment that\ndescribed the remote as self-styling with --ds-* variables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* docs(host-contract): document the WorkSpec design-token theming contract\n\nRewrite the decision-ui README''s Theming section for S10: the contract is\n@workspec/design''s tokens; the provider binds the palette inline via\nthemeStyle() and carries the dual theme signal\n(data-aesthetic/data-theme + .dark, per the design repo''s docs/theming.md);\nhosts override individual tokens on .ds-root with !important (the inline\nbinding outranks plain stylesheet rules); and the deleted CSS fallback ramp\nis explained — the inline binding guarantees a bound theme wherever React\nrenders, so a CSS-side copy of the palette was redundant, not load-bearing.\nDocuments the no-preflight compiled stylesheet and the fonts story\n(hosts supply web fonts; token stacks degrade to system fonts).\nAligns the tech spec''s two token-layer mentions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* docs(spec): describe the post-migration MF styling contract accurately\n\nThe CSS fallback ramp was deleted in the @workspec/design migration and\nthe remote now bundles its own preset-compiled CSS, so ''variables with\nfallbacks'' and ''no Tailwind crosses the boundary'' both described the\nold contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* chore(deps): resolve @workspec/design@0.1.0-alpha.0 from the registry\n\nThe package is now published, closing the documented frozen-lockfile\ngate on this branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b24bd7f7b3fde1ad301dde706dda03f533d32a86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/trees/b24bd7f7b3fde1ad301dde706dda03f533d32a86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/commits/53fedd09577941d2b8462d271e0e21eaf8c7f75a","verification":{"payload":"tree b24bd7f7b3fde1ad301dde706dda03f533d32a86\nparent 79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1783414021 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783414021 +1200\n\nMigrate to @workspec/design tokens and components (#9)\n\n* feat(ui): migrate decision-ui onto @workspec/design tokens and components\n\nDelete the interim --ds-* token layer (Closes-scope: workspec-decision-studio#8, slice S10):\n\n- themes.ts no longer owns any token values: the theme surface maps the\n  provider''s ''dark'' | ''light'' prop onto @workspec/design''s console-dark /\n  console-light and re-exports TokenName / THEMES / themeStyle from there.\n- The provider binds the full WorkSpec palette inline on .ds-root via the\n  package''s themeStyle(), and carries the dual theme signal\n  (data-aesthetic=\"console\" + data-theme, plus the .dark class for\n  Tailwind''s dark: variant) scoped to its subtree.\n- styles.css drops the :where(.ds-root) fallback ramp, both [data-theme]\n  value blocks, and the shared token definitions: the inline binding\n  guarantees a bound theme wherever React renders, so the CSS-side palette\n  was redundant, not load-bearing. Every var(--ds-x) becomes the WorkSpec\n  var(--x) (verified 1:1 against @workspec/design tokens.json).\n- Adopt design-system components where they cover bespoke elements:\n  Button (all action buttons), Chip (chips + flags), Input/Textarea (catalog\n  cells, qty/amount boxes, rationale editors), Switch (catalog committed\n  toggle), Tabs (app view nav + catalog section nav), Card (DecisionCard\n  shell + ADR rail cards), Lbl (eyebrow labels). Bespoke CSS for those\n  roles is deleted.\n- The package now compiles its own Tailwind CSS from src/index.css: theme +\n  utilities layers only (NO preflight — the remote must never reset a host\n  page) plus a .ds-root-scoped preflight stand-in, with @source pointed at\n  the installed @workspec/design components (Tailwind v4 skips node_modules).\n  The lib build chains @tailwindcss/cli; the MF build adds @tailwindcss/vite.\n  The remote stays self-contained: the S6 constraint was never \"no\n  Tailwind\", only \"no dependence on a host''s Tailwind build\".\n- Readability pass per @workspec/design docs/contrast-audit.md: every\n  --ink-ghost usage on readable text/UI (section counts, group rows, n/a\n  cells, fixed tags, ''/mo'' suffixes, zero amounts, delete icon) moves to\n  the spec-correct text ink; eyebrow labels move to muted-foreground via\n  Lbl. Weak-pair usages that are upstream drift (ink-muted/fade, warn-as-UI,\n  on-accent-on-accent light) are kept and documented.\n\nThe committed pnpm-lock.yaml intentionally contains only the\nregistry-resolvable additions (tailwindcss, @tailwindcss/vite,\n@tailwindcss/cli): @workspec/design@0.1.0-alpha.0 is declared in\npackage.json but unpublished until Brett''s one-time first publish, so CI\nstays red at --frozen-lockfile until then (the documented gate); a plain\npnpm install + lockfile commit closes it after publish.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* feat(site): adopt WorkSpec tokens, fonts, and components on the product site\n\n- index.html sets both WorkSpec theme signals (data-aesthetic=\"console\" +\n  data-theme, and the .dark class) from prefers-color-scheme in a no-flash\n  inline script before first paint; main.tsx keeps them in sync when the OS\n  preference changes — always writing both signals together per the\n  dual-signal contract in @workspec/design docs/theming.md.\n- styles.css imports tailwindcss + the @workspec/design preset + fonts.css\n  and deletes the site''s own unprefixed page vars (--page-bg, --panel-bg,\n  --ink, --ink-muted, --line, --accent, --accent-ink, --code-bg,\n  --code-ink) in favour of WorkSpec tokens. Body copy that used the weak\n  --ink-muted moves to --ink-soft (AA-clean on every documented surface per\n  the upstream contrast audit). Chrome rules live in the base cascade layer\n  so component utilities always win (the documented unlayered-a-vs-utility\n  cascade bug).\n- Marketing CTAs and the demo bar adopt the design system''s Button (asChild\n  around the router Link for the CTAs); eyebrows adopt Lbl.\n- The demo keeps mounting DecisionApp from the PUBLISHED\n  @workspec/decision-ui, which still ships its own interim token layer —\n  the embedded studio picks up the migrated look when the packages\n  republish (same publish gate as the lockfile).\n- The hero screenshot (public/workspace.png) is re-captured post-merge\n  against the live deploy, not regenerated here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* refactor(studio): point the standalone shell chrome at WorkSpec tokens\n\nThe shell renders inside .ds-root, where the migrated provider binds the\nWorkSpec palette inline, so the host chrome reads var(--bg-soft),\nvar(--ink), var(--accent), … directly — the --ds-* names it referenced no\nlonger exist anywhere. Also corrects the mf-host smoke.css comment that\ndescribed the remote as self-styling with --ds-* variables.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* docs(host-contract): document the WorkSpec design-token theming contract\n\nRewrite the decision-ui README''s Theming section for S10: the contract is\n@workspec/design''s tokens; the provider binds the palette inline via\nthemeStyle() and carries the dual theme signal\n(data-aesthetic/data-theme + .dark, per the design repo''s docs/theming.md);\nhosts override individual tokens on .ds-root with !important (the inline\nbinding outranks plain stylesheet rules); and the deleted CSS fallback ramp\nis explained — the inline binding guarantees a bound theme wherever React\nrenders, so a CSS-side copy of the palette was redundant, not load-bearing.\nDocuments the no-preflight compiled stylesheet and the fonts story\n(hosts supply web fonts; token stacks degrade to system fonts).\nAligns the tech spec''s two token-layer mentions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* docs(spec): describe the post-migration MF styling contract accurately\n\nThe CSS fallback ramp was deleted in the @workspec/design migration and\nthe remote now bundles its own preset-compiled CSS, so ''variables with\nfallbacks'' and ''no Tailwind crosses the boundary'' both described the\nold contract.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KqrWxMSePQKrdqcxxcMwfE\n\n* chore(deps): resolve @workspec/design@0.1.0-alpha.0 from the registry\n\nThe package is now published, closing the documented frozen-lockfile\ngate on this branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 