e":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/53fedd09577941d2b8462d271e0e21eaf8c7f75a","node_id":"C_kwDOTNyhHNoAKDUzZmVkZDA5NTc3OTQxZDJiODQ2MmQyNzFlMGUyMWVhZjhjN2Y3NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755","sha":"79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755"}],"sha":"53fedd09577941d2b8462d271e0e21eaf8c7f75a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/53fedd09577941d2b8462d271e0e21eaf8c7f75a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T09:55:25Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T09:55:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(pages): deploy apps/site to decision-studio.workspec.io (#7)\n\n* ci(pages): deploy apps/site to decision-studio.workspec.io\n\nSchema hosting has moved to FieldstateNZ/workspec-schemas, freeing this\nrepo''s single GitHub Pages slot, so pages.yml now builds and deploys the\nproduct site (apps/site) instead of serving the JSON Schemas.\n\n- pages.yml: install → `pnpm --filter @workspec/site build` → upload\n  `apps/site/dist` → deploy-pages. Triggers on pushes to main touching\n  `apps/site/**` (and manual dispatch). A verify step asserts the custom\n  domain + SPA fallback landed. Because the site consumes the PUBLISHED\n  @workspec/* packages, a green deploy also proves the released artifacts\n  still build for consumers.\n- apps/site/public/CNAME → `decision-studio.workspec.io` (Vite copies it\n  to dist/CNAME; DNS for that host → fieldstatenz.github.io is in place).\n- Docs: apps/site README deployment section is now live (not pending);\n  the root README schema-hosting note points at workspec-schemas as the\n  canonical `schema.workspec.io` server.\n\nCloses #5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* ci(pages): redeploy on repo-level build inputs, not just apps/site\n\nWith `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, the deployed site is pinned by the\nlockfile, so a dependency bump (e.g. the site''s @workspec/* moving to a\nnewer published version) must retrigger the Pages deploy. Add\npnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, .npmrc, and the root package.json to\nthe trigger paths so the live site never drifts from main''s build inputs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"65e799c36885be1a648a4ebf859daa5830b9df00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/trees/65e799c36885be1a648a4ebf859daa5830b9df00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/commits/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755","verification":{"payload":"tree 65e799c36885be1a648a4ebf859daa5830b9df00\nparent aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1783331725 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783331725 +1200\n\nci(pages): deploy apps/site to decision-studio.workspec.io (#7)\n\n* ci(pages): deploy apps/site to decision-studio.workspec.io\n\nSchema hosting has moved to FieldstateNZ/workspec-schemas, freeing this\nrepo''s single GitHub Pages slot, so pages.yml now builds and deploys the\nproduct site (apps/site) instead of serving the JSON Schemas.\n\n- pages.yml: install → `pnpm --filter @workspec/site build` → upload\n  `apps/site/dist` → deploy-pages. Triggers on pushes to main touching\n  `apps/site/**` (and manual dispatch). A verify step asserts the custom\n  domain + SPA fallback landed. Because the site consumes the PUBLISHED\n  @workspec/* packages, a green deploy also proves the released artifacts\n  still build for consumers.\n- apps/site/public/CNAME → `decision-studio.workspec.io` (Vite copies it\n  to dist/CNAME; DNS for that host → fieldstatenz.github.io is in place).\n- Docs: apps/site README deployment section is now live (not pending);\n  the root README schema-hosting note points at workspec-schemas as the\n  canonical `schema.workspec.io` server.\n\nCloses #5.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* ci(pages): redeploy on repo-level build inputs, not just apps/site\n\nWith `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, the deployed site is pinned by the\nlockfile, so a dependency bump (e.g. the site''s @workspec/* moving to a\nnewer published version) must retrigger the Pages deploy. Add\npnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, .npmrc, and the root package.json to\nthe trigger paths so the live site never drifts from main''s build inputs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS3uNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsV4QAAi+tQt0RJszT8FtzuNPIqJp\ndcA4IspGOlM15u3GI0gKU/9iKt3NGvBrZvy+WS7Oq7DKivhqBuBYWrBnXkH85CW8\nV8NRUAE6Z+HwiGU/XPPh5c8VAoCwirjJ6fB+bmi3JZW/8WwL+rap+cNJR+/1Uh3w\nJzdCCT9DxVLzHUjV8+mmLvLERLuZDWSeZwWi6dUGwWEUEu1El1IosuwnBr8SnVIR\nNLxvUgzVjMdiJQ2s+zwBDi3UbufCqffTe1aVqAt6tGsVAaO+2BmWUL9t3tmnJJh6\nSrh2SdVeyyUyKmBHMeN9fLIxiwm3zB64lV9NTJRTmebavWeivUS8IRIGM5SHXbtE\nHW0laqCHtV5yFMBmsia0GmJbgagsF2OpQD5PPyAPIZ7NcR92jqGdvghh/BnuHC5d\n2k4k0FNE0fh89f/jsM69oUOO1rAZffX7CTwdxTQYeCnjr5wv5eOMFZZtMiwjWXPG\nBqjdCugfbvFLOLNkLXgkY4pKEtsPhr5irT7rLHYtKY2rlS1R0N3HJPyFXk9XIlk5\n1vdhZZEGHXJzNoCs6Ii7EvZudSW1pNmYMqJXVy7BY6LZ1UzG8RaO9zNOdEz+EEbk\nOtOOrLzp0IOYXnthijv+/fPIlxoKClDsVmJ/ACAB+hMGyYPrl/jlKoJySs+dJeP6\nzdoAc7NHR23PTQB2fZqO\n=cw4b\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-06T09:55:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755","node_id":"C_kwDOTNyhHNoAKDc5YjFmYzUzZGNkNWQxMmRhYmI1NzdkNjhjZGI0NWU5NDVlM2I3NTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503","sha":"aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503"}],"sha":"79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/79b1fc53dcd5d12dabb577d68cdb45e945e3b755"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-06T08:16:15Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-06T08:16:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add product site and in-browser demo for Decision Studio (#6)\n\n* feat(site): product page + in-browser demo (apps/site) — S9\n\nAdds `apps/site`, the marketing page and fully in-browser demo for\nDecision Studio (issue #5):\n\n- Marketing (`/`): hero + positioning, the `npx` quickstart, the\n  $schema / editor-IntelliSense story, a workspace screenshot, and the\n  open-core model. Calm and documentation-adjacent, theme-aware.\n- Demo (`/demo`): mounts the real four-view DecisionApp via\n  DecisionStudioProvider over a MemoryRepository seeded with BOTH worked\n  examples. Lever toggles, cost edits, compare, and the decide flow all\n  run in memory; a persistent banner says so. \"Export ADR\" downloads the\n  deterministic Markdown from the SAME renderer as the CLI''s render-adr\n  (buildAdrModel → renderAdrMarkdown).\n\nThe site is a living integration test of the PUBLISHED artifacts: it\ndepends on the registry versions of @workspec/{decision-ui,engine,schema}\n(concrete versions, not workspace:*). Root `.npmrc` sets\n`link-workspace-packages=false` so pnpm installs them from npm and the\nlockfile records the registry tarballs — if the site builds, the\npackages work for outside consumers. The vendored `src/examples/*` are a\nverbatim copy of the repo examples and validate against the published\nschema''s apiVersion (workspec.io/v1alpha1).\n\nWiring: `apps/*` added to pnpm-workspace and the root Vitest projects (a\n`site` project that resolves @workspec/* from the registry, no source\naliases). A build-time plugin writes dist/404.html for SPA deep links.\n\nDeliberately deferred: the pages.yml switch to serve apps/site at\n`decision-studio.workspec.io` and the removal of schema-serving from this\nrepo''s Pages. Per issue #5 that cutover is blocked until schema hosting\nmoves to FieldstateNZ/workspec-schemas (its #1) frees this repo''s Pages\nslot; claiming the CNAME early would break the schema.workspec.io host\nthat PR #2 just set up. Tracked as follow-up.\n\nGate: typecheck, lint, 158 tests (incl. the demo mounting the published\npackages), and `pnpm -r build` all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* fix(site): address PR review — download revoke, Link scheme handling, a11y, theme\n\nFour fixes from the PR #6 review:\n\n- export-adr: defer `URL.revokeObjectURL` to a later tick — revoking\n  synchronously after `anchor.click()` can cancel an in-flight download\n  in some browsers.\n- router: `Link` now intercepts ONLY in-app absolute paths (\"/\", \"/demo\").\n  External URLs, protocol-relative \"//host\", `mailto:`/`tel:`, and \"#hash\"\n  fall through to the browser instead of being pushed into history.\n- demo: the example switcher was `role=\"tablist\"`/`role=\"tab\"` without the\n  full tabs pattern (roving tabindex, arrow keys, aria-controls). Swapped\n  it for a proper toggle button group (`role=\"group\"` + `aria-pressed`).\n- demo: the embedded studio was hard-pinned to `theme=\"dark\"`. It now\n  follows `prefers-color-scheme` (reacting to changes), matching the rest\n  of the theme-aware page; falls back to dark where matchMedia is absent.\n\nGate: typecheck, lint, site tests (3/3), and site build all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cc0369590ad8df00b0b37913c9c39b3eb39030b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/trees/cc0369590ad8df00b0b37913c9c39b3eb39030b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/commits/aa9cf0eb5538d096f5b361fb14a6b501af0b1503","verification":{"payload":"tree cc0369590ad8df00b0b37913c9c39b3eb39030b8\nparent 0da5ddd147c05716b562015af36ffdb5a91f4ce1\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1783325775 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783325775 +1200\n\nAdd product site and in-browser demo for Decision Studio (#6)\n\n* feat(site): product page + in-browser demo (apps/site) — S9\n\nAdds `apps/site`, the marketing page and fully in-browser demo for\nDecision Studio (issue #5):\n\n- Marketing (`/`): hero + positioning, the `npx` quickstart, the\n  $schema / editor-IntelliSense story, a workspace screenshot, and the\n  open-core model. Calm and documentation-adjacent, theme-aware.\n- Demo (`/demo`): mounts the real four-view DecisionApp via\n  DecisionStudioProvider over a MemoryRepository seeded with BOTH worked\n  examples. Lever toggles, cost edits, compare, and the decide flow all\n  run in memory; a persistent banner says so. \"Export ADR\" downloads the\n  deterministic Markdown from the SAME renderer as the CLI''s render-adr\n  (buildAdrModel → renderAdrMarkdown).\n\nThe site is a living integration test of the PUBLISHED artifacts: it\ndepends on the registry versions of @workspec/{decision-ui,engine,schema}\n(concrete versions, not workspace:*). Root `.npmrc` sets\n`link-workspace-packages=false` so pnpm installs them from npm and the\nlockfile records the registry tarballs — if the site builds, the\npackages work for outside consumers. The vendored `src/examples/*` are a\nverbatim copy of the repo examples and validate against the published\nschema''s apiVersion (workspec.io/v1alpha1).\n\nWiring: `apps/*` added to pnpm-workspace and the root Vitest projects (a\n`site` project that resolves @workspec/* from the registry, no source\naliases). A build-time plugin writes dist/404.html for SPA deep links.\n\nDeliberately deferred: the pages.yml switch to serve apps/site at\n`decision-studio.workspec.io` and the removal of schema-serving from this\nrepo''s Pages. Per issue #5 that cutover is blocked until schema hosting\nmoves to FieldstateNZ/workspec-schemas (its #1) frees this repo''s Pages\nslot; claiming the CNAME early would break the schema.workspec.io host\nthat PR #2 just set up. Tracked as follow-up.\n\nGate: typecheck, lint, 158 tests (incl. the demo mounting the published\npackages), and `pnpm -r build` all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* fix(site): address PR review — download revoke, Link scheme handling, a11y, theme\n\nFour fixes from the PR #6 review:\n\n- export-adr: defer `URL.revokeObjectURL` to a later tick — revoking\n  synchronously after `anchor.click()` can cancel an in-flight download\n  in some browsers.\n- router: `Link` now intercepts ONLY in-app absolute paths (\"/\", \"/demo\").\n  External URLs, protocol-relative \"//host\", `mailto:`/`tel:`, and \"#hash\"\n  fall through to the browser instead of being pushed into history.\n- demo: the example switcher was `role=\"tablist\"`/`role=\"tab\"` without the\n  full tabs pattern (roving tabindex, arrow keys, aria-controls). Swapped\n  it for a proper toggle button group (`role=\"group\"` + `aria-pressed`).\n- demo: the embedded studio was hard-pinned to `theme=\"dark\"`. It now\n  follows `prefers-color-scheme` (reacting to changes), matching the rest\n  of the theme-aware page; falls back to dark where matchMedia is absent.\n\nGate: typecheck, lint, site tests (3/3), and site build all green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqS2RPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHNYQAFOJAb57/CA2YW32KhRt5TMB\nylYQNYFABd4rDka8bXzXGWzTzMnJD6cVTQM5UYqH+g+hB7qZuU1+QaNHetmKwh4Z\nWw7Y1UtXu1ILqYhYdOgl0ZGHgMkN2JI2bmQLdsW/WnYjBUKAK4i+zvIA