"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/9cfe22f51c763665457720818bba9bc3ba8b0e33","node_id":"C_kwDOTNyhHNoAKDljZmUyMmY1MWM3NjM2NjU0NTc3MjA4MThiYmE5YmMzYmE4YjBlMzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commit/be6f4c97d9bbead16cf993f5e5ef852ca7d1ed0c","sha":"be6f4c97d9bbead16cf993f5e5ef852ca7d1ed0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/be6f4c97d9bbead16cf993f5e5ef852ca7d1ed0c"}],"sha":"9cfe22f51c763665457720818bba9bc3ba8b0e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/9cfe22f51c763665457720818bba9bc3ba8b0e33"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/commits/be6f4c97d9bbead16cf993f5e5ef852ca7d1ed0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-05T11:32:01Z","email":"brett@pukekos.co.nz","name":"Brett Smith"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-05T11:32:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci(release): fix workspace:* publishing, pin npm, correct provenance note (#3)\n\n* ci(release): fix workspace:* publish, pin npm, correct provenance note\n\nAddresses the three unresolved review comments on PR #1:\n\n1. workspace:* rewriting (publish-breaking): raw `npm publish` from each package\n   directory ships manifests that literally contain `\"workspace:*\"` (npm has no\n   workspace protocol), which consumers can''t install. Switch to `pnpm pack`\n   (which rewrites workspace:* to the concrete version inside the tarball) →\n   `npm publish <tarball>` (which still performs npm''s OIDC trusted-publishing\n   token exchange and attaches provenance). Verified: the packed engine manifest\n   resolves @workspec/decision-schema to 0.1.0-alpha.0, not workspace:*.\n2. Reproducibility: pin the npm upgrade to `npm@^11.5.1` instead of `@latest`,\n   so a future npm major can''t silently drop Node 20.\n3. Docs: the header/step comments no longer claim the workflow attaches\n   provenance \"automatically\" — provenance comes from each package''s\n   publishConfig.provenance:true, honored from the packed tarball in this OIDC\n   CI context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* ci(release): exact-pin npm and harden the pack/publish glob\n\nAddresses PR #3 review comments:\n- Pin npm to an exact 11.5.1 (was ^11.5.1) for reproducible releases.\n- Enable nullglob and assert at least one tarball exists before publishing, so a\n  no-op pnpm pack fails clearly instead of running npm publish on a literal glob.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bb50d0683ecae83569de2212931b1afeef33ddaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/trees/bb50d0683ecae83569de2212931b1afeef33ddaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/FieldstateNZ/workspec-decision-studio/git/commits/be6f4c97d9bbead16cf993f5e5ef852ca7d1ed0c","verification":{"payload":"tree bb50d0683ecae83569de2212931b1afeef33ddaa\nparent 4a3a0b40b01dc05f5bf86b84a7f2f3478e0bb098\nauthor Brett Smith <brett@pukekos.co.nz> 1783251121 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783251121 +1200\n\nci(release): fix workspace:* publishing, pin npm, correct provenance note (#3)\n\n* ci(release): fix workspace:* publish, pin npm, correct provenance note\n\nAddresses the three unresolved review comments on PR #1:\n\n1. workspace:* rewriting (publish-breaking): raw `npm publish` from each package\n   directory ships manifests that literally contain `\"workspace:*\"` (npm has no\n   workspace protocol), which consumers can''t install. Switch to `pnpm pack`\n   (which rewrites workspace:* to the concrete version inside the tarball) →\n   `npm publish <tarball>` (which still performs npm''s OIDC trusted-publishing\n   token exchange and attaches provenance). Verified: the packed engine manifest\n   resolves @workspec/decision-schema to 0.1.0-alpha.0, not workspace:*.\n2. Reproducibility: pin the npm upgrade to `npm@^11.5.1` instead of `@latest`,\n   so a future npm major can''t silently drop Node 20.\n3. Docs: the header/step comments no longer claim the workflow attaches\n   provenance \"automatically\" — provenance comes from each package''s\n   publishConfig.provenance:true, honored from the packed tarball in this OIDC\n   CI context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n* ci(release): exact-pin npm and harden the pack/publish glob\n\nAddresses PR #3 review comments:\n- Pin npm to an exact 11.5.1 (was ^11.5.1) for reproducible releases.\n- Enable nullglob and assert at least one tarball exists before publishing, so a\n  no-op pnpm pack fails clearly instead of running npm publish on a literal glob.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018fNZdxNZR2pf6qpWWXEohy\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude 