/github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/89d7fd8f7242e1006581d4601b1f6d67bc05f3bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:50:56Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T19:50:56Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"message":"docs: warn about the Metro cache faking a missing env var\n\nA web export can ship a bundle where process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_* was folded to\nundefined by a cached transform, so the app boots with \"Missing\nEXPO_PUBLIC_...\" while .env is filled in correctly. The fix is\n`expo export -p web --clear`. Found while recording a demo of the paid\nedition; the same trap applies here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1f4e78a6ea82da1b0ddc45642e8966fe146919a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/trees/1f4e78a6ea82da1b0ddc45642e8966fe146919a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/commits/89d7fd8f7242e1006581d4601b1f6d67bc05f3bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/89d7fd8f7242e1006581d4601b1f6d67bc05f3bf","node_id":"C_kwDOTN4GENoAKDg5ZDdmZDhmNzI0MmUxMDA2NTgxZDQ2MDFiMWY2ZDY3YmMwNWYzYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea","sha":"763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea"}],"sha":"89d7fd8f7242e1006581d4601b1f6d67bc05f3bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/89d7fd8f7242e1006581d4601b1f6d67bc05f3bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:51:39Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:51:39Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"message":"docs: one contact address, and a security policy that names it\n\nSECURITY.md told reporters to \"email the address in package.json\", and\npackage.json had no author field — so anyone finding a vulnerability had\nnowhere to write. It now states the address directly, and package.json\ncarries author (plus bugs, on the free edition) so the pointer resolves\neither way.\n\nAlso unifies the contact on guido.burak@gmail.com; the paid edition''s\nsupport policy listed a different one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c6ba9bdf87b06d9a2e14fe837f3a8a9afa82950a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/trees/c6ba9bdf87b06d9a2e14fe837f3a8a9afa82950a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/commits/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea","node_id":"C_kwDOTN4GENoAKDc2M2M3YTAyYjM1ZDYxZjQ4NDU1OTNkNTYwNjBiMDM1NjRkNDE2ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d","sha":"8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d"}],"sha":"763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/763c7a02b35d61f4845593d56060b03564d416ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:00:56Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T19:00:56Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"message":"docs: add the pre-ship checklist the free edition never had\n\nVerified the quick start end to end on a virgin Supabase project for the\nfirst time: fresh project, migration 001, signup through the real auth API.\nEverything behaved as documented — the trigger created the profile from user\nmetadata, select=* was denied, explicit columns worked, anon was denied, and\nemail was not writable.\n\nTwo things were missing from the README:\n\n- No security section at all, even though 001 ships column-level grants. Now\n  there''s a Before you ship checklist covering the grants, the two-user\n  requirement for the smoke test, and the write-side trap where\n  `.update({...}).select()` fails with a hint that would have you undo the\n  hardening.\n- The features heading still said \"(lite)\", left over from the old framing.\n\nAlso notes that signing up with you@example.com bounces: Supabase rejects\nreserved domains, and the error reads like the signup is broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"73b8443d45c6c30b603aa3892ebf281eaf6d651e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/trees/73b8443d45c6c30b603aa3892ebf281eaf6d651e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/commits/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d","node_id":"C_kwDOTN4GENoAKDhjODk2Y2Q1NTQ0ZDI0OTZjNTBlYjVkMjg0ODQ4YzQ0ZTk1YWU1MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a","sha":"8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a"}],"sha":"8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8c896cd5544d2496c50eb5d284848c44e95ae50d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:52:52Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:52:52Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"message":"fix: the RLS smoke test could never report a failure, and overpromised\n\nThree things, all found by running the test against a real database with a\nnegative control instead of only reading it.\n\n- `fails := fails || ''message''` doesn''t append to a text[]: Postgres tries to\n  read the string as an array literal and raises \"malformed array literal\".\n  Every failure branch did that, so a real violation produced a type error\n  instead of naming what leaked. The green path never ran those lines. Now\n  array_append.\n- With a single account in the project, \"this user sees no other profiles\"\n  is true because there are no other profiles. The test now counts profiles\n  before dropping privileges and reports INCONCLUSIVE below two, rather than\n  a pass it didn''t earn.\n- SECURITY.md claimed the test simulates two users, which is the paid\n  edition''s version. It now describes this one.\n\nREADME no longer introduces the project as the \"lite version\" of something\nelse. It''s MIT and complete on its own; the Pro version is a separate\nparagraph, not the frame.\n\nVerified against a real project: PASS with real fixtures, readable FAIL when\nan assertion is deliberately broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d54615b59d299da20cc2234a1842696177e556d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/trees/2d54615b59d299da20cc2234a1842696177e556d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/commits/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a","node_id":"C_kwDOTN4GENoAKDhkNGU1NzdhZjA3NTNkYWJmNzg1YmZhZDAxM2Y0NzE2ZTUzZGYyM2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/331b3936d72896a2488da4f2365b51037898699e","sha":"331b3936d72896a2488da4f2365b51037898699e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/331b3936d72896a2488da4f2365b51037898699e"}],"sha":"8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/8d4e577af0753dabf785bfad013f4716e53df23a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commits/331b3936d72896a2488da4f2365b51037898699e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:57:27Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:57:27Z","email":"guido.burak@gmail.com","name":"Guido Dev"},"message":"fix: reproducible lint and a documented audit position\n\nSame audit follow-up as the paid edition, minus the parts that don''t exist\nhere.\n\n`npm run lint` wasn''t reproducible: `expo lint` autogenerates an ESLint\nconfig on first run, rewriting package.json and the lockfile mid-command,\nand still failed. eslint and eslint-config-expo are now explicit\ndevDependencies with a committed flat config, the jest.mock hoisting pattern\nis allowed in tests, and the three deliberate dependency arrays carry a\none-line reason instead of a warning. Clean run, no errors, no warnings.\n\nSECURITY.md documents why `npm audit` stays red: the two remaining\nadvisories are denial-of-service issues in metro and the Expo config\nplugins, both build-time only and unreachable from the shipped bundle. The\nonly fix npm offers downgrades Expo two majors, and forcing newer versions\nthrough overrides breaks the web build. The two that could be cleared\nsafely are pinned.\n\nVerified: install, jest 9/9, typecheck, eslint, web export.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5a67424f196a58bcf07726aa80d3298fa42a2d57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/trees/5a67424f196a58bcf07726aa80d3298fa42a2d57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/git/commits/331b3936d72896a2488da4f2365b51037898699e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131815957?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor","id":131815957,"login":"Guidondor","node_id":"U_kgDOB9taFQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Guidondor","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Guidondor/expo-supabase-starter/commit/331b39