/api.github.com/users/bendaj11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/commits/a792e29d6e369dad4d071c38d182ba46e319bb15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:23:40Z","email":"bendaj11@gmail.com","name":"jbd"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T08:23:40Z","email":"bendaj11@gmail.com","name":"jbd"},"message":"fix(runtime,bootstrap): show the unified loader through every loading phase\n\n- Start placement mounts in the loading state so route and slot apps show\n  the shared spinner while styles, the remote entry and the framework\n  bootstrap load, and after a retry.\n- Keep the widget loader until the widget has mounted, render widget status\n  into its own outlet so clearing it never removes widget content, and\n  support widget show/hide/waitUntilReady with a readiness timeout.\n- Hide app and widget content while the loader is shown.\n- Keep the bootstrap placeholder until the host renders, show host status in\n  the host container while no status anchor is rendered, and clear it once a\n  host anchor renders or after the next render.\n- Use a compact loader for slot placements.\n- Indent the loader markup in generated atlas.bootstrap.html and use the\n  shared spinner in the demo hosts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"435fc25d626b223ad17edfae271d689b4695136d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/git/trees/435fc25d626b223ad17edfae271d689b4695136d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/git/commits/a792e29d6e369dad4d071c38d182ba46e319bb15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62200832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bendaj11","id":62200832,"login":"bendaj11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMjAwODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bendaj11/atlas/commit/a792e29d6e369dad4d071c38d182ba46e319bb15","node_id":"C_kwDOTOV58doAKGE3OTJlMjlkNmUzNjlkYWQ0ZDA3MWMzOGQxODJiYTQ2ZTMxOWJiMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bendaj11/atlas/commit/fd50c493dc25ba6b62c1920727bc1c14469866c7","sha":"fd50c493dc25ba6b62c1920727bc1c14469866c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/commits/fd50c493dc25ba6b62c1920727bc1c14469866c7"}],"sha":"a792e29d6e369dad4d071c38d182ba46e319bb15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/commits/a792e29d6e369dad4d071c38d182ba46e319bb15"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62200832?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bendaj11","id":62200832,"login":"bendaj11","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMjAwODMy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bendaj11","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/commits/fd50c493dc25ba6b62c1920727bc1c14469866c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:34:22Z","email":"bendaj11@gmail.com","name":"jbd"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T06:34:22Z","email":"bendaj11@gmail.com","name":"jbd"},"message":"perf(cli): cut sequential storage round trips when publishing\n\n- Confirm the publish lease once before uploads instead of before every\n  immutable file; registry writes keep their own lease checks.\n- Verify each file inside its upload worker so payloads are confirmed\n  before the manifest is uploaded, and skip read-back when storage\n  verifies its own writes (verifiesCreatedObjects is now verifiesWrites).\n- S3 create/replace send a CRC32 checksum and confirm the write from the\n  returned checksum, falling back to a read-back when none is returned;\n  the manifest''s HTTP metadata is still checked once per publish.\n- Add optional readWithVersion (S3 GetObject body + ETag, Artifactory\n  content SHA-256) so the registry is read in one request, reuse the\n  release registry state from before uploads, and skip the registry\n  read-back when storage verifies writes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e873afc1f854a3d8a050f3abf5f3ba8378723560","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/git/trees/e873afc1f854a3d8a050f3abf5f3ba8378723560"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bendaj11/atlas/git/commits/fd50c493dc25ba6b62c1920727bc1c14469866c7","verification":{"payload":null,"re