o-html-link-for-pages`. The one `@ts-expect-error` in TopicPills.test,\nwhich the lint rule only accepts with a description, became a typed\ncast of `undefined` instead.\n\nNo behavior change: lint (2 pre-existing React Compiler warnings), tsc,\nthe 138 unit tests and a production build pass.","tree":{"sha":"181c44ad353cb330714f3b69ee383dd29ad8e182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/181c44ad353cb330714f3b69ee383dd29ad8e182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/f70824688b1a3be21b16f805810038829f3fdbdc","verification":{"payload":"tree 181c44ad353cb330714f3b69ee383dd29ad8e182\nparent 811685e266264417b138dfa10e497dab3b83b262\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1791248974 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791248974 -0300\n\nchore: remove code comments from the public repository (#104)\n\nThis repository is public and read as a portfolio, so the code carries no\ncomments: the reasoning they held lives in commit messages and pull\nrequest descriptions instead. 1,328 comments were removed across 109\nfiles (TypeScript, TSX, config, CSS, workflow YAML and the HTML the\nembed demo serves).\n\nWhat stays are the functional directives, without their descriptions:\nthe `eslint-disable-next-line` lines for `@next/next/no-img-element` and\n`no-html-link-for-pages`. The one `@ts-expect-error` in TopicPills.test,\nwhich the lint rule only accepts with a description, became a typed\ncast of `undefined` instead.\n\nNo behavior change: lint (2 pre-existing React Compiler warnings), tsc,\nthe 138 unit tests and a production build pass.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxEpOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAX7kQADQb1xS1KmakWI/cz3g6AnZo\n3++5i81pDfS/Rxw28A9xuKyHBTAEexvimyUdFEvX2N3YfsokcOV9HWYackOYDV7x\nw1/4yLKzjXzXsIrDxPO11o4SIoPNPwkt0WD5bXFeM2qNXQe2+CtFHpsaguJVk1IT\n7oTatUjZBfxxTD+RZyn/C5lwHVk8Q1TlYWxv4wPC1E+qe0rmMeWSV95hy6zjhed9\nQJiiLCpcTgd7xabfjz6IFLWK1rDBM/T