santana/vertex-web/commit/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8","sha":"49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8"}],"sha":"11ba671071ec1de77be907aa3bd3cf69184fecc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/11ba671071ec1de77be907aa3bd3cf69184fecc1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:09:20Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T21:09:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(theme): swap Ink & Cobalt for the Navy & Emerald palette (#100)\n\nReplace the token values in :root and .dark with \"Navy & Emerald\", the\nsite''s original identity tuned: the navy page it always had (#161c2a),\none emerald accent (#3fd59b) instead of the old emerald-to-cyan gradient,\ncards one step lighter than the page and text off pure white. shadcn\nsemantics are unchanged (--primary is the brand accent, --accent the hover\nsurface), so no component changes: the chrome already reads the tokens.\n\nIn the dark set, body text measures 13.2:1 on a card, secondary text\n6.6:1 on a card and 5.9:1 on muted, the accent 8.4:1 on a card, button\ntext 10.1:1 on the accent, and the focus ring 8.4:1 against a card.\n\nCode blocks go back to the highlight.js theme''s own #0d1117. The card\nsurface was there because #0d1117 vanished into the near-black Ink page;\non navy it reads as the recessed well the site always had, while a\ncard-coloured block nearly disappears (1.08:1 from the page against\n1.11:1) and lowers the theme''s comment colour from 6.2:1 to 5.1:1.\n\nThe focus ring stays at full strength: at 50% the emerald ring passes\n3:1 against a card only by 0.1.","tree":{"sha":"deed05a2830248d25d6230dede89e3218e7a3ee3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/deed05a2830248d25d6230dede89e3218e7a3ee3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8","verification":{"payload":"tree deed05a2830248d25d6230dede89e3218e7a3ee3\nparent 9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1790975360 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790975360 -0300\n\nfeat(theme): swap Ink & Cobalt for the Navy & Emerald palette (#100)\n\nReplace the token values in :root and .dark with \"Navy & Emerald\", the\nsite''s original identity tuned: the navy page it always had (#161c2a),\none emerald accent (#3fd59b) instead of the old emerald-to-cyan gradient,\ncards one step lighter than the page and text off pure white. shadcn\nsemantics are unchanged (--primary is the brand accent, --accent the hover\nsurface), so no component changes: the chrome already reads the tokens.\n\nIn the dark set, body text measures 13.2:1 on a card, secondary text\n6.6:1 on a card and 5.9:1 on muted, the accent 8.4:1 on a card, button\ntext 10.1:1 on the accent, and the focus ring 8.4:1 against a card.\n\nCode blocks go back to the highlight.js theme''s own #0d1117. The card\nsurface was there because #0d1117 vanished into the near-black Ink page;\non navy it reads as the recessed well the site always had, while a\ncard-coloured block nearly disappears (1.08:1 from the page against\n1.11:1) and lowers the theme''s comment colour from 6.2:1 to 5.1:1.\n\nThe focus ring stays at full strength: at 50% the emerald ring passes\n3:1 against a card only by 0.1.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwB2ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaMQQACAYTXOdpVZKNFD+F6/Kxrbm\nFFiJ+OZIxkR1vHYRaDxkRVQQtnfLXVXFeWPl0Z883+JLNRuAWB/8NSxIhaNy28cv\nulHUbDiscbXnQr0cH/l1JHCispQehha35QyV8AMyxkhOBVktoIWNYLDKb0lb/OlQ\nEVW29kPlOwZ3zuQGD0TtHYJdOJRmgLqJcuItWTiPQeTviGBty0wLR5KTgPHmPleH\nNS5XSpKoX/HjaCwIE5gg+UOcEsTE4k65/y0PbmSi5saaS3DRDQn3Zy36AcFFIGWA\nfEkbBR21BagYqJDCrfyiavvWaUb/OM/vqYxroXvF9D7uaaahrQQUr7gdyz7KESbY\ns4apeeA6Mua8KuuRM8KT6C8s3NWninCo7iYXwUY40udnAoNSJMTWm0DELfaXJJBf\nolJOYFqVFdC+03V2Z+dw0lcRBSKW7cm/gjTo8AqCrnwe86wLT+YyOoKPbpE52ysc\nn23mga4U83Lw8pueKNA12YZ9AfzWuhkwxWZKE80ILfeGjN3XU8L/DWkv2zCWA//W\nv1qpSYPEgWW7EWTgtoE88aKPNEiPhdbJtKeeZpC7eMqf1sTRF8dZjZFRorSJL1G+\nE4aq/oi1XQsJpAz+iiiOR3ORnZd3GVPTr5KFC3zxt3T7NU3hWVZlx48tr5W4ZnWi\n4lVa+9minroEHiV9m8G2\n=jwEe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T21:09:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDQ5Zjg0OGRjMWYwMDJjNWM0YjFkZGU1MDdlMWU3YTk2YzBiMzRlYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32","sha":"9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32"}],"sha":"49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/49f848dc1f002c5c4b1dde507e1e7a96c0b34ea8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:39:14Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:39:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(theme): apply the Ink & Cobalt palette to the public site (#98)\n\n* feat(theme): Ink & Cobalt tokens\n\nReplace the shadcn neutral defaults in :root and .dark with the approved\n\"Ink & Cobalt\" palette, keeping shadcn semantics: --primary is the brand\naccent, --accent the subtle hover surface.\n\nForce the dark theme on both root layouts that use ThemeProvider (the\npublic site and the admin panel, which renders the public chrome). The\nsite is dark-only today; once its colours come from the tokens, following\nthe OS would serve the unreviewed light set. The light set stays defined\nfor a future toggle. A static `dark` class and `.dark { color-scheme }`\ncover the prerendered HTML before next-themes'' script runs.\n\nMap the typography plugin''s colour variables to the tokens with an\nunlayered rule, and let the code block take the card surface instead of\nthe highlight.js background, which is indistinguishable from the new page\nbackground. Use the full ring for the outline colour: at 50% the cobalt\nring measures 2.9:1, under the 3:1 a focus indicator needs.\n\n/micro-frontends, which has no ThemeProvider, now renders the light set.\n\n* refactor(ui): move layout shell colors to theme tokens\n\nBackground, header bar, footer, the (blog) layout''s base text, the 404\npage and the OAuth callback screen now read the theme tokens instead of\nfixed slate/emerald utilities and the #161c2a page colour.\n\nThe emerald/cyan gradients on the logo and the 404 button become solid\nprimary, and the green glows (behind the page and under the header and\nthe 404 button) are removed: the palette has one accent and no glows.\n\n* refactor(ui): move home page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe hero, the featured card and the post grid now read the theme tokens.\nThe hero''s second line loses its emerald-teal-cyan gradient for solid\nprimary, and the cards keep their translucency (card/50, accent/80 on\nhover) but drop the emerald hover shadow tint.\n\n* refactor(ui): move post page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe post header, table of contents, code block copy button, share button\nand comments now read the theme tokens. The cross-language notice takes\nthe primary tint in place of cyan; the translation-fallback notice stays\namber, the one named exception, since the palette has no warning colour.\n\nThe article drops prose-invert: globals.css now maps the typography\nplugin''s colours to the tokens for any .prose element, so the class no\nlonger does anything. The comment form''s gradient buttons and their\ngreen glow become solid primary.\n\n* refactor(ui): move about page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe section cards and the profile card read the theme tokens. The\ngradient section numbers, the gradient name and the gradient avatar ring\nbecome solid colours, and the avatar''s blurred glow and the cards'' green\nshadows are removed. The prose blocks drop the now-inert prose-invert.\n\nThe profile card''s \"// connect\" label and social handles move from\nslate-500 (3.4:1 on the card) to muted-foreground (7.0:1). The\ntranslation-fallback notice stays amber, as on the post page.\n\n* refactor(ui): move login modal and header control colors to theme tokens\n\nThe login modal, the login button, the signed-in account menu, the mobile\nnav and the language switcher read the theme tokens. The login button''s\ngradient and green glow become solid primary; menus and the modal sit on\npopover, inputs on background with the ring as their focus colour, and\nerror and sign-out text use destructive.\n\nFilled controls rest on secondary and hover to the input tone rather than\nto accent: secondary and accent are 1.03:1 apart in this palette, so\naccent would leave no visible hover.\n\n* refactor(ui): move public feature component colors to theme tokens\n\nTopic pills, the home page''s admin shortcut bar, the per-post admin\nactions and the confirmation dialog they open now read the theme tokens.\n\nThe dialog''s destructive button takes background-coloured text instead\nof white: white on the dark palette''s destructive red measures 2.9:1,\nthe page background on it 6.5:1.\n\nThe feature components rendered only by the admin panel (post, about,\ntopic and profile forms, user and topic rows, OAuth link buttons) are\nleft as they are, along with the admin pages that host them.","tree":{"sha":"8758233b76725f8d363dc5dd74e3608288395fe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/8758233b76725f8d363dc5dd74e3608288395fe8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/9327bf22dc2d02404e30e049e8e6e937755caa32","verification":{"payload":"tree 8758233b76725f8d363dc5dd74e3608288395fe8\nparent 978dda4d3ee9c1b65fac18b829fabd8450a41ef6\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1790973554 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790973554 -0300\n\nfeat(theme): apply the Ink & Cobalt palette to the public site (#98)\n\n* feat(theme): Ink & Cobalt tokens\n\nReplace the shadcn neutral defaults in :root and .dark with the approved\n\"Ink & Cobalt\" palette, keeping shadcn semantics: --primary is the brand\naccent, --accent the subtle hover surface.\n\nForce the dark theme on both root layouts that use ThemeProvider (the\npublic site and the admin panel, which renders the public chrome). The\nsite is dark-only today; once its colours come from the tokens, following\nthe OS would serve the unreviewed light set. The light set stays defined\nfor a future toggle. A static `dark` class and `.dark { color-scheme }`\ncover the prerendered HTML before next-themes'' script runs.\n\nMap the typography plugin''s colour variables to the tokens with an\nunlayered rule, and let the code block take the card surface instead of\nthe highlight.js background, which is indistinguishable from the new page\nbackground. Use the full ring for the outline colour: at 50% the cobalt\nring measures 2.9:1, under the 3:1 a focus indicator needs.\n\n/micro-frontends, which has no ThemeProvider, now renders the light set.\n\n* refactor(ui): move layout shell colors to theme tokens\n\nBackground, header bar, footer, the (blog) layout''s base text, the 404\npage and the OAuth callback screen now read the theme tokens instead of\nfixed slate/emerald utilities and the #161c2a page colour.\n\nThe emerald/cyan gradients on the logo and the 404 button become solid\nprimary, and the green glows (behind the page and under the header and\nthe 404 button) are removed: the palette has one accent and no glows.\n\n* refactor(ui): move home page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe hero, the featured card and the post grid now read the theme tokens.\nThe hero''s second line loses its emerald-teal-cyan gradient for solid\nprimary, and the cards keep their translucency (card/50, accent/80 on\nhover) but drop the emerald hover shadow tint.\n\n* refactor(ui): move post page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe post header, table of contents, code block copy button, share button\nand comments now read the theme tokens. The cross-language notice takes\nthe primary tint in place of cyan; the translation-fallback notice stays\namber, the one named exception, since the palette has no warning colour.\n\nThe article drops prose-invert: globals.css now maps the typography\nplugin''s colours to the tokens for any .prose element, so the class no\nlonger does anything. The comment form''s gradient buttons and their\ngreen glow become solid primary.\n\n* refactor(ui): move about page colors to theme tokens\n\nThe section cards and the profile card read the theme tokens. The\ngradient section numbers, the gradient name and the gradient avatar ring\nbecome solid colours, and the avatar''s blurred glow and the cards'' green\nshadows are removed. The prose blocks drop the now-inert prose-invert.\n\nThe profile card''s \"// connect\" label and social handles move from\nslate-500 (3.4:1 on the card) to muted-foreground (7.0:1). The\ntranslation-fallback notice stays amber, as on the post page.\n\n* refactor(ui): move login modal and header control colors to theme tokens\n\nThe login modal, the login button, the signed-in account menu, the mobile\nnav and the language switcher read the theme tokens. The login button''s\ngradient and green glow become solid primary; menus and the modal sit on\npopover, inputs on background with the ring as their focus colour, and\nerror and sign-out text use destructive.\n\nFilled controls rest on secondary and hover to the input tone rather than\nto accent: secondary and accent are 1.03:1 apart in this palette, so\naccent would leave no visible hover.\n\n* refactor(ui): move public feature component colors to theme tokens\n\nTopic pills, the home page''s admin shortcut bar, the per-post admin\nactions and the confirmation dialog they open now read the theme tokens.\n\nThe dialog''s destructive button takes background-coloured text instead\nof white: white on the dark palette''s destructive red measures 2.9:1,\nthe page background on it 6.5:1.\n\nThe feature components rendered only by the admin panel (post, about,\ntopic and profile forms, user and topic rows, OAuth link buttons) are\nleft as they are, along with the admin pages that host them.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwBZyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFn0QAHjfBrL9MtyteFynfllvWjQI\nPuybvHhqO/ZQzDR4yAjtGu8Uc6dO1+VZPnnwy5G6kZxfId1VmPGHXDziKVakXc59\nWHAlOnSWWVmgTKJhDkpTyHyBZwLZwbvKJ4ISvsZWsv1rxfYA9qaNhcJv5M7AqSaS\nCeOWDn8fYhcLZFESOPF402Z