ers/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/07da0ab7912c493e1509ba9cfdb0d5c3d7e988e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:44:10Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T18:44:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(blog): localized post dates, one-line card meta, whole featured cover (#93)\n\n* fix(posts): write post dates in the page''s own language\n\nThe home cards formatted every date with \"MMMM d, yyyy\", so Portuguese read \"setembro 25, 2026\":\nEnglish word order with Portuguese words. Both the cards and the post page also mapped every\nnon-English locale to pt-BR, so the Spanish pages showed \"02 de outubro de 2026\".\n\nformatPostDate gives each locale its own pattern: \"02 de outubro de 2026\", \"October 02, 2026\",\n\"02 de octubre de 2026\". The post page keeps the output it had for pt and en.\n\n* fix(home): keep a card''s date and reading time on one line\n\nAt four columns (1280px and up) a card''s text is 202px wide, and the date next to the reading\ntime broke both onto two lines: \"setembro 25, / 2026\" and \"6 / min\".\n\nThe grid cards now use a short date (\"25 set 2026\", \"Sep 25, 2026\", \"25 sep 2026\"), each item\nis nowrap, and the row wraps between items instead of inside them if it ever runs out of room.\nThe featured card has the width for the long date and keeps it.\n\n* fix(admin): write the posts list dates in the admin''s language\n\nThe dashboard''s post list mapped every non-English locale to pt-BR, the same bug the public pages\nhad, so a Spanish admin read Portuguese months. It now uses formatPostDate''s short style.\n\n* fix(home): show the featured cover whole on tablets\n\nFrom 640px the featured cover stretched to the text column''s height and object-cover cut its\nsides: only 65% of its width showed at 768px and 88% at 1024px (measured on the live home).\n\nThe cover now keeps its 1200x630 shape at every width. The card is side by side only from lg,\nwhere the two columns are close in height, with the cover centred if the text runs taller, and\nstacked below that, as on phones. Measured after the change at 390, 768, 1024, 1280 and 1440px:\nthe whole cover shows at all five.","tree":{"sha":"8f454d5fdad0e578f4fc8fd929e225b44ae83335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/8f454d5fdad0e578f4fc8fd929e225b44ae83335"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/07da0ab7912c493e1509ba9cfdb0d5c3d7e988e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f454d5fdad0e578f4fc8fd929e225b44ae83335\nparent 2e6c2f0b24dcb989881435a97944cdc9e5f60050\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1790966650 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790966650 -0300\n\nfix(blog): localized post dates, one-line card meta, whole featured cover (#93)\n\n* fix(posts): write post dates in the page''s own language\n\nThe home cards formatted every date with \"MMMM d, yyyy\", so Portuguese read \"setembro 25, 2026\":\nEnglish word order with Portuguese words. Both the cards and the post page also mapped every\nnon-English locale to pt-BR, so the Spanish pages showed \"02 de outubro de 2026\".\n\nformatPostDate gives each locale its own pattern: \"02 de outubro de 2026\", \"October 02, 2026\",\n\"02 de octubre de 2026\". The post page keeps the output it had for pt and en.\n\n* fix(home): keep a card''s date and reading time on one line\n\nAt four columns (1280px and up) a card''s text is 202px wide, and the date next to the reading\ntime broke both onto two lines: \"setembro 25, / 2026\" and \"6 / min\".\n\nThe grid cards now use a short date (\"25 set 2026\", \"Sep 25, 2026\", \"25 sep 2026\"), each item\nis nowrap, and the row wraps between items instead of inside them if it ever runs out of room.\nThe featured card has the width for the long date and keeps it.\n\n* fix(admin): write the posts list dates in the admin''s language\n\nThe dashboard''s post list mapped every non-English locale to pt-BR, the same bug the public pages\nhad, so a Spanish admin read Portuguese months. It now uses formatPostDate''s short style.\n\n* fix(home): show the featured cover whole on tablets\n\nFrom 640px the featured cover stretched to the text column''s height and object-cover cut its\nsides: only 65% of its width showed at 768px and 88% at 1024px (measured on the live home).\n\nThe cover now keeps its 1200x630 shape at every width. The card is side by side only from lg,\nwhere the two columns are close in height, with the cover centred if the text runs taller, and\nstacked below that, as on phones. Measured after the change at 390, 768, 1024, 1280 and 1440px:\nthe whole cover shows at all five.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv/t6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUnoQAHz42R6s19+qpzayzU/kGlDH\nkHof/jM5gg0biQh6t+IFwJ6rWOxe2sgeHinkMgVkboyROuo+X0W4KVhC4iiIXdT+\nPfcy+XAI+7jRQYtOwo1bRbtHYlzTTKzKG/P01j9nvQs6i+/zQaIsSRxltrcQYFy0\nsETXsJGmLBUuVb+2lIJxg3fRFfeqUusL9/qselU02/iSGzhEH/WVUaBzRcyLgz3U\nnmb2OdL3WcV5KTCAB52S3Um91v9gRAkZHN3ZZblJYIuD2cqjaiLrru+CiJ9ivnBA\nClFywM