m/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/153297f615bc4b57ccfc92f836767a1abce8a1aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T12:48:43Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T12:48:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: bump vulnerable transitive dependencies (#90)\n\nThe weekly scheduled audit went red on advisories published against\nversions already pinned in the lockfile, with no change of ours to\ntrigger it — exactly the case the cron exists for.\n\nTwo high findings crossed the `--audit-level=high` gate: browserslist\n<=4.28.6 (unbounded cache growth, prototype write via untrusted\nbrowserslist-stats.json) and fast-uri 3.0.0-3.1.5 (host confusion and\nSSRF via IDN/IPv6/percent-decoding normalization). The moderate qs\nfinding rides along in the same fix.\n\nAll three arrive through build and CLI tooling only — browserslist and\nqs via shadcn''s @babel/core and express, fast-uri via ajv under\nsecretlint and shadcn — so none of them ship in the client bundle. Fixed\nby semver-compatible bumps within the existing ranges: package.json is\nuntouched, only the lockfile moves. `npm audit` now reports zero\nvulnerabilities; lint, unit tests and build are unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"9d99c475a84a6ea655707752cc043524ecaa8b22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/9d99c475a84a6ea655707752cc043524ecaa8b22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/153297f615bc4b57ccfc92f836767a1abce8a1aa","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d99c475a84a6ea655707752cc043524ecaa8b22\nparent f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1788785323 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788785323 -0300\n\nchore: bump vulnerable transitive dependencies (#90)\n\nThe weekly scheduled audit went red on advisories published against\nversions already pinned in the lockfile, with no change of ours to\ntrigger it — exactly the case the cron exists for.\n\nTwo high findings crossed the `--audit-level=high` gate: browserslist\n<=4.28.6 (unbounded cache growth, prototype write via untrusted\nbrowserslist-stats.json) and fast-uri 3.0.0-3.1.5 (host confusion and\nSSRF via IDN/IPv6/percent-decoding normalization). The moderate qs\nfinding rides along in the same fix.\n\nAll three arrive through build and CLI tooling only — browserslist and\nqs via shadcn''s @babel/core and express, fast-uri via ajv under\nsecretlint and shadcn — so none of them ship in the client bundle. Fixed\nby semver-compatible bumps within the existing ranges: package.json is\nuntouched, only the lockfile moves. `npm audit` now reports zero\nvulnerabilities; lint, unit tests and build are unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnrKrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAp2AQAHnMGxR0RxDiv9Qk4hYpjjcy\ncY+prBFfnga5Eq62pyi8lO8oZaR4sc1WfNc+VWM8emRGJ/lt5uD6vlR7ebtPoLso\n5GVN3IDMnSzsWn9/6sx+IWXMo3PtLTlb4N5le7dgjadgVC7qBHLO+5Q7wPLwVcDs\nrfEGFjs3WIPe6VF2gDIGspyAnJ0cgQqEPfAHTNtfAIVm3DkGq1I1eBADBiF8aKLY\ndzGf50qByoUsPSCqiVL+N/90aa708oOsisEIqSgnOqC+/SztDZ7G5sbScCPNivUy\nz/vG3vl8JonaTaJjiI8A/fFrtR9cfuxusYaF5Twvq6gOH1GbvaFn5rgcaRSjdpNp\nj/rQ84y7VXyRCR/dIRuLPxDwGu8FWDf0WCmnslqhKQ0dW67xPaFPLBlZ280gtWUQ\nDSoFmjfu3zSUamTAkq1bMZafvHBpLIWb10j9jD9UKmliOjoLa7T5T0IfE7EFae/n\nI7o98y1R57guwbeDZ/e5cyC68dN/Weo7yKbeTgdNAuNkRaRWv49d3ovJsYg8aBhX\nUmFxF7MUv/0n7LL9DdcMkv2d6Av+KY6L4YdW42+p5UcOfIyyedRiCYYl26kg8UFx\nmb8ywsAKQt+lnr3pxuEYKNgMhh/F3h0T/zqgQJEmog3k00+5PsP5+Qo0PBkIYggu\n3hHOZyoTvI5eDqoqB3rP\n=XvBV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T12:48:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/153297f615bc4b57ccfc92f836767a1abce8a1aa","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDE1MzI5N2Y2MTViYzRiNTdjY2ZjOTJmODM2NzY3YTFhYmNlOGExYWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3","sha":"f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3"}],"sha":"153297f615bc4b57ccfc92f836767a1abce8a1aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/153297f615bc4b57ccfc92f836767a1abce8a1aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T14:03:38Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T14:03:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: paint the signed-in identity from the local hint, not after the fetch (#89)\n\nThe session hint stored a boolean, so a returning signed-in visitor got the\naccount control at first paint but with nothing in it: a generic \"sign out\"\nbutton that became their name and avatar once /api/me answered.\n\nMeasured on the live site, with a real session:\n\n  first-contentful-paint            ~115 ms\n  generic account control appears   ~112-133 ms\n  name and avatar appear            ~900 ms\n\nThat is ~780 ms of the header knowing someone is signed in and not who.\nThe cost is in the round trip itself — a signed-in GET /api/me takes\n~750-860 ms against ~260-350 ms signed out, and the difference is\nvertex-api reading the user row.\n\nThe hint now carries the resolved display name and avatar URL alongside\nthe boolean, so both paint at hydration. Nothing about its security\nposture changes: it is still a forgeable string in localStorage that\ngrants nothing, /api/me still overwrites it on every load, and both\nfields were already rendered on screen for this same visitor.\n\nOld entries keep working. Every browser that visited before this has \"1\"\nstored, which still parses as \"authenticated, identity unknown\" — the\nprevious behaviour for one load, until the next write upgrades it.\n\nThe identity is exposed as its own context field rather than folded into\n`user`. `user` carries id, email and role, and nothing that decides what\na visitor may do should be able to read a store the browser can forge.\nAn authenticated session with no resolved profile still writes the bare\nboolean, so a backend hiccup cannot erase a good identity from a previous\nload.\n\nAdminHeaderActions now takes that resolved identity instead of a profile\nshape, which also removes its own displayName ?? name ?? email fallback —\none caller resolves it, both callers pass it.\n\nNot fixed here, and worth being clear about: a browser with no hint yet —\na first visit, a private window, cleared storage — still shows the login\nbutton for ~780 ms to someone who is signed in. That is the round trip\nitself, and it needs the API side.","tree":{"sha":"6808171cfb43e8df3c0b549ca8783d4a33742087","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/6808171cfb43e8df3c0b549ca8783d4a33742087"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3","verification":{"payload":"tree 6808171cfb43e8df3c0b549ca8783d4a33742087\nparent 625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787321018 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787321018 -0300\n\nperf: paint the signed-in identity from the local hint, not after the fetch (#89)\n\nThe session hint stored a boolean, so a returning signed-in visitor got the\naccount control at first paint but with nothing in it: a generic \"sign out\"\nbutton that became their name and avatar once /api/me answered.\n\nMeasured on the live site, with a real session:\n\n  first-contentful-paint            ~115 ms\n  generic account control appears   ~112-133 ms\n  name and avatar appear            ~900 ms\n\nThat is ~780 ms of the header knowing someone is signed in and not who.\nThe cost is in the round trip itself — a signed-in GET /api/me takes\n~750-860 ms against ~260-350 ms signed out, and the difference is\nvertex-api reading the user row.\n\nThe hint now carries the resolved display name and avatar URL alongside\nthe boolean, so both paint at hydration. Nothing about its security\nposture changes: it is still a forgeable string in localStorage that\ngrants nothing, /api/me still overwrites it on every load, and both\nfields were already rendered on screen for this same visitor.\n\nOld entries keep working. Every browser that visited before this has \"1\"\nstored, which still parses as \"authenticated, identity unknown\" — the\nprevious behaviour for one load, until the next write upgrades it.\n\nThe identity is exposed as its own context field rather than folded into\n`user`. `user` carries id, email and role, and nothing that decides what\na visitor may do should be able to read a store the browser can forge.\nAn authenticated session with no resolved profile still writes the bare\nboolean, so a backend hiccup cannot erase a good identity from a previous\nload.\n\nAdminHeaderActions now takes that resolved identity instead of a profile\nshape, which also removes its own displayName ?? name ?? email fallback —\none caller resolves it, both callers pass it.\n\nNot fixed here, and worth being clear about: a browser with no hint yet —\na first visit, a private window, cleared storage — still shows the login\nbutton for ~780 ms to someone who is signed in. That is the round trip\nitself, and it needs the API side.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiFq6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATEsQAHPHb8CPCrT4fTEDmzNq+QoF\nTcQ80D8U3fbvaWTjxZPI+VLASRJ/Fg9jhVkGqJnSQsBpdrmnKCvey2b2hdygfLaW\ntHWiybvTVrzlLxNT3RHDDijW4T/2wJRhQ/pR+B+2+HcHNPeH9L5n9nkHuPU0d0Xf\nVusNAeT+TJAF324CnWzyHRGq8tKeDEXNac2Pq2Fc0Sd/XOavu6jvalhQNE2j6Jfs\nk8Kp40LDPG/eOVAc3K6va4aoAkmRj9AQMuBB9WNEybOHmIqrWhL97RHodSB8PQLC\n8vx1+LfCgQeBOeS7853rpNbyX42jD47d5i1Fkjj9TqxsmFaHEbb2G+LrvfHwxaqp\nqV/SNPkIR8DUFpgVqN4E7JVoSxGFGmhXgmlZ1ooxpCRMzHVVm1v+fIWVHmdvpS3k\nENIUkIb5QxxC+hyNzES4ahJHcOesCPrXRF8bOffaNgU8W4Xh0hZdwmAaAnNH29dL\nGUtw+wtleI+tnPrgetJLT4KmkTRd9PkzF3sLy/Hqg8idDWjdnHBdr7t8jws5dEHx\nGj6gSntaIlV0pVWDMvKel+z6QwdB+VfOF6V93HgQDMLETmdd/AMJoJxdKcMPHAUj\n5zrKLIkTYN3lhC6JWSg7HXzNCEllp1oVdKTt+RbHL4p0p17yh3klvgCW/kaUtvby\nPPvLqcpheWPpqsFeO+XT\n=dLJZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T14:03:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGY1MDc2ODc4NTdhZWFmMzk3YzdkNzgzMDk5NDdlYTNjZTlkZDBlZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda","sha":"625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda"}],"sha":"f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f507687857aeaf397c7d78309947ea3ce9dd0ef3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:15:36Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:15:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: move the admin panel out of the [locale] segment (#88)\n\nThe panel lived at src/app/[locale]/(blog-admin)/, so every one of its\nroutes went through next-intl''s URL scheme. With localePrefix \"as-needed\"\nthat made /dashboard, /en/dashboard and /es/dashboard three spellings of\none route, and the auth gate in proxy.ts had to undo that scheme before it\ncould ask its own question — ~20 lines of prefix stripping so that a\nsingle startsWith could run against the result.\n\nA crawlable URL per language is what the public site needs and what the\npanel never did: it is gated, noindex, and read by one signed-in person.\nEverything now sits under /admin, the gate is a prefix check, and\nrobots.ts lists one path instead of generating six from the locale config.\n\nThe panel stays translated in all three languages. That is the part the\nmove had to not break, and it is why the change is bigger than a rename:\nall ten of its route files translate, along with six feature components it\nrenders and the header and footer it shares with the public site.\n\nLanguage now comes from next-intl''s own NEXT_LOCALE cookie — the same one\nthe public middleware writes, so arriving in the panel keeps whatever\nlanguage you were already reading in. i18n/admin-locale.ts resolves it and\npublishes it with setRequestLocale, and every admin layout and page calls\nthat helper rather than only the root layout: layouts and pages render\nconcurrently, so a page can ask for the locale before its layout has\ncached one. Under [locale] that race showed up as routes dropping out of\nthe prerender; here it would show up as a page rendering in Portuguese\ninside a layout rendering in English.\n\nLanguageSwitcher splits along the same line. Switching language is a\nnavigation on the public site and a stored preference in the panel, so the\nshared markup moved to LanguageSwitcherView and the two behaviours became\ntwo small containers, rather than one component growing a mode flag\nthrough code that is entirely about routing.\n\nLinks into the panel from public components (HomeAdminPanel,\nPostAdminActions, CommentsSection, BlogMobileNav, AdminHeaderActions,\nUserRow) switch to plain next/link, since these paths take no locale\nprefix and the localized Link would invent one. Redirects *out* of the\npanel keep the localized redirect: they land on the public site, which\ndoes put the locale in the path.\n\nVerified against a production build: the public route table is unchanged\n(everything still prerendered), the panel answers under /admin with\n<html lang> and its header following the cookie across pt/en/es, an\nunknown cookie value falls back to pt, and the pre-move URLs — including\na locale-prefixed spelling of the new one — all 404 rather than aliasing.\n\nNot verified: the panel''s own pages against a live vertex-api, which was\nnot reachable in this environment. Route resolution, locale plumbing and\ngating were exercised; the dashboards'' contents were not.\n\nThe URLs change, so admin bookmarks break. That is the cost, and for a\npanel with one user it is the whole of it.","tree":{"sha":"3207347a77f7936d20815f420d9e6a6c89f5dc5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/3207347a77f7936d20815f420d9e6a6c89f5dc5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda","verification":{"payload":"tree 3207347a77f7936d20815f420d9e6a6c89f5dc5e\nparent c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787318136 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787318136 -0300\n\nrefactor: move the admin panel out of the [locale] segment (#88)\n\nThe panel lived at src/app/[locale]/(blog-admin)/, so every one of its\nroutes went through next-intl''s URL scheme. With localePrefix \"as-needed\"\nthat made /dashboard, /en/dashboard and /es/dashboard three spellings of\none route, and the auth gate in proxy.ts had to undo that scheme before it\ncould ask its own question — ~20 lines of prefix stripping so that a\nsingle startsWith could run against the result.\n\nA crawlable URL per language is what the public site needs and what the\npanel never did: it is gated, noindex, and read by one signed-in person.\nEverything now sits under /admin, the gate is a prefix check, and\nrobots.ts lists one path instead of generating six from the locale config.\n\nThe panel stays translated in all three languages. That is the part the\nmove had to not break, and it is why the change is bigger than a rename:\nall ten of its route files translate, along with six feature components it\nrenders and the header and footer it shares with the public site.\n\nLanguage now comes from next-intl''s own NEXT_LOCALE cookie — the same one\nthe public middleware writes, so arriving in the panel keeps whatever\nlanguage you were already reading in. i18n/admin-locale.ts resolves it and\npublishes it with setRequestLocale, and every admin layout and page calls\nthat helper rather than only the root layout: layouts and pages render\nconcurrently, so a page can ask for the locale before its layout has\ncached one. Under [locale] that race showed up as routes dropping out of\nthe prerender; here it would show up as a page rendering in Portuguese\ninside a layout rendering in English.\n\nLanguageSwitcher splits along the same line. Switching language is a\nnavigation on the public site and a stored preference in the panel, so the\nshared markup moved to LanguageSwitcherView and the two behaviours became\ntwo small containers, rather than one component growing a mode flag\nthrough code that is entirely about routing.\n\nLinks into the panel from public components (HomeAdminPanel,\nPostAdminActions, CommentsSection, BlogMobileNav, AdminHeaderActions,\nUserRow) switch to plain next/link, since these paths take no locale\nprefix and the localized Link would invent one. Redirects *out* of the\npanel keep the localized redirect: they land on the public site, which\ndoes put the locale in the path.\n\nVerified against a production build: the public route table is unchanged\n(everything still prerendered), the panel answers under /admin with\n<html lang> and its header following the cookie across pt/en/es, an\nunknown cookie value falls back to pt, and the pre-move URLs — including\na locale-prefixed spelling of the new one — all 404 rather than aliasing.\n\nNot verified: the panel''s own pages against a live vertex-api, which was\nnot reachable in this environment. Route resolution, locale plumbing and\ngating were exercised; the dashboards'' contents were not.\n\nThe URLs change, so admin bookmarks break. That is the cost, and for a\npanel with one user it is the whole of it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiE94CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkIgQAJubE8NpiQ/Ws4dpZ4JdOiMS\n3LDqbBoZnKO1A03jwsOtyZ+PoRzGJZiINjKzfXPaRwv3tDO0VgB5mMLbfsBec/Dh\nTG4KaBU3NlO8TY0XCL+GGQYY063Y0nH4OYomnBdcy3iqcJ3a3HfcdWtztL7E4i71\neFCk81XUR2JiAgWDetPsl4EEylA0U0k1mTvURlhjmCDdjtMSElooPwRGkGnQyAwo\nK6jk/93SrmQ02TITkFO9JpplwGudEpnDCM02in2GJWnfm2m2cfDJ+htlDUJEYTew\nYfCuPc2BsZiyBM4Y3MYEZmZ4f0pF3Gz16M+HIiSSOEFgda0S97xeaFZpRB4GoSlW\nsuBytAS9HY6+CAcjmShtqkFmAMUWj59VSIaE0rlAJXQfUJJm7ZVg+ZGK5fn0wf0H\nDTJe8nZk/x5fTrSUEkeObnGcVWAjVoqD4PKScPk3y2PCGxLTP/sGZfbUt1Gcnniv\nfFbNQI4gZatjLHkOh9V5CoepamXO9pgt65oQkOtBswAf9zXL0tSvQpJtW8Dlmmiv\n+ex89Vdr/JnjS1pWjMSl2qWrVN66aFtfD+dyu6eixh91MP7+xWzV8X7CYCiA6aNF\n/fESh3ZLdKAhqi2wA8ukDI78yRIYfgkKWHJ0fLS6UY/MsdOlPt6qceYINa05L2Kv\nsq7TS7PHBrFTyGBY8Ka2\n=9wf1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T13:15:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDYyNWEyMWE4YWRkYjUyNThkZDcwMTViZDIyZmRmMTJhYzkzNWVkZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55","sha":"c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55"}],"sha":"625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/625a21a8addb5258dd7015bd22fdf12ac935edda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:15:32Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T13:15:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: stop federation specs failing on the remote API''s cold start (#87)\n\nThe @external job went red on PR #86, which changed nothing on\n/micro-frontends. The widget mounted — its title was visible — but the\nrows never arrived, because they come from the remote''s own fetch to the\nCygnus API, which runs on a free tier that sleeps when idle and can take\nmost of a minute to wake.\n\nTwo deadlines were wrong for that.\n\nThe row assertion was the only one in the file still on the 5s default,\nso the slowest path in the suite carried the tightest deadline while the\ntitle above it — which renders before any data — was given 30s.\n\nRaising it alone would not have been enough. Playwright''s default budget\nis 30s per test and it caps every assertion inside one, so the\n\"passes props in and callbacks back out\" spec timed out despite asking\nfor 30s of its own. The describe block now gets 90s.\n\nThis does not hide an outage. A remote that is genuinely down still fails\nthe job — it just takes longer to say so, which is the right trade for a\nsignal whose only value is being trustworthy.","tree":{"sha":"578c894fb293dfabd08e1c8f3d1a9a426d7f9553","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/578c894fb293dfabd08e1c8f3d1a9a426d7f9553"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55","verification":{"payload":"tree 578c894fb293dfabd08e1c8f3d1a9a426d7f9553\nparent 923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787318132 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787318132 -0300\n\ntest: stop federation specs failing on the remote API''s cold start (#87)\n\nThe @external job went red on PR #86, which changed nothing on\n/micro-frontends. The widget mounted — its title was visible — but the\nrows never arrived, because they come from the remote''s own fetch to the\nCygnus API, which runs on a free tier that sleeps when idle and can take\nmost of a minute to wake.\n\nTwo deadlines were wrong for that.\n\nThe row assertion was the only one in the file still on the 5s default,\nso the slowest path in the suite carried the tightest deadline while the\ntitle above it — which renders before any data — was given 30s.\n\nRaising it alone would not have been enough. Playwright''s default budget\nis 30s per test and it caps every assertion inside one, so the\n\"passes props in and callbacks back out\" spec timed out despite asking\nfor 30s of its own. The describe block now gets 90s.\n\nThis does not hide an outage. A remote that is genuinely down still fails\nthe job — it just takes longer to say so, which is the right trade for a\nsignal whose only value is being trustworthy.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiE90CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAocQADWDKkFCVvwva9lItd+bkm41\nvFwuvA0SDDqfu8VnNMTGJHsQQhvgEW6sOKDwSul3MUxe2+0vi/TLwWstkH6c9az0\nrOw96o7HE4I8zwhfug63vTajgEE4I1O6tld6XApMV+ottQ+Ttqz685DVdk7KFK8s\nOf02emS95DrX9W+c9cfyptvVlNSykwyfDzj9DXCbkVQ4B/UoW2Ldczo8291KnST0\nworKhlRMq/sHQT9bksFxqsUoqjxPEGhQUfmVf6cczI6yPo0J1gNMbbpj2kJjyfGc\npVqAguXjQ0XTLQVQrIfvs5mVaiz4+4BRHKv+ObvPliDUeHmtEdz2ly4QVYVEKMLW\nHC83Kmhe4cWkX44zsKxk0aYyuKf7zTGJD8yD74n8D/7kK9a1o8Xnhhobw//Fl1Gn\nh8nMbz+XSJSJxs4uXKjJeUIk8sU14SnBZextfgf5c5NpdIcDnGgPDG0cxLnJ1vfO\nP5x7DVquLtxMCtwYnnhGLocKR9Mjr6VPSI8FW9sl3YbfybnANUDxER6z9gBC3j21\nOQ1qHQPcxoo8H4k0hAB3GeR3zni+fTRATqty351NMz0NH5/jnHFOViaXWEpoY2Fe\n5TyYl7mOKJkXQS8e1fzX/fPYAiWmhusPyVqfVoSHgY66dBU4tWmns+SnzjXgbFiI\n7WiDQ+vtgEiHdtFxp1t5\n=ptRZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T13:15:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGM3ZDM5MmRlMjM2MmJhZDI5YjhlNzY1ZTM3ODgwZGM1ODIyZGRkNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4","sha":"923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4"}],"sha":"c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c7d392de2362bad29b8e765e37880dc5822ddd55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:30:32Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:30:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: prerender blog posts by resolving comment auth on the client (#86)\n\nThe post page called cookies() + getProfile() to hand CommentsSection the\nsigned-in visitor, because access_token is HttpOnly and a client component\ncannot read it. That one call kept every post out of the prerender: each\nanonymous visitor paid a vertex-api round trip so the composer could be\naddressed to someone who, for all but one visitor, isn''t there.\n\nPR #83 already built the way out — GET /api/me plus CurrentUserProvider,\nwhich wraps (blog)/layout.tsx and therefore already wraps this page.\nCommentsSection was the last place that hadn''t adopted it. It now reads\nuseCurrentUser() and takes no currentUser prop.\n\nThe three-state trap that came with the move, and how each caller handles\nit:\n\n- The composer is gated on isAuthenticated (the cookie''s answer,\n  optimistically pre-filled from the local session hint), so a returning\n  signed-in visitor is not shown the sign-in card while /api/me is in\n  flight. That flash is exactly the bug the hint store was built to fix in\n  the header.\n- Nothing renders in that slot until isResolved. This markup is\n  prerendered and identical for everyone, so committing to either branch\n  server-side would show one group the wrong one.\n- The delete button and the admin link read `user` instead, since they\n  are controls only some visitors get: appearing a beat late once the\n  profile lands is correct, rendering one the API would reject is not.\n- A successful create refetches the list when `user` is null. The cookie\n  authenticates the Server Action, but without an author the optimistic\n  row cannot be rendered, and dropping it would look like the submit\n  failed.\n\ngenerateStaticParams now lists every published post per locale. Without\nit the route had no dynamic API left but still no param list to build\nfrom, so it stayed f in the route table and the first visitor to each URL\npaid for the render. dynamicParams keeps its default of true, so a post\npublished after the build renders on demand and is cached from then on.\ngetPosts() returns [] on an unreachable vertex-api, so a backend outage\nduring a build degrades to that same on-demand behaviour instead of\nfailing the deploy.\n\nMeasured with next build: /[locale]/blog/[slug] goes from f to SSG. That\nthe cookies() removal was the last dynamic dependency was confirmed\nseparately by building with `dynamic = \"error\"`, which fails on any\ndynamic API — it passed.\n\nNew unit tests cover the server render (neither branch present), the\nreturning-visitor case before /api/me answers, both resolved answers, and\na stale hint being corrected.","tree":{"sha":"5e3a35ef3db2258b1d5e0b8e9e2d2e1fafc8d448","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/5e3a35ef3db2258b1d5e0b8e9e2d2e1fafc8d448"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4","verification":{"payload":"tree 5e3a35ef3db2258b1d5e0b8e9e2d2e1fafc8d448\nparent 5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787315432 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787315432 -0300\n\nperf: prerender blog posts by resolving comment auth on the client (#86)\n\nThe post page called cookies() + getProfile() to hand CommentsSection the\nsigned-in visitor, because access_token is HttpOnly and a client component\ncannot read it. That one call kept every post out of the prerender: each\nanonymous visitor paid a vertex-api round trip so the composer could be\naddressed to someone who, for all but one visitor, isn''t there.\n\nPR #83 already built the way out — GET /api/me plus CurrentUserProvider,\nwhich wraps (blog)/layout.tsx and therefore already wraps this page.\nCommentsSection was the last place that hadn''t adopted it. It now reads\nuseCurrentUser() and takes no currentUser prop.\n\nThe three-state trap that came with the move, and how each caller handles\nit:\n\n- The composer is gated on isAuthenticated (the cookie''s answer,\n  optimistically pre-filled from the local session hint), so a returning\n  signed-in visitor is not shown the sign-in card while /api/me is in\n  flight. That flash is exactly the bug the hint store was built to fix in\n  the header.\n- Nothing renders in that slot until isResolved. This markup is\n  prerendered and identical for everyone, so committing to either branch\n  server-side would show one group the wrong one.\n- The delete button and the admin link read `user` instead, since they\n  are controls only some visitors get: appearing a beat late once the\n  profile lands is correct, rendering one the API would reject is not.\n- A successful create refetches the list when `user` is null. The cookie\n  authenticates the Server Action, but without an author the optimistic\n  row cannot be rendered, and dropping it would look like the submit\n  failed.\n\ngenerateStaticParams now lists every published post per locale. Without\nit the route had no dynamic API left but still no param list to build\nfrom, so it stayed f in the route table and the first visitor to each URL\npaid for the render. dynamicParams keeps its default of true, so a post\npublished after the build renders on demand and is cached from then on.\ngetPosts() returns [] on an unreachable vertex-api, so a backend outage\nduring a build degrades to that same on-demand behaviour instead of\nfailing the deploy.\n\nMeasured with next build: /[locale]/blog/[slug] goes from f to SSG. That\nthe cookies() removal was the last dynamic dependency was confirmed\nseparately by building with `dynamic = \"error\"`, which fails on any\ndynamic API — it passed.\n\nNew unit tests cover the server render (neither branch present), the\nreturning-visitor case before /api/me answers, both resolved answers, and\na stale hint being corrected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiEToCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlOgQAAwQcg1sbqK75jrnDSuTCcAw\niNdyqFTVYFBgoUPC8hpyeG4eoUTKnt+XRljeb2EPZjiCTOZSfxBnl8vZ8HUUdT3o\nXGhyuG6GYNcrgML3wMto/4GxB2uhhsM6dJuOebEmGzS54ktSyrWT9y+bBpGuEMEj\naHLiej4VlJkC3pdasBL/e7znmTn8xcvgQ98DrFvB4bvHTNAXffo9yF3S0qw9EiFV\n4ICWFRKk3peSBMUtdT8sJzd8/cBTW/s1Jzb9lildNjqAqPRV8UGCEOjIoPtPM6tj\niLAQrQpduz3yiBTOki+lzseWJIaQJppXoeA0KAg4YKr42WThCSZou/vVUbuZVeo5\n50w1+tutkcoXrlnAZefsLMlTucUMnwP6m0GiqFSslXf/eavEkVA1oDAxXb9z5/JN\n5PpKjJDe9i3ka16Rkw2Qpn12wCQ6hMWgdcz63+d8/rUmGO7kWaSksH6GuJEJ+1UB\ngbfKgSQcxdZCM6BOdq32DnWtOIdhGoVC+vHtpqwNa5pB4cpZstC4hUI1CDDncQYY\nhZZ6G1FLH23ItluU/9VC97YZzRzkdP/bfwY+WpGpgiIveMDbm/YvF9IUE6Wf+trm\nxErjA6E1V8Q8LJmEYqQLL1RBU36EWTN00rSvW3pvg82oJaj1RHsSyRBCMCVXiDdO\nYc5HEwKegDd3zw1XqPjA\n=TKeZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T12:30:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDkyM2ViNjhlNTM3ZTI0OGRkY2ZkZWZmODM3Y2Q3ZGFjOGZhMzdmZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64","sha":"5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64"}],"sha":"923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/923eb68e537e248ddcfdeff837cd7dac8fa37ff4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T11:57:34Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T11:57:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: resolve the site origin at build time so public pages prerender (#85)\n\n* perf: resolve the site origin at build time so public pages prerender\n\ngetSiteUrl() read the request''s Host header, which is a dynamic API. Any\npage that needed an absolute URL was therefore server-rendered per request\npurely to learn its own domain — including /about, which has no\nper-request data at all, and robots.txt and sitemap.xml, whose output is\nidentical for every visitor.\n\nThe Host header was introduced to fix a real bug: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL\npointed at the apex domain, the apex 308-redirects to www, and LinkedIn''s\ncrawler (confirmed live against its own user agent) dropped\nog:description while validating an og:url that redirected elsewhere. But\nthe defect was a configured value disagreeing with the domain, not the\nexistence of the value. A constant next to the code cannot drift the way\na dashboard setting can, and it costs no dynamic render.\n\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL survives as a local-development override only, and\nis ignored in production builds. Its previous fallback to\nhttp://localhost:3000 meant a deploy landing before the variable did\nwould publish canonical and og:url pointing at localhost — silently, and\nworse than the bug it replaced. Ignoring it in production removes that\nordering risk instead of documenting it.\n\nPreview deployments now report the production origin rather than their\nown *.vercel.app host. That is deliberate: a preview that self-references\ninvites search engines to index it as a second copy of the site.\n\nRoute changes, measured with next build:\n\n  /[locale]/about   f dynamic -> SSG + ISR 1m (x3 locales)\n  /robots.txt       f dynamic -> static\n  /sitemap.xml      f dynamic -> static + ISR 1m\n\n/[locale]/blog/[slug] stays dynamic: it also calls cookies() to resolve\nthe comment author, which is a separate change.\n\nThe root layout no longer keeps its own copy of the origin for\nmetadataBase, and sitemap.ts stops threading the resolved value through\nthree helpers now that it is a module constant.\n\n* docs: correct why previews report the production origin\n\nThe reason given was that a self-referencing preview canonical invites\nsearch engines to index the preview as a second copy of the site. That\nargument had already been checked against a real preview in this repo and\ndoes not hold: Vercel puts previews behind SSO and serves them with\nX-Robots-Tag: noindex, so no crawler reads a preview''s canonical either\nway. Re-verified against this branch''s own preview.\n\nThe decision is unchanged — what it actually buys is one value with one\ndefinition, instead of a variable that has to be correct in every\nenvironment and fails silently in the one that lacks it.","tree":{"sha":"c98fb92f8907c0089ace1a0da8985403210609ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/c98fb92f8907c0089ace1a0da8985403210609ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64","verification":{"payload":"tree c98fb92f8907c0089ace1a0da8985403210609ea\nparent c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787313454 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787313454 -0300\n\nperf: resolve the site origin at build time so public pages prerender (#85)\n\n* perf: resolve the site origin at build time so public pages prerender\n\ngetSiteUrl() read the request''s Host header, which is a dynamic API. Any\npage that needed an absolute URL was therefore server-rendered per request\npurely to learn its own domain — including /about, which has no\nper-request data at all, and robots.txt and sitemap.xml, whose output is\nidentical for every visitor.\n\nThe Host header was introduced to fix a real bug: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL\npointed at the apex domain, the apex 308-redirects to www, and LinkedIn''s\ncrawler (confirmed live against its own user agent) dropped\nog:description while validating an og:url that redirected elsewhere. But\nthe defect was a configured value disagreeing with the domain, not the\nexistence of the value. A constant next to the code cannot drift the way\na dashboard setting can, and it costs no dynamic render.\n\nNEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL survives as a local-development override only, and\nis ignored in production builds. Its previous fallback to\nhttp://localhost:3000 meant a deploy landing before the variable did\nwould publish canonical and og:url pointing at localhost — silently, and\nworse than the bug it replaced. Ignoring it in production removes that\nordering risk instead of documenting it.\n\nPreview deployments now report the production origin rather than their\nown *.vercel.app host. That is deliberate: a preview that self-references\ninvites search engines to index it as a second copy of the site.\n\nRoute changes, measured with next build:\n\n  /[locale]/about   f dynamic -> SSG + ISR 1m (x3 locales)\n  /robots.txt       f dynamic -> static\n  /sitemap.xml      f dynamic -> static + ISR 1m\n\n/[locale]/blog/[slug] stays dynamic: it also calls cookies() to resolve\nthe comment author, which is a separate change.\n\nThe root layout no longer keeps its own copy of the origin for\nmetadataBase, and sitemap.ts stops threading the resolved value through\nthree helpers now that it is a module constant.\n\n* docs: correct why previews report the production origin\n\nThe reason given was that a self-referencing preview canonical invites\nsearch engines to index the preview as a second copy of the site. That\nargument had already been checked against a real preview in this repo and\ndoes not hold: Vercel puts previews behind SSO and serves them with\nX-Robots-Tag: noindex, so no crawler reads a preview''s canonical either\nway. Re-verified against this branch''s own preview.\n\nThe decision is unchanged — what it actually buys is one value with one\ndefinition, instead of a variable that has to be correct in every\nenvironment and fails silently in the one that lacks it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiD0uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvuwQAFm8j0rxGly4dUldCRcz13UN\nPM5YhSBZZnEArgV3GIH4kwT1U9I1agZWPrD/dM34OS5a1L1SFmn1sDE+21Be0aCn\nu6QbWAG2DNcxB1WCUFotgOEQoGOi0ENsWg2cX/IbuyV4YKaclC1EKUfA2AyF70Ri\ndo/dE80z5ehRtRwBd1MwITe4tjEc6kqevWE9CmhncCwHvjQkHq6wevCdAKLuBD5M\naiZaubCEGLy799CrVwJuYpfN+b04LQ4l6aGFvjsk/r0pLRbe0LeY4FlXxmhj+y3r\nDVcYhSJ12PZjXwqe3yJtEwSbxzSO5e5l2LLtilHfm5OzJdh449UxzmvprOWPluIQ\nctpAMd1uKQ4gP9FWaBx1Z2cswwB1Xr3zizdCioZHXfzSI66LNsWiKVFrHY1FZ2gl\nIkqLQKUcY8+IxOrINkARrLgZfsVF4n+GhCIz+C85EY+LT8s7pXd/r/lRS4z3LgB9\nyO44qUFIYnc05bDDkZgShmQS8VOzdkGigyXL1/SgIy8xbA1XS1K77Ep4Yps4LYjG\nOND+dLs89cyc9z7FsU5iNM2RIb/xx75KnDjT04+yub1afnSyeuNcbVxNg+LpEYRX\nSMQ5WN+L10P5u3IkCw9FbK5329+ixiN+4a17LL1TaATHXHFxg39jBOuqeS24Qa9K\nQsq+D4hMd0KSReZwN+4w\n=cXh5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T11:57:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDUxNzU2ODI4NzhkN2VkYTE0MDkyMzRkNzBlMGYyZDNmODBjYjJjNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135","sha":"c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135"}],"sha":"5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/5175682878d7eda1409234d70e0f2d3f80cb2c64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:26:15Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:26:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(micro-frontends): host a cross-origin Module Federation remote (#84)\n\n* feat(micro-frontends): host a cross-origin Module Federation remote\n\nAdds /micro-frontends, which mounts a React component published by the cygnus\nrepository, served from cygnus.samuelsantana.dev, into this page''s own React\ntree — resolved over the network at runtime, with nothing of it in this\nbundle.\n\nUses the Module Federation runtime API rather than a bundler plugin, because\nthere is no plugin path here: @module-federation/nextjs-mf declares\n`next: ^12 || ^13 || ^14 || ^15` and this app is on Next 16 with Turbopack.\nThe runtime API turns out to be the better fit anyway — the plugin''s job is\nrewriting imports into container lookups at build time, and this host has no\nsuch imports. What it does have to do by hand is publish its own React into\nthe share scope, which is `lib: () => React` in federation.ts.\n\n`type: \"module\"` on each remote is load-bearing and its absence is opaque. The\nVite plugin emits an ESM container; without it the runtime injects the entry\nthrough a plain <script>, the browser rejects it with \"Cannot use import\nstatement outside a module\", and what surfaces is RUNTIME-001 \"failed to get\nremoteEntry exports\" — an error about exports, for a file fetched with a 200\nand never evaluated. A unit test pins it.\n\nprobeSharing() makes the negotiation observable instead of assumed. It\ncompares `useState` and `createElement` by reference, since two copies of the\nsame version are still two objects. Verified end to end: both sides report\n19.3.0-canary — the React build Next vendors for the App Router — while the\nremote is compiled against 19.2.8, so it is announcing a version it does not\nship and could only have been handed. Note what that implies: under strict\nsemver a prerelease does not satisfy `^19.0.0`, and the runtime accepted it.\nHad it refused, the remote would have fallen back to its own React, rendered\nperfectly, and broken later.\n\nThe page is static and the remote is client-only, so the server render carries\nno trace of it — asserted, because markup in the HTML would mean the remote\nwas resolved at build time and this was a bundling demo.\n\nIsolation is deliberate: own root layout, noindex, excluded from locale\nrouting, and touching nothing under (blog) or (blog-admin). It shares a deploy\nwith the blog and should not share anything else.\n\nThe offline toggle points at a .invalid hostname rather than a missing path on\nthe real origin — *.samuelsantana.dev is a wildcard and cygnus rewrites\nunmatched paths to its SPA shell, so a bad path answers 200 with HTML and\ndemonstrates content-type filtering rather than an unreachable remote.\n\ne2e/micro-frontends.spec.ts covers all five claims against a real browser and\na real second origin. Like the rest of e2e/, not wired into CI.\n\n* ci: run the end-to-end suite, split by who can break it\n\nThe suite was kept out of CI on the belief that it needed a live vertex-api\nand a Postgres to back it. Measured instead of assumed: with nothing listening\non :3333, all 18 specs pass. They assert layout, locale routing, the auth\ngate''s redirects and the federation boundary — not one of them reads a post, a\ntopic or a profile. The blocker was a requirement that did not exist, and the\nwork to satisfy it was never needed.\n\nThat bounds the coverage too, and playwright.config.ts now says so rather than\nimplying the suite is broader than it is: nothing here would notice vertex-api\nreturning garbage. Specs that assert on real content are still owed, and those\nwill bring the Postgres requirement with them for real.\n\nTwo jobs, not one. The federation specs reach cygnus.samuelsantana.dev, an\norigin this repository does not deploy, so they are tagged @external and run\nseparately. Folded together, a PR touching the blog would go red when that\norigin blips and nobody could tell which had happened from the red X. Kept\nunmocked deliberately: /micro-frontends genuinely stops working when that\norigin does, and a mocked remote turns the one property worth testing into a\ntautology.\n\nCI runs against a production build rather than the dev server, and not only\nfor speed: /micro-frontends is prerendered, `next dev` renders it per request,\nand the spec asserting the remote is absent from the server HTML would\notherwise be checking a pipeline that never ships. The build is its own step\nso a compile error reads as a build failure instead of a server that never\ncame up.\n\nVerified locally on the CI path — CI=1, production build, npm start, single\nworker: 18 passed.","tree":{"sha":"b0ad412b283bbbe4bf4f48a85952ad26ee45cf66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/b0ad412b283bbbe4bf4f48a85952ad26ee45cf66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135","verification":{"payload":"tree b0ad412b2