s: under strict\nsemver a prerelease does not satisfy `^19.0.0`, and the runtime accepted it.\nHad it refused, the remote would have fallen back to its own React, rendered\nperfectly, and broken later.\n\nThe page is static and the remote is client-only, so the server render carries\nno trace of it — asserted, because markup in the HTML would mean the remote\nwas resolved at build time and this was a bundling demo.\n\nIsolation is deliberate: own root layout, noindex, excluded from locale\nrouting, and touching nothing under (blog) or (blog-admin). It shares a deploy\nwith the blog and should not share anything else.\n\nThe offline toggle points at a .invalid hostname rather than a missing path on\nthe real origin — *.samuelsantana.dev is a wildcard and cygnus rewrites\nunmatched paths to its SPA shell, so a bad path answers 200 with HTML and\ndemonstrates content-type filtering rather than an unreachable remote.\n\ne2e/micro-frontends.spec.ts covers all five claims against a real browser and\na real second origin. Like the rest of e2e/, not wired into CI.\n\n* ci: run the end-to-end suite, split by who can break it\n\nThe suite was kept out of CI on the belief that it needed a live vertex-api\nand a Postgres to back it. Measured instead of assumed: with nothing listening\non :3333, all 18 specs pass. They assert layout, locale routing, the auth\ngate''s redirects and the federation boundary — not one of them reads a post, a\ntopic or a profile. The blocker was a requirement that did not exist, and the\nwork to satisfy it was never needed.\n\nThat bounds the coverage too, and playwright.config.ts now says so rather than\nimplying the suite is broader than it is: nothing here would notice vertex-api\nreturning garbage. Specs that assert on real content are still owed, and those\nwill bring the Postgres requirement with them for real.\n\nTwo jobs, not one. The federation specs reach cygnus.samuelsantana.dev, an\norigin this repository does not deploy, so they are tagged @external and run\nseparately. Folded together, a PR touching the blog would go red when that\norigin blips and nobody could tell which had happened from the red X. Kept\nunmocked deliberately: /micro-frontends genuinely stops working when that\norigin does, and a mocked remote turns the one property worth testing into a\ntautology.\n\nCI runs against a production build rather than the dev server, and not only\nfor speed: /micro-frontends is prerendered, `next dev` renders it per request,\nand the spec asserting the remote is absent from the server HTML would\notherwise be checking a pipeline that never ships. The build is its own step\nso a compile error reads as a build failure instead of a server that never\ncame up.\n\nVerified locally on the CI path — CI=1, production build, npm start, single\nworker: 18 passed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqh38HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGPgQAAgN9ACXcGkKNl+kHFN2hJ1H\nbu1CZ10guy0f6M5PFaTl4uGyNniJX4EUId2gBhW6vIm3gBgLuy6khPYAdSHIoV2P\nd8W3MmQWFej94zh0Lus4jYTSjFymh2fHlAgXYk2JpFMw2U5r8nXdDbRxxtkxmg7g\nBujW7+Ds2DTiDSPjJcoOidpgy/uk8DQ+BaS40rGKcwXnuKd3Qw6VhhboWw7rJJ40\nzsBecb1FIsJo5NLHJJPSy/vZ7vhOmKobkqIZWpYK9cNSM9EQOFCN+ycSz52/Btnb\nqocf7/DwqOVpyxBgv1vws4J/Ct02EOvFY/UvvYADW2Sg+8+ui5NGrM+vilxj0x2n\nJ0frMUiKyOiT4xd4Khb0qXEWlYerZM5Mcy6PoU1PK1H1xSIQHnJJPD+6qHNxxoIE\nEYaheIOIB3jxfl4fdGqJUCjar5R4izx10c1Pn3yTeLySVQvcqF86Qsogit3/ZT3G\nTAIjQ2QIaL6xhs94sodoASz4KRuahl7Yd7Lg6Jl8CaHfDeWNNhKXIBijUK0AhiFA\nCAgGwzBnGdZiqG35QA+8LPF+0MRQGUwNsJk5iVQNACf5RV2Wp+kpdmF05AeycyNl\n57tu0WRcZAxB2AwOmF4aUxq+NiCTrvDmKkDq5i6ife5VBXHzXI8WQKa4U8yDgPkI\nI9HdalDwV5xLz2Cvm0Jn\n=RFqY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T22:26:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGM5NTQxMjUwMjhiOWFkY2M5YzM3ZWIyNTFhOTM0ODkxYTJhOGQxMzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0","sha":"f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0"}],"sha":"c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/c954125028b9adcc9c37eb251a934891a2a8d135"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:19:43Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:19:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(auth): stop the header from guessing signed-out before it knows (#83)\n\nReported from the live site: signed in, every reload showed the logged-out\nheader first and then flipped to the account menu.\n\nThat was the documented cost of moving auth out of the render path — the\nprerendered HTML is identical for every visitor, so the header could not know\nwho was asking and assumed \"signed out\" while /api/me was in flight. Right for\neveryone except the one person who is signed in, who therefore saw it on every\nsingle load.\n\nThe header no longer guesses. Until it has an answer it renders neither state:\nthe slot holds its footprint and asserts nothing. The answer then comes from a\nlocal hint written after each /api/me — before paint and without the network,\nso both kinds of visitor settle at hydration and neither watches the header\nchange its mind.\n\nThe hint is not a credential and grants nothing. It is a boolean in\nlocalStorage, forgeable by any script on this origin, and the only thing it\ndecides is which UI to paint for the ~200ms before the real answer lands.\n/api/me stays the sole source of truth and overwrites it every load.\n\nThree details that are load-bearing rather than incidental:\n\nuseSyncExternalStore instead of an effect that calls setState. It is the one\nhook that reads an external store *and* takes a separate server snapshot, so\nhydration renders exactly what the server sent and then switches. An effect\nwould paint the wrong header once first, which is the flicker being removed.\n\nsubscribeToHydration notifies once via queueMicrotask, and a no-op subscribe is\nnot equivalent. useSyncExternalStore only re-reads on render, so an unnotified\nstore keeps reporting the server value until something else forces one. For a\nsigned-in visitor the hint store covered that up; for everyone else the next\nrender was the /api/me response, putting the login button back behind the round\ntrip this change exists to remove. Measured in a real browser with /api/me\nblocked: anonymous resolves NEUTRAL -> LOGIN, signed-in NEUTRAL -> ACCOUNT, and\nneither waits on a response.\n\nA failed request no longer clears the hint or the session. That branch is a\ndropped request, not an answer: treating it as a logout signs the user out of\nthe UI over one network blip and reintroduces the flash on the next load.\n\nThe hint is also subscribed, not just read, so signing out in one tab corrects\nthe header in the others instead of leaving a menu for a dead session.","tree":{"sha":"defe8df707475f287db0dba49458d7e6044f80ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/defe8df707475f287db0dba49458d7e6044f80ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0","verification":{"payload":"tree defe8df707475f287db0dba49458d7e6044f80ef\nparent 0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787188783 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787188783 -0300\n\nfix(auth): stop the header from guessing signed-out before it knows (#83)\n\nReported from the live site: signed in, every reload showed the logged-out\nheader first and then flipped to the account menu.\n\nThat was the documented cost of moving auth out of the render path — the\nprerendered HTML is identical for every visitor, so the header could not know\nwho was asking and assumed \"signed out\" while /api/me was in flight. Right for\neveryone except the one person who is signed in, who therefore saw it on every\nsingle load.\n\nThe header no longer guesses. Until it has an answer it renders neither state:\nthe slot holds its footprint and asserts nothing. The answer then comes from a\nlocal hint written after each /api/me — before paint and without the network,\nso both kinds of visitor settle at hydration and neither watches the header\nchange its mind.\n\nThe hint is not a credential and grants nothing. It is a boolean in\nlocalStorage, forgeable by any script on this origin, and the only thing it\ndecides is which UI to paint for the ~200ms before the real answer lands.\n/api/me stays the sole source of truth and overwrites it every load.\n\nThree details that are load-bearing rather than incidental:\n\nuseSyncExternalStore instead of an effect that calls setState. It is the one\nhook that reads an external store *and* takes a separate server snapshot, so\nhydration renders exactly what the server sent and then switches. An effect\nwould paint the wrong header once first, which is the flicker being removed.\n\nsubscribeToHydration notifies once via queueMicrotask, and a no-op subscribe is\nnot equivalent. useSyncExternalStore only re-reads on render, so an unnotified\nstore keeps reporting the server value until something else forces one. For a\nsigned-in visitor the hint store covered that up; for everyone else the next\nrender was the /api/me response, putting the login button back behind the round\ntrip this change exists to remove. Measured in a real browser with /api/me\nblocked: anonymous resolves NEUTRAL -> LOGIN, signed-in NEUTRAL -> ACCOUNT, and\nneither waits on a response.\n\nA failed request no longer clears the hint or the session. That branch is a\ndropped request, not an answer: treating it as a logout signs the user out of\nthe UI over one network blip and reintroduces the flash on the next load.\n\nThe hint is also subscribed, not just read, so signing out in one tab corrects\nthe header in the others instead of leaving a menu for a dead session.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhlYvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbxsQACFyylJKPWFpKDNw7zc8yqY7\n1OQVPsrO5DLDwVhS477yEPeqyWltn+yCjezcftvGHkHE3mlehWF1gj3ChjnNJENc\nFQP4zxinJ7H2EgsPRudWM6H/HnGkfQzVF1NFg7Pc0J4g8o++EwUTpN4a7BGBcbE7\nbCWtPGcSqMkqmoLOOQ6DJmvZFUd0qFzE4hrv0uPy/qkA1oyp6HnF8P/cYLshD0l+\nlm7WxoybpGTbnS7BK5EtWgPO78IP05B02ZbXqGACheBCC3DQfhXyTFXjsV4glLzE\nUWhB4m154jpteKJ1gb1N9qhRxA6/7uKOG5kimYnr6wIxpZHZ+HaeZ/6XUhL+13XV\nmCbPeZYlRnLpXnTkd3zINQu70Fi2vJvKKVQdTWynWYZQ9Utlph9mLaaqN015S8r3\nVX/9/FLJm2UBJgnpTs2OqSeDDwaozTOqtdC0Mp/wTNXgwJ5UxHXljROpr5CrK9l7\nGLxl25FQnnrBWwVgxQnA/MdVm6m7D+M655AaW+ElFpD8LEHa7oJeIX74ASxCe4qi\nrqzNDfsYuvRUtAOa8Mgx+0uKosuWg3g4Nz7GNC/UdRRQ83Kmt0tRtsHIjgbAftCS\nfShSpf5NFysYOFeuNI3wC7g6um4q18pmmwZoNyIuIjvbeLUKz7d0sK0FrhEzVJut\ndd93OgLtva0xwPjFLsAC\n=g3ui\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T01:19:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGYwN2QyODE5NTkzMWQwY2YyM2QxNDZjYTNmMDE2MWRlZjlhNDVlYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf","sha":"0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf"}],"sha":"f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f07d28195931d0cf23d146ca3f0161def9a45ea0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:05:02Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:05:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: emit the demo page HTML verbatim with String.raw (#82)\n\nThe page''s own script was dead in production: a SyntaxError killed every\nlistener on it, so the message log stayed empty and the iframe never resized.\n\nThe widgets were fine. Instrumenting the live page showed both variants\nfetching the API successfully and emitting `ready` with a height — one as a DOM\nevent, one over postMessage. Nothing was listening, which is why the page looked\nlike the embed had failed.\n\nThe cause was one layer up, in this file. Embedding the HTML in a template\nliteral means the literal processes escape sequences before the browser ever\nsees them, so the page script''s join(\"\\n\") was emitted as a real newline inside\na single-quoted string. Checking for backticks and ${ when this was written was\nnot enough — backslashes are the third hazard and the easiest to miss, because\nthe source looks correct and only the output is broken.\n\nString.raw emits the document byte for byte, which removes the whole class of\nproblem rather than escaping this one instance of it.","tree":{"sha":"e0f4291c7199f42628f34382994cfbae304768f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/e0f4291c7199f42628f34382994cfbae304768f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf","verification":{"payload":"tree e0f4291c7199f42628f34382994cfbae304768f2\nparent 6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787187902 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787187902 -0300\n\nfix: emit the demo page HTML verbatim with String.raw (#82)\n\nThe page''s own script was dead in production: a SyntaxError killed every\nlistener on it, so the message log stayed empty and the iframe never resized.\n\nThe widgets were fine. Instrumenting the live page showed both variants\nfetching the API successfully and emitting `ready` with a height — one as a DOM\nevent, one over postMessage. Nothing was listening, which is why the page looked\nlike the embed had failed.\n\nThe cause was one layer up, in this file. Embedding the HTML in a template\nliteral means the literal processes escape sequences before the browser ever\nsees them, so the page script''s join(\"\\n\") was emitted as a real newline inside\na single-quoted string. Checking for backticks and ${ when this was written was\nnot enough — backslashes are the third hazard and the easiest to miss, because\nthe source looks correct and only the output is broken.\n\nString.raw emits the document byte for byte, which removes the whole class of\nproblem rather than escaping this one instance of it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhlK+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWe8QAIBlu2lL9r+bKYDuGsFIelH9\nh0zaPpUC2qYxGp0Rl2+m1+lwtgLfhDuTaz/FzQdb4UYJQS514nW+u0kvbX70zPsj\nGXX4IaNm7mIMqhFj0RpDFT5fqSYqR1ed7pY3I6yBgev3AUKcsggZ8hEAuZcAZi2P\n7gnzwmDiicfdRJtGozg5KzSv2Jfa6HcE5lpjkCXGwENIbsvnUkESqScjDPgin0IO\nEkGUYw9a2xX73++AAoo6kWG6xXDcSwcsx17mYbB4/Qt9bajTpbfpWkUZc4uAdugQ\nV+FOn1L/3yqKZRh6rtUBdix0I1YAto/IWmKf69AbzapzKw0Ap9qo2j4QzaYiECtD\n3rsXE2HhGqNlwy9J5rVHZluiyumk6WLp+5RMSKrFsUKKDgs5rXZ7hbx6pr2ryVac\nWhaqXV1A9DueW4agQRoWfulhKPR8bYWdPUQjTAU1JPPe9WWr6l1u5e0Kj3z+6FYG\nR5Y/mW8tP6P/CyNidxGS1gUx2SoS976/FibaqCArjkDbLg0aq6JYnDGFJHOCWU+e\naR0aguUeWsTi13SJ5M3zm2SBb7mQSnxldaT8JX9S3eWsEUAR8rZPLISwNzEoZCcB\n0CEBhUXTwy4zuiwfUF701FX0UgWpNL/zYsqFJVbgUFSietIklhF2E/CxFMGiixhD\np9hxEbsmikaOXqdVkafQ\n=QFkD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T01:05:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDBiMThkZTA4NDFkMjY1MWM4NjRiOWRjOGJkNGFhZmFhOWZjNWE5YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c","sha":"6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c"}],"sha":"0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/0b18de0841d2651c864b9dc8bd4aafaa9fc5a9bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:40:45Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:40:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: serve the embed demo as a route handler, not a file in public/ (#81)\n\npublic/embed-demo.html 404d in production. Worth recording precisely, because\nthe symptom looks like a failed deploy and is not: Next does not serve .html\nfiles out of public/ — it reserves that extension for its own output — while\nevery other file type there is served normally. og-fallback.png sitting in the\nsame directory and returning 200 is what made the cause visible.\n\nA route handler is the better shape regardless. It needs no root layout, and\nthere is none outside [locale]; it needs no translations for a technical page\nwith no localized twin; and it keeps the demo what it has to be in order to\nprove anything at all — plain HTML, with no framework participating in the\nintegration it is demonstrating.\n\nproxy.ts excludes the path from locale routing for the same reason.","tree":{"sha":"2cf0988da2b35422d86f1a30ad9f9fac9e9bbe72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/2cf0988da2b35422d86f1a30ad9f9fac9e9bbe72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c","verification":{"payload":"tree 2cf0988da2b35422d86f1a30ad9f9fac9e9bbe72\nparent 4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787186445 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787186445 -0300\n\nfix: serve the embed demo as a route handler, not a file in public/ (#81)\n\npublic/embed-demo.html 404d in production. Worth recording precisely, because\nthe symptom looks like a failed deploy and is not: Next does not serve .html\nfiles out of public/ — it reserves that extension for its own output — while\nevery other file type there is served normally. og-fallback.png sitting in the\nsame directory and returning 200 is what made the cause visible.\n\nA route handler is the better shape regardless. It needs no root layout, and\nthere is none outside [locale]; it needs no translations for a technical page\nwith no localized twin; and it keeps the demo what it has to be in order to\nprove anything at all — plain HTML, with no framework participating in the\nintegration it is demonstrating.\n\nproxy.ts excludes the path from locale routing for the same reason.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhk0NCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmmwQAHlF1AWjsAcG0wmkzfS70BfD\n+D7EzrKJRIjYnWtIw+95HfYNxqvM0+y9be10ZcKiVY6JUIfdt2IabC5MU0VJRoq8\ndc7oGS4MUkbaZBipEcMXOPGIUjH/Py3AemancMjFW+4iNArxW2jFoewvNvO7akMA\num6rCc+8YH2CGe7ivpmoasx0O7hLeWx5dFrSbLAYrxtYnIxb9o+34RbFg2Q6pOwI\nVBFUDb+6xhw6DZXmiFIXZiYAYeDBysm/qqm2UwqWyU73P5UftRiIGWlvwk5/ZyQs\nJFHZb52pTRKjYEabqMcoXPqKbX2WgEzQlwfl6ftgeD6exyGO8AZPuz/Ubi8uSYvr\nJqNrTuX+0DpKpZOvr+0TTWs+78WDcmLSxqgySluoYWzz9UoRtwKeCxlZid/ukNu9\nWZfD2uBucElH6P+mg/B+cuqQcsnx7iYNelGja3F5r/paVyMgH/HNStu5Bw7xbWT5\n6+vv2PtBxiI+1bUlmVwp4UaNC2tHJlCCyWw1+4ciwzvHkjkzCpDmQGrU2wIji9bM\nVFobAt4jiyf0LbJrLNd+Is3iicFC/0L104dxh23+HaVu9gJWOIk+v57Z9yLi9+oE\nS4JAipcnKYDwDDKceZmkBRqclRYv0+dAUHvjFiVLErGtQ1veKp3mOlEAZ//l7jH3\ng6kHGeBDA9UrTkp3zZvr\n=jht3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T00:40:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDZkY2IwMzYyOTk5YmFkMTc3ZjMxYjAyYTY3MzY5NDYyYmVjNjYyMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121","sha":"4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121"}],"sha":"6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/6dcb0362999bad177f31b02a67369462bec6621c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:28:54Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T00:28:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: host the Cygnus embed on a cross-origin demo page (#80)\n\nThe embeddable widget lives in the cygnus repo and is served from\ncygnus.samuelsantana.dev. A demo page on that same origin would prove nothing —\nthe whole claim is that it works on a site the widget''s project does not\ncontrol, and this domain is exactly that.\n\nPlain HTML in public/, not a route, for three reasons. There is no root layout\noutside [locale], so a route would have to live under it and carry translations\nin three languages for a technical page nobody reads in Spanish. The middleware\nmatcher already excludes paths containing a dot, so a .html file bypasses the\nlocale rewriting instead of fighting it. And a page with no framework in it\ndemonstrates something a React route could not: the integration needs no React,\nno bundler, and no build step on the host''s side.\n\nBoth variants are shown side by side with the trade-off stated, and every message\neither one emits is logged live — including the version check, which is the only\npart of a versioned contract that actually does anything.\n\nThe navigate handler shows the intended shape: the embed asks, the host decides.\nHere it opens a tab; a different host could ignore it entirely.","tree":{"sha":"8ec1b003254a7643324ba292e46d67d1cc5ebc14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/8ec1b003254a7643324ba292e46d67d1cc5ebc14"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ec1b003254a7643324ba292e46d67d1cc5ebc14\nparent 90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787185734 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787185734 -0300\n\nfeat: host the Cygnus embed on a cross-origin demo page (#80)\n\nThe embeddable widget lives in the cygnus repo and is served from\ncygnus.samuelsantana.dev. A demo page on that same origin would prove nothing —\nthe whole claim is that it works on a site the widget''s project does not\ncontrol, and this domain is exactly that.\n\nPlain HTML in public/, not a route, for three reasons. There is no root layout\noutside [locale], so a route would have to live under it and carry translations\nin three languages for a technical page nobody reads in Spanish. The middleware\nmatcher already excludes paths containing a dot, so a .html file bypasses the\nlocale rewriting instead of fighting it. And a page with no framework in it\ndemonstrates something a React route could not: the integration needs no React,\nno bundler, and no build step on the host''s side.\n\nBoth variants are shown side by side with the trade-off stated, and every message\neither one emits is logged live — including the version check, which is the only\npart of a versioned contract that actually does anything.\n\nThe navigate handler shows the intended shape: the embed asks, the host decides.\nHere it opens a tab; a different host could ignore it entirely.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhkpGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkXoQAD63pI8a0aT6wv38pU3+8WIf\n6GXKAIXmxXwa+sityuYtugL9CMWVtH40+KJ5L7ZHqqBkUZcrzo+lEj3dxWQfCvTY\nFLoQLYoqls8vU8D6nyE87jq0adYdW42jEDKxr8rWwihzMPzDVVhaxVlZYqsecubA\n/ZJbLE0ruj6sPWNdCsUFF0JJMLGlM4wW670ac1ErmzvlVQt2PaEAV/tNNoFK8yRK\ngGISpltb6E3BNZL8HgLe2sFu2l1j2fyX7FciNgknRWX87fk0e0QDf7+01xH4X84f\n2nehLv82XF+0mSK1UItNzJdiU73SGvVg+RJzBZPCe8VVCBd8ZjC3L/eT2K55bHNp\nxHkqfEx5H5nny7gBhVduLtav5grIHdEVNj3AjU874g1R4qqEBk0u+egQd82k0dax\nDcH1A8gB95sJDGWKDLenuR5kMMH7xW4FWjIV8JUSbyKrKaE1OzXAjLhYYj9XOdZw\nPDYsrkvsL/cp/XgOC/hByGB4XD/NE2jt1U72lFV+DmM+77yaxtlTHo0RNVNNqJXS\nYAOB0L+Rvcg+oZPCo3f+j2kwpgZkpE9UOjUKxLDTQCeKb1lKSBMuuzCG7KsvjSHo\nYMu2GrKXHPdBy6wOysKlocy05Xt1D74JqPSFRX0UVEVe7nsm1mP6ion6Knx5z6Fi\n8vyT3oMkfeJhkcubIA3g\n=bYNB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-20T00:28:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDRhZWY0YWVjYjdlNDFiNzU5NDU2NGVhM2NhOTQyYWJmMDk1YzQxMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674","sha":"90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674"}],"sha":"4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/4aef4aecb7e41b7594564ea3ca942abf095c4121"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:06:25Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T23:06:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: prerender public pages by moving auth out of the render path (#78)\n\n* perf: prerender public pages by moving auth out of the render path\n\nBlogHeader read the auth cookie in a Server Component and is rendered from\nthe (blog) layout, so every public page was server-rendered per request —\ngenerateStaticParams prerendered nothing and the fetch-level revalidate was\nData Cache only, never page ISR.\n\nAuth is now resolved after hydration via GET /api/me and a provider in the\npublic layout. The home page is prerendered per locale with 60s ISR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct the preview-indexing argument against host-derived canonicals\n\nChecked against a real preview deployment: Vercel gates previews behind SSO\nand serves them with X-Robots-Tag: noindex, so the self-referencing canonical\nnever reaches a crawler. Recording it so it does not come back as a reason to\nswitch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: apply the private-docs convention to this branch\n\nmain now gitignores docs/ and untracks everything in it. This branch predates\nthat and still carried docs/rendering-strategies.md as a tracked file, so\nmerging it would have re-added to main exactly what was just removed.\n\nThe six comments that cited the document are rewritten to stand on their own.\nEach already carried its reasoning — the citation was an extra, and an extra\nthat would resolve to nothing for anyone reading this repository on GitHub.\nThe one exception was layout.tsx''s \"lists which ones and why\", which deferred\nreal information; it now names the mechanism instead (`export const dynamic`).\n\nNo behaviour changes. The document itself stays on disk, untracked.\n\n* fix(e2e): point Playwright at the port the dev server actually uses\n\nplaywright.config.ts declared baseURL and webServer.url as localhost:3000,\nbut `npm run dev` runs `next dev -p 3021`. The suite could therefore never\nstart: Playwright launched the dev server, waited two minutes for a port\nnothing was listening on, and failed with a webServer timeout before running\na single test.\n\nThat is why this suite had never run — it was read as an environment problem\n(the config does need a vertex-api instance) when the first failure came\nearlier than that and was pure configuration.\n\nWith the port corrected, all 13 tests pass: dashboard gating, locale routing,\nthe language switcher, and the home page.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9bd047f3bac960a9f424b72124a3105996d4751c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/9bd047f3bac960a9f424b72124a3105996d4751c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/90b76648989c2e6bdd38c1c13492a9e4404ce674","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bd047f3bac960a9f424b72124a3105996d4751c\nparent 1fe54226c1d803621837957023a117a32699fd70\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1787180785 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787180785 -0300\n\nperf: prerender public pages by moving auth out of the render path (#78)\n\n* perf: prerender public pages by moving auth out of the render path\n\nBlogHeader read the auth cookie in a Server Component and is rendered from\nthe (blog) layout, so every public page was server-rendered per request —\ngenerateStaticParams prerendered nothing and the fetch-level revalidate was\nData Cache only, never page ISR.\n\nAuth is now resolved after hydration via GET /api/me and a provider in the\npublic layout. The home page is prerendered per locale with 60s ISR.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct the preview-indexing argument against host-derived canonicals\n\nChecked against a real preview deployment: Vercel gates previews behind SSO\nand serves them with X-Robots-Tag: noindex, so the self-referencing canonical\nnever reaches a crawler. Recording it so it does not come back as a reason to\nswitch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: apply the private-docs convention to this branch\n\nmain now gitignores docs/ and untracks everything in it. This branch predates\nthat and still carried docs/rendering-strategies.md as a tracked file, so\nmerging it would have re-added to main exactly what was just removed.\n\nThe six comments that cited the document are rewritten to stand on their own.\nEach already carried its reasoning — the citation was an extra, and an extra\nthat would resolve to nothing for anyone reading this repository on GitHub.\nThe one exception was layout.tsx''s \"lists which ones and why\", which deferred\nreal information; it now names the mechanism instead (`export const dynamic`).\n\nNo behaviour changes. The document itself stays on disk, untracked.\n\n* fix(e2e): point Playwright at the port the dev server actually uses\n\nplaywright.config.ts declared baseURL and webServer.url as localhost:3000,\nbut `npm run dev` runs `next dev -p 3021`. The suite could therefore never\nstart: Playwright launched the dev server, waited two minutes for a port\nnothing was listening on, and failed with a webServer timeout before running\na single test.\n\nThat is why this suite had never run — it was read as an environment problem\n(the config does need a vertex-api instance) when the first failure came\nearlier than that and was pure configuration.\n\nWith the port corrected, all 13 tests pass: dashboard gating, locale routing,\nthe language switcher, and the home page.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhjbxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtMoQAGKM4h0fW1aGp8HdXW8SUUfw\njZTeS8iSmfPPqCN0xoGb9TL8kX745LELG4DSebhah7/7JNZ1GjRwFOxsgIGT0Dkb\njjKR/1JdMc5Slfd6fu+hsv1bfeOx0h+xpduYCdN/BNHeQX1wBkGo56d2Il/H8ZGE\nW9jP3AN3aU7HQh6Jy1fHkYSYZDLJefbx7Q1rR2lZ5rE3QtEKi217A+lQ85iqIl8J\nrZG5/GxniT1zwQy+9UIIfoNwST7uyj3TEaMlc2+9lMAStNyaxoUFgwLwgaIguzPD\n/RM+ctIHNCmPv3BgSeqb0/q0XPT5oeOcvrbVFMT1wpVmN+OjAonEjAaTERPOFb8r\nA8mi41t5KgemfVgYmbHQsQ0pECwigA0dtvnpduwFJa6DPA0bgLWSuF0U7DYIMkRt\nK6nN+SeKmSEvAiSzcLe1ZpxP2EUyPlvfIHPKpiu1fX8JHipwQ6x0Ur95DFVKtCCb\n4+fQ/yv3Z2h37HQJY8vkPRTqojxCnexXhXXFwefKTtJ9OHG64hE2Its+/lSCi0u7\nuAxbuj9XPExLOXdD+x3LYBEMpHwr5244NoMkYZm6Js72+ezVG+OaUZel06U9fZtS\n3