ly \"hovered\" the elements carrying the tooltip, and it\nnever showed. Moving title to that Link (confirmed via\nelementFromPoint to be the real hit target) fixes it for both the\nfeatured card and the grid.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a926b55368b0a3bff9c8b05e0bef1e4af6ff2a7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/a926b55368b0a3bff9c8b05e0bef1e4af6ff2a7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/af312f4fddb589d2d95aa363b625181d9b5cb645","verification":{"payload":"tree a926b55368b0a3bff9c8b05e0bef1e4af6ff2a7d\nparent d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1785033670 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785033670 -0300\n\nfix: move Home card hover tooltip off the pointer-events-none elements (#70)\n\ntitle lived on the h2/p, but both are pointer-events-none so clicks\nfall through to the full-card overlay Link — which meant the mouse\nnever actually \"hovered\" the elements carrying the tooltip, and it\nnever showed. Moving title to that Link (confirmed via\nelementFromPoint to be the real hit target) fixes it for both the\nfeatured card and the grid.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZXPGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9rMQAH8iscyPxcATbjwOpSeRKeiS\nEMHYHcpxAsvpnKdJ9MT85sdwT4kbGgwiQ0xc5H49FsMhuXUrhkOQ1sxEIBdwvnFg\nwDe2opSYFgTeptPQm5Y+XfOo9sODVW/idQeTkgCHK3YXDhtGOvLECzdsv5Dsqtjm\n4suiawo5ZVLUBBQkF3ufftxfBam39KiTtEmInBz/JodzQy/XHi/1urkIt+h2uA8a\n2V5+e2QKUMdBlcCxRaPE0GDJ9d9nTycvaJ89TRR4OhA9GoNx4bhtyvl+8+v6FBzD\n4Wa+auP+FKWHUm9NC1FL2QHHZo1uF3AxaTW7U0R4sx6KQlhagFAtieXgdyTqJc+X\n1mZ+KR9GIghjkv9YH3e2xR0PIoT+OoNubyt5J7UguZDy9Vx96SGCJ+XiFp1SL6Ab\nm67+ltU8IMGG+FR+2HmKOL7HkOssPp/g+d7jGP2VdauQwfWzBei0t3dYF3IY5RDO\nnfP7l7N+V7RKrI7hQEYVIuNHw9QdmC7Kb6+mBiS53Sl2owIFp0qkJ5LXNh3fFxvR\nk4YeqhfxqBkVVyFeOY8KA8xbnS51HLp6CEr64LPu7GqMUZ+VKf9nDTAHb6PTZZLv\n7JcX0rYlRUTFiRuSo8t5xfm8yi4f4M4R0ym8hFf7cw33gtYJveWiu7bIfc3cqTYo\nuciaomzdEU9GK0+4hYM0\n=+Mkh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T02:41:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/af312f4fddb589d2d95aa363b625181d9b5cb645","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGFmMzEyZjRmZGRiNTg5ZDJkOTVhYTM2M2I2MjUxODFkOWI1Y2I2NDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14","sha":"d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14"}],"sha":"af312f4fddb589d2d95aa363b625181d9b5cb645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/af312f4fddb589d2d95aa363b625181d9b5cb645"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-26T02:32:39Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-26T02:32:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: redesign the About page with a sticky profile sidebar and richer Home post cards (#69)\n\n* feat: refresh blog visual identity and restructure the About page into sections\n\nAdopts a refined glass-morphism system (near-black background, softer glows,\npill-shaped header) across Home, About and Post, and splits About''s single\nmarkdown blob into numbered section cards driven by its own headings so the\npage finally has real visual hierarchy instead of one continuous wall of text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore the blue-tinted base background over the near-black one\n\nKeeps the refreshed glows/noise from the redesign, but the near-black\n#08090b base read too neutral compared to the site''s usual blue-tinted\ndark backdrop — reverting to #161c2a for a side-by-side visual check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: highlight the About section a TOC link actually jumps to\n\nShort sections (e.g. \"Um pouco da minha trajetória\") scroll correctly to\ntheir own card, but the next card immediately fills most of the viewport\nbelow it, making the jump look like it landed one section too far. A\npure-CSS :target ring on the section that matches the URL hash removes\nthe ambiguity regardless of how short that section''s text is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: sync active TOC link from URL hash instead of only IntersectionObserver\n\nClicking a TOC link scrolled to the right section, but the highlight\nsometimes didn''t follow — the IntersectionObserver only recognizes a\nheading once it crosses a narrow band near the top of the viewport, and\non taller viewports the next section can already be poking into that\nsame band by the time the observer''s callback runs, overriding the\ncorrect one. Now a hashchange listener sets the active id directly from\nthe URL first, and briefly suppresses the observer so it can''t\nimmediately stomp on that during the smooth-scroll landing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert: drop the glass-morphism redesign, keep only the Home card layout\n\nReverts About, Post, header, background, TOC and comments back to their\npre-redesign look. The one thing kept is the Home page''s structural\nsplit — the most recent post as a featured card above the grid, the\nrest below it — reimplemented with the original slate/emerald styling\ninstead of the redesign''s glass tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: redesign About with a sticky profile sidebar and numbered sections\n\nReplaces the plain profile card + single markdown blob with a two-column\nlayout: a sticky profile card (avatar, role badge, real social links) on\nthe right, and the About content split into numbered cards on the left,\none per top-level \"##\" heading. Sections are derived from the real\nmarkdown via splitMarkdownSections/extractHeadings — no new content or\ndata fields — and rendered through the existing ReactMarkdown pipeline\nrather than raw HTML.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: truncate long social handles in the About profile card\n\nThe LinkedIn handle (a full URL with no spaces) had nowhere to wrap and\noverflowed the card — flex items default to min-width: auto, which\nblocks shrinking below content size. Giving the handle row min-w-0 and\ntruncating the handle text itself keeps every row inside the card,\nshowing an ellipsis instead of spilling out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: show just the username in About''s social rows, not the full URL\n\nGitHub/LinkedIn already say which service via their icon and label, so\nrepeating \"github.com\"/\"linkedin.com\" was redundant and forced the\nrecent truncation fix to earn its keep. Showing just the username\n(still derived from SOCIAL_PROFILES, still linking to the real URL) is\ncleaner and short enough to never need an ellipsis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add reading time, excerpt and cover hover effect to post cards\n\nPorts three details from a reference design onto the Home page''s\nfeatured card and grid: a Calendar/Clock metadata row with an estimated\nreading time, an auto-generated excerpt (stripped from the post''s own\ncontent, same technique already used for meta descriptions), and a\nsubtle zoom + overlay-fade on the cover on hover. Title/excerpt get a\nnative title attribute so the full text is available on hover once\nline-clamp truncates them. No new data — everything is derived from the\ncontent the list endpoint already returns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: only a real \"#\" h1 should suppress About''s sr-only h1 fallback\n\nstartsWithHeading matched \"#\" through \"######\", so content starting\ndirectly with a \"##\" section (e.g. \"## Sobre mim\", with no separate\nopening greeting) was wrongly treated as already having its own h1 —\nbut that heading renders as an h2 card title, not a page h1, leaving\nthe page with none at all. Only a single \"#\" should count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: show the full article text in the Home cards'' hover tooltip\n\nThe excerpt paragraph''s title attribute showed the same truncated\nexcerpt as its visible text, so hovering revealed nothing new. It now\ncarries the full plain-text article (stripped markdown, same helper\nused for meta descriptions) while the visible line-clamped text stays\nshort — the native tooltip is the one place the whole thing shows up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: show About''s profile card first on mobile, not after all sections\n\nBelow lg the sidebar becomes a normal single-column stack in DOM order\n— content first, profile card last — so a visitor had to scroll past\nall three \"##\" sections before seeing who the page is even about.\norder-last (content) / lg:order-none flips just the visual order below\nlg, leaving the desktop two-column layout and DOM/tab order untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"be26a695c89750bbca64b35cb782e4d1389578f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/be26a695c89750bbca64b35cb782e4d1389578f5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/d498b9b649ffee8e8bcfca672863499b6abb3c14","verification":{"payload":"tree be26a695c89750bbca64b35cb782e4d1389578f5\nparent c8aadbdc061f6fb205497179eb9b2b73d726de86\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1785033159 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785033159 -0300\n\nfeat: redesign the About page with a sticky profile sidebar and richer Home post cards (#69)\n\n* feat: refresh blog visual identity and restructure the About page into sections\n\nAdopts a refined glass-morphism system (near-black background, softer glows,\npill-shaped header) across Home, About and Post, and splits About''s single\nmarkdown blob into numbered section cards driven by its own headings so the\npage finally has real visual hierarchy instead of one continuous wall of text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: restore the blue-tinted base background over the near-black one\n\nKeeps the refreshed glows/noise from the redesign, but the near-black\n#08090b base read too neutral compared to the site''s usual blue-tinted\ndark backdrop — reverting to #161c2a for a side-by-side visual check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: highlight the About section a TOC link actually jumps to\n\nShort sections (e.g. \"Um pouco da minha trajetória\") scroll correctly to\ntheir own card, but the next card immediately fills most of the viewport\nbelow it, making the jump look like it landed one section too far. A\npure-CSS :target ring on the section that matches the URL hash removes\nthe ambiguity regardless of how short that section''s text is.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: sync active TOC link from URL hash instead of only IntersectionObserver\n\nClicking a TOC link scrolled to the right section, but the highlight\nsometimes didn''t follow — the IntersectionObserver only recognizes a\nheading once it crosses a narrow band near the top of the viewport, and\non taller viewports the next section can already be poking into that\nsame band by the time the observer''s callback runs, overriding the\ncorrect one. Now a hashchange listener sets the active id directly from\nthe URL first, and briefly suppresses the observer so it can''t\nimmediately stomp on that during the smooth-scroll landing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert: drop the glass-morphism redesign, keep only the Home card layout\n\nReverts About, Post, header, background, TOC and comments back to their\npre-redesign look. The one thing kept is the Home page''s structural\nsplit — the most recent post as a featured card above the grid, the\nrest below it — reimplemented with the original slate/emerald styling\ninstead of the redesign''s glass tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: redesign About with a sticky profile sidebar and numbered sections\n\nReplaces the plain profile card + single markdown blob with a two-column\nlayout: a sticky profile card (avatar, role badge, real social links) on\nthe right, and the About content split into numbered cards on the left,\none per top-level \"##\" heading. Sections are derived from the real\nmarkdown via splitMarkdownSections/extractHeadings — no new content or\ndata fields — and rendered through the existing ReactMarkdown pipeline\nrather than raw HTML.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: truncate long social handles in the About profile card\n\nThe LinkedIn handle (a full URL with no spaces) had nowhere to wrap and\noverflowed the card — flex items default to min-width: auto, which\nblocks shrinking below content size. Giving the handle row min-w-0 and\ntruncating the handle text itself keeps every row inside the card,\nshowing an ellipsis instead of spilling out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: show just the username in About''s social rows, not the full URL\n\nGitHub/LinkedIn already say which service via their icon and label, so\nrepeating \"github.com\"/\"linkedin.com\" was redundant and forced the\nrecent truncation fix to earn its keep. Showing just the username\n(still derived from SOCIAL_PROFILES, still linking to the real URL) is\ncleaner and short enough to never need an ellipsis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add reading time, excerpt and cover hover effect to post cards\n\nPorts three details from a reference design onto the Home page''s\nfeatured card and grid: a Calendar/Clock metadata row with an estimated\nreading time, an auto-generated excerpt (stripped from the post''s own\ncontent, same technique already used for meta descriptions), and a\nsubtle zoom + overlay-fade on the cover on hover. Title/excerpt get a\nnative title attribute so the full text is available on hover once\nline-clamp truncates them. No new data — everything is derived from the\ncontent the list endpoint already returns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: only a real \"#\" h1 should suppress About''s sr-only h1 fallback\n\nstartsWithHeading matched \"#\" through \"######\", so content starting\ndirectly with a \"##\" section (e.g. \"## Sobre mim\", with no separate\nopening greeting) was wrongly treated as already having its own h1 —\nbut that heading renders as an h2 card title, not a page h1, leaving\nthe page with none at all. Only a single \"#\" should count.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: show the full article text in the Home cards'' hover tooltip\n\nThe excerpt paragraph''s title attribute showed the same truncated\nexcerpt as its visible text, so hovering revealed nothing new. It now\ncarries the full plain-text article (stripped markdown, same helper\nused for meta descriptions) while the visible line-clamped text stays\nshort — the native tooltip is the one place the whole thing shows up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: show About''s profile card first on mobile, not after all sections\n\nBelow lg the sidebar becomes a normal single-column stack in DOM order\n— content first, profile card last — so a visitor had to scroll past\nall three \"##\" sections before seeing who the page is even about.\norder-last (content) / lg:order-none flips just the visual order below\nlg, leaving the desktop two-column layout and DOM/tab order untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqZXHHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAziYQAJqnRs6jnvSuJTQwXFQhSVkp\njfnogecAorzJYXX8X1a4rU8PCYhEjrRMsxq8xLLoCbI5LC/jLPYAE2LcMGRMPkVD\n7asKoDZvPu1zr0sds+twmBP+hOEuA5QyinLS8PrPWBCcmw1X3ltzCwdbfMTMybD4\n3xRzRt2i4oOc++btNlgRbkJYsRbyPWIBH2Ilfic9xDhuL+O/eeD6VJAfAHp/+P9E\nNYHb3l0n57osPOrAw7gS9S8h+/d6s2Xf/PySRnsR5E52lXKnrlw4ULUzVEUYisUA\nCqDg0F9VVzCMeaPJdTgc7hMsxsyLQp/tUC01yyZXHH1CVpUL/m3AS37JSqND8//1\nH9LE5KDf9bz7eRaq5SN4mJ7K7y1lGSjJRVKFXOWjwZdHuYQiy67C8RL+qlzo92UU\nVBa3Qofxt7RWrGcd6sn7xh5bDYiZd22GqbSCrKHPSVDB3Jk774BBkq0OeHG0n4Kc\nR3mMURJCWFJqG9B8oEaPo7fK9kAvRBTvhhGEwXySLSoJw2JQmuBK/ewkG5O76mSk\nGd9enTWtueuymJh4RsCJg/Z1WTJnXF6v8RcW9OWG/9gCBzfh/2ET54emZDPU9e1p\nL6+Ie73V7/QK7TJRePxUX7nGF5xJmLTu4Wx/Kdw7YnwYVzXZEKhXPz11kL5MO5lN\n6fcqcE+t6hnUnarxlLdn\n=yjvG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-26T02:32:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":