bb","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGNmMzVhZjc5ZmVkNDZhOTBmZWYzYWZlZGUxMWJkZWNmMjk4OWVhYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/9b9a20a305a836a8ee5411b7c3412c545bf55fdf","sha":"9b9a20a305a836a8ee5411b7c3412c545bf55fdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/9b9a20a305a836a8ee5411b7c3412c545bf55fdf"}],"sha":"cf35af79fed46a90fef3afede11bdecf2989eabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/cf35af79fed46a90fef3afede11bdecf2989eabb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/9b9a20a305a836a8ee5411b7c3412c545bf55fdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T23:38:35Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T23:38:35Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: derive absolute metadata URLs from the request Host instead of an env var (#40)\n\n* fix: derive absolute metadata URLs from the request Host instead of an env var\n\nConfirmed live: LinkedIn''s own crawler (simulated with its exact bot\nuser agent) received a fully correct og:description tag, yet its Post\nInspector still only showed title/link/image, never the description.\nRoot cause: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL points at the apex domain\n(samuelsantana.dev), but the site''s canonical, non-redirecting domain\nis actually www.samuelsantana.dev — the apex 308-redirects to www for\nevery path, including the page itself and og-fallback.png. So og:url\nand og:image both pointed at URLs that immediately redirect elsewhere.\nCrawlers that validate og:url against the URL they actually fetched\n(LinkedIn does) treat that mismatch as untrustworthy and silently drop\nthe rest of the card rather than erroring outright.\n\nAdds getSiteUrl() (src/lib/site-url.ts), which reads the incoming\nrequest''s Host header instead of trusting the env var to match\nwhichever domain variant actually serves traffic — verified live with\nspoofed Host headers that canonical/og:url/og:image now always match\nwhatever domain the request came in on. Since the apex redirect happens\nbefore any Next.js code runs, every request that reaches this app in\nproduction will have Host: www.samuelsantana.dev, so this is always\ncorrect without needing the env var to be exactly right.\n\nApplied everywhere NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL was used for absolute URLs:\n[locale]/layout.tsx''s metadataBase (converted from a static `metadata`\nexport to async generateMetadata, since a plain object can''t await\nheaders() — this makes every page dynamically rendered rather than\nstatically optimized, an acceptable tradeoff at this app''s scale for\nfixing metadata correctness sitewide, not just on post pages),\nblog/[slug]/page.tsx''s generateMetadata and JSON-LD, sitemap.ts, and\nrobots.ts.\n\n* revert: keep root layout''s metadataBase static, not host-derived\n\nPer feedback: the dynamic-rendering tradeoff (opting the whole app out\nof static optimization) isn''t worth it just for the layout-level\nog:image fallback used by pages without their own metadata override.\nblog/[slug]/page.tsx already builds its own fully-qualified ogImageUrl\nvia getSiteUrl() independently of metadataBase, so the actual reported\nbug (blog post shares missing their description) stays fixed — only\nthe site-wide default (home/about/dashboard pages sharing with no\npost-specific override) still depends on NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL being\ncorrect, same as before this change.","tree":{"sha":"0ccc98947cf4575088c0bdf687931885574a2d7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/0ccc98947cf4575088c0bdf687931885574a2d7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/9b9a20a305a836a8ee5411b7c3412c545bf55fdf","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ccc98947cf4575088c0bdf687931885574a2d7d\nparent 46bf01ac65e6039c6239048759fbec1d22364efe\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783553915 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783553915 -0300\n\nfix: derive absolute metadata URLs from the request Host instead of an env var (#40)\n\n* fix: derive absolute metadata URLs from the request Host instead of an env var\n\nConfirmed live: LinkedIn''s own crawler (simulated with its exact bot\nuser agent) received a fully correct og:description tag, yet its Post\nInspector still only showed title/link/image, never the description.\nRoot cause: NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL points at the apex domain\n(samuelsantana.dev), but the site''s canonical, non-redirecting domain\nis actually www.samuelsantana.dev — the apex 308-redirects to www for\nevery path, including the page itself and og-fallback.png. So og:url\nand og:image both pointed at URLs that immediately redirect elsewhere.\nCrawlers that validate og:url against the URL they actually fetched\n(LinkedIn does) treat that mismatch as untrustworthy and silently drop\nthe rest of the card rather than erroring outright.\n\nAdds getSiteUrl() (src/lib/site-url.ts), which reads the incoming\nrequest''s Host header instead of trusting the env var to match\nwhichever domain variant actually serves traffic — verified live with\nspoofed Host headers that canonical/og:url/og:image now always match\nwhatever domain the request came in on. Since the apex redirect happens\nbefore any Next.js code runs, every request that reaches this app in\nproduction will have Host: www.samuelsantana.dev, so this is always\ncorrect without needing the env var to be exactly right.\n\nApplied everywhere NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL was used for absolute URLs:\n[locale]/layout.tsx''s metadataBase (converted from a static `metadata`\nexport to async generateMetadata, since a plain object can''t await\nheaders() — this makes every page dynamically rendered rather than\nstatically optimized, an acceptable tradeoff at this app''s scale for\nfixing metadata correctness sitewide, not just on post pages),\nblog/[slug]/page.tsx''s generateMetadata and JSON-LD, sitemap.ts, and\nrobots.ts.\n\n* revert: keep root layout''s metadataBase static, not host-derived\n\nPer feedback: the dynamic-rendering tradeoff (opting the whole app out\nof static optimization) isn''t worth it just for the layout-level\nog:image fallback used by pages without their own metadata override.\nblog/[slug]/page.tsx already builds its own fully-qualified ogImageUrl\nvia getSiteUrl() independently of metadataBase, so the actual reported\nbug (blog post shares missing their description) stays fixed — only\nthe site-wide default (home/about/dashboard pages sharing with no\npost-specific override) still depends on NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL being\ncorrect, same as before this change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTt97CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz5gQAIJ8aWBIlhXRa7aUoBMW7Thn\nDfIeJdrActVS/6WhcVzeo0hrzUx8ThRXuQYUB0V+bf2gLDlp1WnxSQ9+fI6W0z+f\nikJ0wp5pqzZzBaVT9GzyGEMtcB4m2IGAi4kEwZ2Eb5r1uLCe3g4rCGTUiqrX/0mO\n/TkAswPOQpAs4rUbNohG0xMfMtNc4Fu6