ion around it. Standardized on \"Article\" (the\ndominant term already used almost everywhere) rather than \"Post\" —\nsmaller diff, and reads more naturally for a reader-facing blog.\nThe underlying Post type/posts table/PostsService naming is\nunaffected; this is translated UI copy only.","tree":{"sha":"4e6b602e698095744ee1649a7a084334b87ec2e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/4e6b602e698095744ee1649a7a084334b87ec2e9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/46bf01ac65e6039c6239048759fbec1d22364efe","verification":{"payload":"tree 4e6b602e698095744ee1649a7a084334b87ec2e9\nparent d3b5c5881c02a5d631bf4575d8f8cf013434e619\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783553888 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783553888 -0300\n\nfix: standardize on \"article\" over \"post\" in user-facing copy (#39)\n\nThe same UI concept was labeled inconsistently across the admin\nsurface: the home page said \"Nenhum artigo publicado ainda\" for the\nempty state while the dashboard''s identical empty state said \"Nenhum\npost publicado ainda\" (same for en/es), and the \"Manage Posts\"\nsection heading didn''t match the \"Artigo\" wording used by every\ncreate/edit/delete action around it. Standardized on \"Article\" (the\ndominant term already used almost everywhere) rather than \"Post\" —\nsmaller diff, and reads more naturally for a reader-facing blog.\nThe underlying Post type/posts table/PostsService naming is\nunaffected; this is translated UI copy only.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTt9gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWOEQADHiTgSDa4jCtaSihvJaStTv\n8aL1ojPl1UUTz6VLgAoD3QyiKlOwgHsDizVqtM6uI7Ib/CcFvx9wVtLzBu95JHVX\naFEAGSPy0SGR+r7yPCrn8HepNbCaNlzFuvny8z0EXsOKtyNnFudi2cTLPIx/W+kO\nAXvaZxz/8W7vKLLP0/MAq+al0g9lB8hCe1oCNPJsv92QWhK/+pUYTHatphb+Z+xr\nC1aG6xKlKLqZhsoqcLoaaJg2f6BaTl03/lE9ozTKCSJoCd6OBtVSG0rISQyh5yb5\n1aQwzSK7OchECeW4b9hTti8k0IPz+6xTP9z2zWv1TKM3uLq5m