ana/vertex-web/commits/bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392"}],"sha":"dbbf07bb11c673b8030a7ac3d85f2f1bff7c3cfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/dbbf07bb11c673b8030a7ac3d85f2f1bff7c3cfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T23:01:10Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T23:01:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: portal the confirm dialog and fix cross-locale cache invalidation (#36)\n\nTwo related bugs reported on the home page''s post listing:\n\n- ConfirmDialog rendered its fixed inset-0 overlay inline instead of\n  through a portal. The home page''s post cards use backdrop-blur-sm,\n  which (like transform/filter) creates a new containing block for\n  position:fixed descendants — so the dialog was sized and clipped to\n  the card''s own small box instead of the viewport, visibly spilling\n  the Cancel button past its left edge. LoginModal.tsx already portals\n  to document.body for the same reason; ConfirmDialog now does too.\n\n- Deleting (or creating/updating) a post called revalidatePath with a\n  literal path (\"/\", \"/dashboard/posts\"), which only busts the cache\n  entry for that exact path. Both routes actually live under the\n  [locale] dynamic segment, so this only ever revalidated the\n  unprefixed pt route — /en and /es visitors kept seeing stale data\n  until the underlying 60s fetch cache expired on its own. The docs''\n  recommended fix for this (revalidatePath with the dynamic route\n  pattern and a \"page\" type) was verified live to not actually bust\n  the cache in this Next.js 16 + Turbopack dev setup; revalidatePath(\"/\",\n  \"layout\") — the docs'' \"revalidate everything\" option — was verified\n  to work reliably and near-instantly instead.","tree":{"sha":"474f015b9729c917a2bbc726e0108eb5c5eb5a10","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/474f015b9729c917a2bbc726e0108eb5c5eb5a10"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392","verification":{"payload":"tree 474f015b9729c917a2bbc726e0108eb5c5eb5a10\nparent 750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783551670 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783551670 -0300\n\nfix: portal the confirm dialog and fix cross-locale cache invalidation (#36)\n\nTwo related bugs reported on the home page''s post listing:\n\n- ConfirmDialog rendered its fixed inset-0 overlay inline instead of\n  through a portal. The home page''s post cards use backdrop-blur-sm,\n  which (like transform/filter) creates a new containing block for\n  position:fixed descendants — so the dialog was sized and clipped to\n  the card''s own small box instead of the viewport, visibly spilling\n  the Cancel button past its left edge. LoginModal.tsx already portals\n  to document.body for the same reason; ConfirmDialog now does too.\n\n- Deleting (or creating/updating) a post called revalidatePath with a\n  literal path (\"/\", \"/dashboard/posts\"), which only busts the cache\n  entry for that exact path. Both routes actually live under the\n  [locale] dynamic segment, so this only ever revalidated the\n  unprefixed pt route — /en and /es visitors kept seeing stale data\n  until the underlying 60s fetch cache expired on its own. The docs''\n  recommended fix for this (revalidatePath with the dynamic route\n  pattern and a \"page\" type) was verified live to not actually bust\n  the cache in this Next.js 16 + Turbopack dev setup; revalidatePath(\"/\",\n  \"layout\") — the docs'' \"revalidate everything\" option — was verified\n  to work reliably and near-instantly instead.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTta2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYWMQAJG+sSr+UP7nKi/Ra0eo0eAL\ndTy7SlNXov8NxzkEWTWXziBD+wKrobrvB8JkQukxvPgD7O1S/Tkh7CMhA85/31kF\nWJFl4hQB2O3h7w6rNO1Q+dewerNBjjsxdqevBkurBP7kqUBugJExZI8Q/CMW1TYr\nfabmRtoCjmkh/NIZRJVwPrD5njSoJszzE3SjjtMljBCtCBOIGiCAJxuuaDHck5GT\nAMaLNkeQ5QnWsPeYj6wmy4JNzWf7ShJLKeXBMFoi9GfH31IBEGgwgBv9ZCnQnJP1\nBgQfRIviWSNhtgRVubCsfksVgViMO6btcm7flOSJLOoB0F6uIuEqxfWj0alPIMmV\nNfDSzNAxk6gsc5O3bHeJvsQL0TMevneVMZcp0yBf9vQ7gOSdFEFSWdpuEYBa4s4L\nv/YkZk8OxuDW45J2zGxV9aTnrDgZW1nVXEbR/PVa12QSOyl+iPjjwg1+uN2t/8GM\nD/ywtWLPPbQ76DONJqThVoRqnx8Vajzm0EzYg+V3zJcB98VjYoG9CpmMnPCNABzv\nHQ2P1bNVq4bWQ3ZvOPETRyUJwyEoOFw2yoOv/1/KBKzxcYSzh+X6D4lr1NE0F+A3\nmkdJms26M2PoO9HLrCt5wbvB8+NLt8bLy3FbFdfUbjcoCpj79y32oqUh0pFqnDSh\ngkNgFBvmeNfiGjBDnTKy\n=13FB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T23:01:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGJhYjU5MDUzOGExYzliNTkxZmJjYjI5NTJkYjg3ZmU5NTkwNTIzOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4","sha":"750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4"}],"sha":"bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/bab590538a1c9b591fbcb2952db87fe959052392"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T22:18:26Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T22:18:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: only advertise hreflang/canonical for genuinely translated locales (#35)\n\nThe sitemap and per-post metadata treated every locale as a real\ntranslation, even for posts that only exist in Portuguese: a pt-only\npost''s /en/ and /es/ URLs (which just render the pt fallback content)\nwere listed in the sitemap with hreflang=\"en\"/\"es\" alternates, and the\npage itself self-referenced its own URL as the canonical — telling\nsearch engines \"this is a genuine English page\" about a URL that''s\nactually Portuguese content under an English-tagged URL.\n\nAdds getTranslatedLocales() (which locales a post has its own content\nin, not just which locales it resolves under) and uses it to: only\nemit a sitemap entry/hreflang alternate for locales with real content,\nand point a fallback page''s canonical back at the real pt original\ninstead of self-referencing. Also replaces the Manage Posts dashboard\ntable''s near-identical local helper with this shared one.","tree":{"sha":"e2d6c7372799fb4f3b801bf74c2cdf9c4c6585e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/e2d6c7372799fb4f3b801bf74c2cdf9c4c6585e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/750e5899fe2cd7048d6a7af0934814d1cc348db4","verification":{"payload":"tree e2d6c7372799fb4f3b801bf74c2cdf9c4c6585e7\nparent c491006b79325964f3c9fb0620cb6b583fdba65c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783549106 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783549106 -0300\n\nfix: only advertise hreflang/canonical for genuinely translated locales (#35)\n\nThe sitemap and per-post metadata treated every locale as a real\ntranslation, even for posts that only exist in Portuguese: a pt-only\npost''s /en/ and /es/ URLs (which just render the pt fallback content)\nwere listed in the sitemap with hreflang=\"en\"/\"es\" alternates, and the\npage itself self-referenced its own URL as the canonical — telling\nsearch engines \"this is a genuine English page\" about a URL that''s\nactually Portuguese content under an English-tagged URL.\n\nAdds getTranslatedLocales() (which locales a post has its own content\nin, not just which locales it resolves under) and uses it to: only\nemit a sitemap entry/hreflang alternate for locales with real content,\nand point a fallback page''s canonical back at the real pt original\ninstead of self-referencing. Also replaces the Manage Posts dashboard\ntable''s near-identical local helper with this shared one.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTsyyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzX8QACkoKOeJ9U+8gFlu50p03QiY\nyR3opidnwD606wTO0+amDlxbkZJf0ATS+kY9+h49kMoUPy61OQ+2ws/zodlsv5Xb\nSysiRre4vAzpZGxG7HIcUbgZmxIa31akkZQPNdSFIWe7wSeC9LKWi4XXVf1kBiOf\nYHl9t/cDbAqM+fZywLjYUMzEc+m26tnabOf3mwq4J5m4Eq7wHhjHZyjS8NV1StUO\n7glC9visD5F0BMQVMToJ0UmgQbCx93mxDaqqAEwTupRO31K1fk/Tynn1oneR6/F7\nuRuM3oH18vIs850epM59aukfRO+ZzziQqPXHzvgPA6NOFgN9tf5iMGskxuT2zYS7\niz3hjkGF0MeA1zRGRE7HNGmAfwGUo8pjxZUQbTfhxOXM5IRuHBCfJMUJixB0WFUG\nKZXgGsCQxbWCXRd1/zeLZi0fbtx0pwtvAxRVJ2j3blak1GxT8XwcT2nmkIUY6JW3\neNwuk11328R0bTWaPgvPhFjxdRMQXaLvtjbLRkDkvB9X0XSWim0l6K89mIY13J+s\n1/HgZ5ui0mcET5dkaY/IvHpkWiO92wrkVfPS2an0ipyE87MUrE5uenAo6UtVSO84\n67nFn/xK8n4w4KlGuUCm1k3IM