","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/5462d23772afb214430b229e15adf8e645ef631f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:45:52Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T19:45:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: give post creation its own dedicated dashboard page (#28)\n\nClicking \"Novo Artigo\" from the home page''s admin panel landed on\n/dashboard/posts, a page whose own h1 read \"Gerenciar Posts\" — a\nmismatch with the link''s label, and it crammed the create form\ndirectly above the full posts listing/management table.\n\nSplits them, mirroring how /dashboard/posts/[id]/edit is already its\nown page separate from the listing:\n- /dashboard/posts/new — new page, h1 \"Novo Artigo\", just the create\n  form (same \"back to panel\" link + heading-duplicated-in-the-form-card\n  pattern the edit page already uses).\n- /dashboard/posts — now purely the management page: h1 \"Gerenciar\n  Posts\", the listing table, and a prominent \"Novo Artigo\" button that\n  links to the new page instead of hosting the form inline.\n\ncreatePostAction now redirects to /dashboard/posts on success (same\npattern updatePostAction already uses) instead of just calling the\nform''s reset() — there''s no listing on the same screen to reset back\ninto anymore, so staying put after creating would strand the admin on\nan empty form with no visible confirmation.","tree":{"sha":"34b8425d69aac3908d1cf38e1a47e4ced55540df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/34b8425d69aac3908d1cf38e1a47e4ced55540df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/5462d23772afb214430b229e15adf8e645ef631f","verification":{"payload":"tree 34b8425d69aac3908d1cf38e1a47e4ced55540df\nparent 2d5081a8a8398d5be25e3db21301ca013e3f2f1e\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783539952 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783539952 -0300\n\nfeat: give post creation its own dedicated dashboard page (#28)\n\nClicking \"Novo Artigo\" from the home page''s admin panel landed on\n/dashboard/posts, a page whose own h1 read \"Gerenciar Posts\" — a\nmismatch with the link''s label, and it crammed the create form\ndirectly above the full posts listing/management table.\n\nSplits them, mirroring how /dashboard/posts/[id]/edit is already its\nown page separate from the listing:\n- /dashboard/posts/new — new page, h1 \"Novo Artigo\", just the create\n  form (same \"back to panel\" link + heading-duplicated-in-the-form-card\n  pattern the edit page already uses).\n- /dashboard/posts — now purely the management page: h1 \"Gerenciar\n  Posts\", the listing table, and a prominent \"Novo Artigo\" button that\n  links to the new page instead of hosting the form inline.\n\ncreatePostAction now redirects to /dashboard/posts on success (same\npattern updatePostAction already uses) instead of just calling the\nform''s reset() — there''s no listing on the same screen to reset back\ninto anymore, so staying put after creating would str