tForm reused a single <input>/<textarea> per\nfield group (title, slug, content), swapping which form field\nregister() bound it to based on the active language tab. react-hook-\nform doesn''t resync an uncontrolled input''s displayed DOM value when\nthe field name behind it changes — so switching tabs could carry over\nstale text into the wrong field, or wipe a field''s real value entirely\nonce you tabbed away and back.\n\nReproduced on a pre-existing post (created before per-locale fields\nexisted): opening its edit form, clicking English then Spanish, then\nback to Português, cleared the Portuguese title that had loaded\ncorrectly moments earlier — a real data-loss bug on save, not just a\ndisplay glitch.\n\nFix: render one persistent input/textarea per language (title, slug,\ncontent), each with its own stable register() call, and toggle\nvisibility with the \"hidden\" attribute instead of swapping which field\na shared element is bound to. Verified via Playwright: typed distinct\ntext into en and es tabs, round-tripped through all three tabs, saved,\nand confirmed the DB held the right value in each column with the\noriginal pt data untouched.","tree":{"sha":"a871bf2efab4e8c5f508a147cedb87c632b0aeb7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/a871bf2efab4e8c5f508a147cedb87c632b0aeb7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/2d5081a8a8398d5be25e3db21301ca013e3f2f1e","verification":{"payload":"tree a871bf2efab4e8c5f508a147cedb87c632b0aeb7\nparent fb08dd81f01a906ce3759127dc1df4c20241b983\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783538624 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783538624 -0300\n\nfix: stop language tabs from wiping post form fields (#27)\n\nCreatePostForm/EditPostForm reused a single <input>/<textarea> per\nfield group (title, slug, content), swapping which form field\nregister() bound it to based on the active language tab. react-hook-\nform doesn''t resync an uncontrolled input''s displayed DOM value when\nthe field name behind it changes — so switching tabs could carry over\nstale text into the wrong field, or wipe a field''s real value entirely\nonce you tabbed away and back.\n\nReproduced on a pre-existing post (created before per-locale fields\nexisted): opening its edit form, clicking English then Spanish, then\nback to Português, cleared the Portuguese title that had loaded\ncorrectly moments earlier — a real data-loss bug on save, not just a\ndisplay glitch.\n\nFix: render one persistent input/textarea per language (title, slug,\ncontent), each with its own stable register() call, and toggle\nvisibility with the \"hidden\" attribute instead of swapping which field\na shared element is bound to. Verified via Playwright: typed distinct\ntext into en and es tabs, round-tripped through all three tabs, saved,\nand confirmed the DB held the right value in each column with the\noriginal pt data untouched.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTqPACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHQoQAACO8PvHttnmOkbHrPUthH4f\n3aTfnwrqXaUrlYC23odRInwPfZu/U08ueb+2XZ/4qzXCyrdtuODfQ+KYqU3yMBhC\nqBzV+l4WxZB3gYGblKgaoUvaDyqHuMpUuDz8hhSIb8ZI/0q122M7y9E/ot5gTPDP\nvH/KrtjKSWMmqmdygk9OdIXiJ7JsaLJuaXKrm54L8epXQHyT6q70VKTgZ56AhO+e\non4xDA1xI0hfvU+xWnzbWyGFV0LprUUEQdxMqhKH7Uia30ssnYUmhYt+MJot0wQg\nMK4FcQ3xpsb4U8WuhGzJAjK4ZM+4EJkVu2sThRx/tVWjAI6mpRz7h0sz/o0cJhI7\n0Ub/fp2QztionXXTIjttSX9TA9X5Gycm3MKWEJVc+Qctzm2/fEc2SiE34rQtSWmv\nP1/DiyHySle7ftWpsQb6q/l22fD2YS0jozWn9sl4BVmE9jvrZ1IcN1Fz3Mvu3F0R\nzK6FpX2AChmcS40juQZWlnmTIHT5d6cqR5iY49dfndu1wrUkRj9OhndpgPXyaEeb\n7ZD/Q7IqcEaV1OR2YG5FFla/ZPCLRxzOlWp6NEVe89I6GDCMLvsxBsAQx41o+LXz\nfjy/6PXcHNwTIrl3gbkFpL5VPnJc0d8mwHQIVs2kfg/nS1W0l3e8/pOvEXBEDbed\nJcqNVf8xvb6tamDiB/Cm\n=mdOz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T19:23:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{