0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T17:55:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: reserve scrollbar gutter to stop header shifting on content load (#21)\n\nEvery mx-auto-centered element (the sticky header, most visibly) sits\nslightly differently depending on whether the page currently needs a\nvertical scrollbar — a classic (non-overlay) scrollbar consumes ~15-17px\nof layout width the moment content grows past one screenful, and a\nmargin:auto box re-centers into whatever''s left. On the home page this\nshowed up as the header nudging over once enough posts had rendered in\nto push the page past the fold.\n\nscrollbar-gutter: stable on <html> reserves that space unconditionally,\nso the available width — and the header''s position — never depends on\nwhether the page happens to be tall enough to scroll yet.","tree":{"sha":"9be9a344272fbd17970eaa9dea4666684ced156c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/9be9a344272fbd17970eaa9dea4666684ced156c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/f8d5b84184b30192f45af61c196555f720d7e2b6","verification":{"payload":"tree 9be9a344272fbd17970eaa9dea4666684ced156c\nparent a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783533317 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783533317 -0300\n\nfix: reserve scrollbar gutter to stop header shifting on content load (#21)\n\nEvery mx-auto-centered element (the sticky header, most visibly) sits\nslightly differently depending on whether the page currently needs a\nvertical scrollbar — a classic (non-overlay) scrollbar consumes ~15-17px\nof layout width the moment content grows past one screenful, and a\nmargin:auto box re-centers into whatever''s left. On the home page this\nshowed up as the header nudging over once enough posts had rendered in\nto push the page past the fold.\n\nscrollbar-gutter: stable on <html> reserves that space unconditionally,\nso the available width — and the header''s position — never depends on\nwhether the page happens to be tall enough to scroll yet.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTo8FCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVv0QAEB+sbLptmt7/z/jOX4Xvi1q\npcj2t6gwUBLQnKiRFeyUtyL2qfx6V9wKWVTBnhs1QqkB7oDOXSynC1iUVy0v+sbG\nzUPBAtTiiMUDjlEgHBu4nI+ZZoHVKKBf5DyiJo9ITu02UE8WY60tgO8mNfop34Az\nBG75BYzjCBcBJCml+23tGF5G5ehGWmt/e7ksUsNuR/hJZr7xoCtvEsw57nHN8B0H\n/tIsPPmw9I7Hf7tZTugHXSA46WgRiQHYD5eRf6xlW+cMgjLA+hwyfKWjvw1Ixy0o\nMjSSno2pGJELLe4jG5x3c9WM8D7tuGCJ2dCcENbXKowh6wnkP90Y8dTXd+XcWjmx\neOPJ+HAQrRU1xnBdyRH9d+KcZwZHeGPG9wkWef24xLzPL/dAmAT3ue1K9I9cAS0k\nCfCvumy6bIZtlso9kLBAwx481KbXXDfRvN9uqWdbTtfHBMShU/s06DEWZgTBbUWu\nleo4IEE+/zxOKQqvgLJTLQ5WbRn8WLlMN1tmI9A+CQ6dtELnlmat3QqNENd7Zjl3\nEduktqiADOBA4UuT2l7nAq2FMmdPRFH3jaLsWucJ5IqKJKHIqHfYrKeA876Fyffr\ncqnUqlEfiFg9jDX+FC5IZ3zTPGl+fcRmB43HsobSGV7tpiUorZKlHEwev8FvKuRt\nLZNJukvgeK2n6hQjmNys\n=qvMZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T17:55:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/f8d5b84184b30192f45af61c196555f720d7e2b6","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGY4ZDViODQxODRiMzAxOTJmNDVhZjYxYzE5NjU1NWY3MjBkN2UyYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25","sha":"a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25"}],"sha":"f8d5b84184b30192f45af61c196555f720d7e2b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/f8d5b84184b30192f45af61c196555f720d7e2b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T17:31:39Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T17:31:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: nest blog/[slug] inside (blog) group to stop header remounts (#20)\n\nblog/[slug] was a sibling of the (blog) route group with its own\nbyte-for-byte copy-pasted layout.tsx (identical BlogBackground +\nBlogHeader + BlogFooter chrome). Next.js can''t recognize two separate\nlayout files as \"the same\" chrome even when their JSX is identical, so\nevery navigation between a post and the home/about pages unmounted and\nremounted the whole header — visible as a flash/reflow on \"Voltar para\no Blog\" (confirmed via a DOM-node marker test: the header element was\na different node after navigating, not the same one re-rendered).\n\nMoving blog/[slug] and blog/page.tsx inside (blog) — route groups add\nno URL segment, so /blog/[slug] and /blog resolve identically — means\nevery page in the group now shares one layout.tsx instance, so React\npreserves the header/background/footer DOM across client-side\nnavigation instead of tearing it down.","tree":{"sha":"44f9363c2b1137065f28a93208ea096c62d601f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/44f9363c2b1137065f28a93208ea096c62d601f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25","verification":{"payload":"tree 44f9363c2b1137065f28a93208ea096c62d601f2\nparent 68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783531899 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783531899 -0300\n\nfix: nest blog/[slug] inside (blog) group to stop header remounts (#20)\n\nblog/[slug] was a sibling of the (blog) route group with its own\nbyte-for-byte copy-pasted layout.tsx (identical BlogBackground +\nBlogHeader + BlogFooter chrome). Next.js can''t recognize two separate\nlayout files as \"the same\" chrome even when their JSX is identical, so\nevery navigation between a post and the home/about pages unmounted and\nremounted the whole header — visible as a flash/reflow on \"Voltar para\no Blog\" (confirmed via a DOM-node marker test: the header element was\na different node after navigating, not the same one re-rendered).\n\nMoving blog/[slug] and blog/page.tsx inside (blog) — route groups add\nno URL segment, so /blog/[slug] and /blog resolve identically — means\nevery page in the group now shares one layout.tsx instance, so React\npreserves the header/background/footer DOM across client-side\nnavigation instead of tearing it down.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTol7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ9wQAAtq1ZVBXP4L6F/7eUDv7DoE\nrQdQRgAWzcxGOSmf44MEhvoPisnidMyBmFr8bbguXjIgxcY9bcL8iyuJCByiOZUf\nJO/KwRcbz0UZLAbE3ncrAOv7V5rEWKld/4Ruea4sUZ/QXXcdA/8EZ3pgQ+E14IeY\nYBs8outsVastV80oNcq5UgjcS1+jFfm7z2dBPyACKGqssXrGXXP15u4Hrx7nfb6U\nfvD8e+O4m6l+xOoWaTo3Gqo3hSsKQdRprYrDwf6XHJPOYn02Rd3+BQbPvcD8B+g/\naSZR7qAx+QYH63AgM8vCnMPVO4WOs/gXwrt1SJDzYxejhs9Acji/53QNLl2wz5wN\nwrtUy4k1nRpDv4NlhROxPwfxvbv71JfVVCnT2cYrCJiKNDSJh3O6Q+HQSKNz6O8q\noCGf9IjlpPAdIuq/x352RT8l5qDEtLM4AIdMgUoC315HoUZ8HlKge9AzMmjI1Eb1\n46TwLKXDJ13OyPA9ugMv4+xafTVK0UEcyXZ+hduX78ftP0pczFieXsHdg1sKJx+j\nfBJuDgR9UxIpLjp9pl7cysfTmkj8Er0MtlFPaF8GgUbzL3NqB2Tfg90dZyf2ZtU/\nVAYwiv4rhL501Qc2tJnroABTNcvm00G0LKjuzrwEsCSDLUmsQH+D1M2Rc+WgKjgV\nGw5W7i/k4/ya7/BwVpZL\n=Mwq9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T17:31:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKGEyMTFkZjAxZmQyZTBkMWYwY2Y4OTFjMWZiNjhhMDQxNjJjNTVkMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281","sha":"68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281"}],"sha":"a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/a211df01fd2e0d1f0cf891c1fb68a04162c55d25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T17:20:43Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T17:20:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: widen header to match content edges, always left-align posts (#19)\n\nBlogHeaderShell nests two layers of \"px-4 sm:px-6\" padding (its own,\nplus the rounded card''s below), so the visible card sat noticeably\nmore inset than the page content beneath it at every viewport. Widening\nthe header''s max-width by 6rem (calc(var(--container-6xl) + 6rem))\ncancels that double inset — measured to ~1px alignment against the H1\nbelow, both on the blog post page and the home page, which share this\nheader.\n\nAlso reverts the post page''s TOC-less centering (added in #17) back to\nalways left-aligning the reading column. Centering meant a post''s\nstarting position shifted depending on whether it happened to have\nheadings; left-aligning keeps it consistent across every post,\nmatching where a TOC-having post''s column already starts. The\ngrid-reservation fix from #17 (no dead 220px gutter without a TOC)\nstays — only the centering behavior is reverted.","tree":{"sha":"a6dee9cea6e8f89b19877628d9a5a098e14671ca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/a6dee9cea6e8f89b19877628d9a5a098e14671ca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/68ebcd8cff990ed7fcc858d3b69306a218725281","verification":{"payload":"tree a6dee9cea6e8f89b19877628d9a5a098e14671ca\nparent 5deaf46dacc8d22358d5bf8a9d0425c61ae88555\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783531243 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783531243 -0300\n\nfix: widen header to match content edges, always left-align posts (#19)\n\nBlogHeaderShell nests two layers of \"px-4 sm:px-6\" padding (its own,\nplus the rounded card''s below), so the visible card sat noticeably\nmore inset than the page content beneath it at every viewport. Widening\nthe header''s max-width by 6rem (calc(var(--container-6xl) + 6rem))\ncancels that double inset — measured to ~1px alignment against the H1\nbelow, both on the blog post page and the home page, which share this\nheader.\n\nAlso reverts the post page''s TOC-less centering (added in #17) back to\nalways left-aligning the reading column. Centering meant a post''s\nstarting position shifted depending on whether it happened to have\nheadings; left-aligning keeps it consistent across every post,\nmatching where a TOC-having post''s column already starts. The\ngrid-reservation fix from #17 (no dead 220px gutter without a TOC)\nstays — only the centering behavior is reverted.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTobrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPpEQAAadar0zcALG5RAEdw+22TTZ\ny83fvlMjFNptr/iRUW2Ik7UfoNsKT+RJtEoIj3w0pm8/kgiuvQXaC9P+Zx6IAI2P\ne1M83zKJhd2xvYUUk9pNlGLA2z7f8GLgRTE3p47S5vViRW0VNPLfaRl7BVQwWt3O\nUTYHdHvD18SMuQmZ/Rjo7k+5yF4QeYgfnK9WHJxNwrCab07p4qQgq4T/oYUdX3eI\nus1HJ3sQTzYtGp/LgRlHEKJedYfoV80h3e3xEE5ZH+X4+dR3WEkRLNDf9yJ6cohM\n2BhLnz2ApAV7D8OfCDiCpOh4dH/wVHJcDIGAWq9wJd0QMyOZF2ThFA54dXPV1tOc\nDob5HBdi+cAzGaHhNp6sB5c1WUHFjYoyMkOg7PW/80UdxiCu8N5XcIfV/PJUHqti\nKbPIjb0O3rHzGWPyqMiME5/f7mn2cS483qzhfH3xQ/vyfYbUE0sZ/NvxPQ+tRS7B\nM/9woTbu81MnVj64c5QGHjayIg7/6OWn3ry7P+Wwf00xuGdqJQaWJE0RoIpKDBCH\nZmx14NynAHRPXz4KBMTnPndaqdC1dmf3kF1v1HDUvXVppbfedrfmOKFKiBhS8/47\nT4j/Y1JP3+zGpg2vDLZVo1shNuZyhx0pLRETuv07kY3tvHPGpFsJL+NoigqWmiQ7\nJOwmkylFaKgjAO8//GMR\n=la5i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T17:20:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/