tps://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/5deaf46dacc8d22358d5bf8a9d0425c61ae88555/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:57:56Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:57:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: restore side padding on post pages between 1024-1279px (#18)\n\nThe outer container dropped all horizontal padding at \"lg:\" (1024px)\non the assumption that its own max-w-6xl cap would already leave\nnatural centering margin beyond that point. That''s only true once the\nviewport is wider than 1152px — between 1024 and 1151px, max-w-6xl is\nwider than the viewport itself, so the removed padding meant the\nheader, article text, and TOC all touched the browser edges with zero\nbreathing room, unlike every other page''s header/nav which keeps its\nown padding regardless of width.\n\nMoves the padding drop from \"lg:px-0\" to \"xl:px-0\" (1280px) — the same\n72px value below the resulting original 1280px threshold is unaffected.","tree":{"sha":"24ca7b8babd448e1d332718e2f56d35cee066b47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/24ca7b8babd448e1d332718e2f56d35cee066b47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/5deaf46dacc8d22358d5bf8a9d0425c61ae88555","verification":{"payload":"tree 24ca7b8babd448e1d332718e2f56d35cee066b47\nparent bd6222931c4d6b93a1e6ec2997a02f2c587bd401\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783529876 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783529876 -0300\n\nfix: restore side padding on post pages between 1024-1279px (#18)\n\nThe outer container dropped all horizontal padding at \"lg:\" (1024px)\non the assumption that its own max-w-6xl cap would already leave\nnatural centering margin beyond that point. That''s only true once the\nviewport is wider than 1152px — between 1024 and 1151px, max-w-6xl is\nwider than the viewport itself, so the removed padding meant the\nheader, article text, and TOC all touched the browser edges with zero\nbreathing room, unlike every other page''s header/nav which keeps its\nown padding regardless of width.\n\nMoves the padding drop from \"lg:px-0\" to \"xl:px-0\" (1280px) — the same\n72px value below the resulting original 1280px threshold is unaffected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqToGUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjAUQAHS4IqvAWA4dibesg2K/FhKJ\nd/vFpqQBk1X7Gy66yq1dFAuBGoCbe1gV1GsON3CSyGV2PEgUg5loFjfpKr1Ac1T7\nldaQQCWvRUgXDhuBS5XTbG8B6vswzFGe73JL1RAs5c/B4mzYFes4Ye4ITNa2/Oxv\n7bCHKrbWEus4ukhvFGnZhHtgUqrd0fj8r+KMFqL5yjavnYtZFPG2vEnBgr3uJdXS\nfs/3GPTW7NKk9fVznI7aMow3GGCCfh8Zi2Lswv5sEaf6jid4pwtMzPAE99gMDGNb\nSYAFH9G/xcVX7XLg/cK7uoOozVcagX38l4hOKlJcv8ygezjWj+tDlCRFTCIKPFy4\n6dlvS1gPPvEv1WfweyU4XMVVkhWanMQO/q05EsqlOj+ZAWun19OhjfsxuJ10H8pm\nKa34WUuwrgwy5cvPuz3kKEPhC6/FKjACPC3fFc4rLJOcxi8j+eS+wTZMd3GwusIg\nLp+fVUsOAMbkWaKIb2imVmO+p9q73ItPMog046OYXuuqN34wNajgALOAnQGZtS1/\n2K7E+ZAko5ZqTU7eUaMQdSAI0b5FJzhG5HEhcoWYTzc8+BJ+vZbsssQu92dh4LRk\n3n4NTpBdtKIfIIa3qPOLyj2nouZkS0UWJmChDrJfj38DdWB621E8i0uh5WmDiE3b\nuQt3SEvmRCK/YzP9kxNO\n=6C+n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T16:57:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY