ana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/bd6222931c4d6b93a1e6ec2997a02f2c587bd401/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:30:53Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T16:30:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: correct back-arrow glyph offset and center TOC-less posts (#17)\n\nTwo small, precisely-measured alignment issues on the post page:\n\n- ArrowLeft''s own vector path leaves ~3.3px of unused space inside its\n  SVG viewBox, so the arrow visually sat ~3px right of the H1/paragraph\n  text below it despite both elements'' DOM boxes being pixel-identical.\n  A -ml-[3px] nudge on just the icon corrects this (measured down to\n  ~0.3px after the fix).\n\n- The two-column grid (article + TOC) was applied unconditionally, so\n  grid-template-columns still reserved the TOC''s 220px+gap track even\n  on posts with no H2/H3 (extractHeadings returns an empty array,\n  TableOfContents renders null) — leaving article content stuck to the\n  left with a dead gutter on the right instead of reading as a normal\n  centered single column. Both the grid and the \"lg:mx-0\" left-align on\n  the content wrapper are now conditional on headings.length > 0.","tree":{"sha":"2ce555e19e05d90a27bf9507376ea5dfad26b868","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/2ce555e19e05d90a27bf9507376ea5dfad26b868"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/bd6222931c4d6b93a1e6ec2997a02f2c587bd401","verification":{"payload":"tree 2ce555e19e05d90a27bf9507376ea5dfad26b868\nparent 1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783528253 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783528253 -0300\n\nfix: correct back-arrow glyph offset and center TOC-less posts (#17)\n\nTwo small, precisely-measured alignment issues on the post page:\n\n- ArrowLeft''s own vector path leaves ~3.3px of unused space inside its\n  SVG viewBox, so the arrow visually sat ~3px right of the H1/paragraph\n  text below it despite both elements'' DOM boxes being pixel-identical.\n  A -ml-[3px] nudge on just the icon corrects this (measured down to\n  ~0.3px after the fix).\n\n- The two-column grid (article + TOC) was applied unconditionally, so\n  grid-template-columns still reserved the TOC''s 220px+gap track even\n  on posts with no H2/H3 (extractHeadings returns an empty array,\n  TableOfContents renders null) — leaving article content stuck to the\n  left with a dead gutter on the right instead of reading as a normal\n  centered single column. Both the grid and the \"lg:mx-0\" left-align on\n  the content wrapper are now conditional on headings.length > 0.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTns9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbMEQAHF7V60UgFFcMDqYUmdMFDtM\nwiuYFzz3ITlg6eIwSFrBaZz/OhTEVC5rfmNTLUahZUyOtQMi9T0msSfFasmrNbqG\n54r99NWnY+UTYeEF03rtzJ6BoTXx907PAUm3nVqgBppVB22DjWlICSTgLC0N4Ysd\nVWBIxUH5AyNrHzjaxqzbSbqVDLcQkd/PSqXenRLXqzKeRM5uR8nBbmZN7nFhJ1om\n7ZiTQ0uPmU1mGf8iR35xb6Rmi5hYjsOL5u2Tr3/c4RRB5WSB+e7s8wb3xLkGJOvo\nBQkxGTw3RpkybZ6Kxdhm34oO/wHSp7V/pQ2qzEPgLfrEA2ePXlw45NC9lzJNIy1i\nksM1u/PAUNyoXKMkk4xB+xzMouuTAbD+GAwMqoh4sintWhJaPTjQ9jgvDrXspISc\n15fxdJNqfKtvU0Y+z3oNHg+IlED8YcSM7VZgeDwc9o08Ke6kx/fvuyw+7YUBczgm\naNPNfFd5FQBHY7/TedEz9byBRPlK+swrwDG6zHWY+4FcQ6kMGu5Rlwlhmc5XrbRz\nxIzj+JAJz9twcQnY8oWFpeNPDoT2ThblXp//zfSoi9jlaCmrQMZOkGtO1a45o+f6\nyR80mrQnJwxyzvsUkGbI0cjxV2r+qzcpKIe0uSBmwiCez4rAQaWF5aF5PY5n09Nk\nvzC5fPOR6DiJ+p4I0Zz2\n=Ak2y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T16:30:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.c