rl":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:32:52Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:32:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: align post header, article body, and comments to one left edge (#16)\n\nThe header block and the comments section each had their own\nindependent \"mx-auto max-w-3xl\" wrapper, centered within the page''s\nfull lg:max-w-6xl container. The article body''s wrapper, by contrast,\nused \"lg:mx-0\" to left-align against the grid''s first column instead\nof centering. On large screens this put the H1/meta ~192px out of step\nwith the article text directly below it.\n\nCollapses all three into a single \"mx-auto max-w-3xl lg:mx-0\" wrapper\nthat is the grid''s first column, so the header, prose, and comments\nare plain block children of the same box and can''t drift apart.","tree":{"sha":"cadf662a0529e47a88f1ea429c97566fab4195c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/cadf662a0529e47a88f1ea429c97566fab4195c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16","verification":{"payload":"tree cadf662a0529e47a88f1ea429c97566fab4195c4\nparent cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783524772 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783524772 -0300\n\nfix: align post header, article body, and comments to one left edge (#16)\n\nThe header block and the comments section each had their own\nindependent \"mx-auto max-w-3xl\" wrapper, centered within the page''s\nfull lg:max-w-6xl container. The article body''s wrapper, by contrast,\nused \"lg:mx-0\" to left-align against the grid''s first column instead\nof centering. On large screens this put the H1/meta ~192px out of step\nwith the article text directly below it.\n\nCollapses all three into a single \"mx-auto max-w-3xl lg:mx-0\" wrapper\nthat is the grid''s first column, so the header, prose, and comments\nare plain block children of the same box and can''t drift apart.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTm2kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR80QAC5xLPkeXQN6uEmwSpU+xzo0\nnY/u3KEjfeA9oIm7jwymws0Hc3wk5u6gmGNVDNvNnosWH+jHdX66vq7vAWjhiFCv\nhNqi91oWPWG20kYvQZ7gxqAbZj0om3DDDt/EZk/8bixO6ykStHDl0Mf0fptF96Ga\n06s95ChCD613thSHuGDxQofGdXCDFG3dfFlraE1RAAHiw/edxCrVg6m1vZZReEQf\nBr8rhWHBkd5QVRCPmVktTUw3+Q4u/Y2QkJxCKTT7C78foLC823PRAyE5Y7P5b0eG\nM2xl4OfULSAsV5G+9LchbADQPEv7c+b29PJCTAhyiSphViF6QyjevtfQidhNguyJ\nOInw1RzgItCG4W42+DUq00xhDOoEn5ELW02XTfW/Bs4ngjgRk9crgv0ud13kDyw8\n/Mf8YXRuAmpAfvpr31HoAa7Mn6egNFxWM4XqGB6tjlBvvGmIXhx24PgRyAXd6W2d\n2uJg5EyrlhATnTKNZV5C7zqoxFtoznkJAtxY5R0ZqGRv7sQuwk/g8+20yxusxpoO\nM2uFY4KeKZUm4fCMKolIL/dJ/G/tFtc0mQHXZaI0XdPJpeUsMNFuKFiLzd8AQbWs\nbfAaIdUPjG1EvQIjpESM9yEqba3mq8U4nsOEjRJ7oHdntDCnjHQahlo6mNh9G7dR\nV9bqhwcZTFGAsXFGyR1Z\n=h7nI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T15:32:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDFiZWM1YjViOWJkOGFjYWRlMmJmZmNkNzA4OTgyYjY2YjQ0NmRlMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778","sha":"cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778"}],"sha":"1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/1bec5b5b9bd8acade2bffcd708982b66b446de16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:22:28Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T15:22:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add an auto-generated table of contents to post pages (#15)\n\nExtracts H2/H3 headings from a post''s Markdown into a deduplicated,\nslugified list (extractHeadings), then threads that same list into the\nMarkdown renderer so the sidebar and the actual heading anchors share\none source of truth instead of two independent slug implementations\nthat could drift apart.\n\nmarkdownHeadingComponents becomes a factory (createHeadingComponents)\nthat still shifts heading levels down one (unchanged behavior) and now\nalso injects matching ids on h2/h3 when a headings list is passed.\n\nTableOfContents is a sticky, desktop-only sidebar (client component)\nthat highlights the current section via IntersectionObserver\n(useActiveHeading) as the reader scrolls, including a fallback for\nshort final sections that can''t otherwise scroll into the detection\nzone.\n\nPost page layout widens to make room for the sidebar on large screens\nwhile the actual reading column stays pixel-identical to before.","tree":{"sha":"3494436fb41403425c801501bddd753f895ce8ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/3494436fb41403425c801501bddd753f895ce8ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/cb35a84d3631730c497ecdf02daf3de64d5b7778","verification":{"payload":"tree 3494436fb41403425c801501bddd753f895ce8ae\nparent d2fa845fa2b06462392f5fcbc7017e5dd533b476\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783524148 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783524148 -0300\n\nfeat: add an auto-generated table of contents to post pages (#15)\n\nExtracts H2/H3 headings from a post''s Markdown into a deduplicated,\nslugified list (extractHeadings), then threads that same list into the\nMarkdown renderer so the sidebar and the actual heading anchors share\none source of truth instead of two independent slug implementations\nthat could drift apart.\n\nmarkdownHeadingComponents becomes a factory (createHeadingComponents)\nthat still shifts heading levels down one (unchanged behavior) and now\nalso injects matching ids on h2/h3 when a headings list is passed.\n\nTableOfContents is a sticky, desktop-only sidebar (client component)\nthat highlights the current section via IntersectionObserver\n(useActiveHeading) as the reader scrolls, including a fallback for\nshort final sections that can''t otherwise scroll into the detection\nzone.\n\nPost page layout widens to make room for the sidebar on large screens\nwhile the actual reading column stays pixel-identical to before.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTms0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7AEQAD8cr5UcKq/mJ/6blnky4D+5\nbP9pWuQKKNpaDrSywNiqnEpGPYRVoW0hDoGOU7+mnQjHk3SVn1zl4EUULVuEd1Ww\nnLlvdceg2TM3e26Kd+8GzAb1KtGkpNe3HgI0OESFOZFw2y4Z0Ahrgd8O31LX+gWy\nEdxCwjcGtMa0vo7H4FpcvvG/kSdskJJ/OAZqXefGpyBHvlz5m9c1CYZuIhx5wU90\nJqlsV048293UjHfx/yeULxR2sJLUrHDAyUEJ4jVFir043bLzQ7Rjd9QL8BWQMnhs\n3g2bVohV2Zgp99Vf6BnM8reCejryrmW23APhVhGahwTazlJ1UZ6uwz+VwhaxOwfp\nGwDFZChpmHvNaAG932UK+MwqcudCnongdNa7vZJqFr+0sBanNcQe/Lvc7sjvvEvn\nwUcR41lSlNM3RiLKK8FaXmF0cckEom8AKNsWLJNKpqE6pqCt7CZlck/q2LZeqYrU\ngVmRUSJSfG5S5pB4qiVni6XharYOgeBNuhtmTbE507s4k/Ac5Bvf5sYnA6pOxxDx\nTWxx7WJwRz+/bxdrHXhjKlqFUCP/YnqjFXVoTWaga+gCNAJ+cck7g33FiYLRNYdM\nK2c8ONi68WR53ElZ2r7m/NgUfpcnCblIZ1IkCY/epZkXGxZQDjJrYmo50K91nY0I\nwD1xfAMTAehiFFQ1T3rl\n=gNdD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T15:22:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://ava