ntent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/76f498fd4e41558db80f3397dd201c8faa526705/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:12:54Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:12:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: address remaining medium-severity accessibility findings (#10)\n\nCover-image alt text: posts had no data-model field for it (only\ncoverUrl), so an admin could never supply real alt text for a cover\nimage even when it was meaningful (a diagram, screenshot) rather than\ndecorative. New optional coverAlt field on both post forms, used as\nthe actual alt attribute on the home grid card and the article hero\n(backend column in the paired vertex-api PR); falls back to alt=\"\"\nwhen unset, same as before.\n\nHeading structure risk from user-authored Markdown:\n- blog/[slug]/page.tsx''s ReactMarkdown now remaps every heading level\n  down by one (h1->h2 ... h6 stays h6) via a shared\n  markdownHeadingComponents helper, so a post body that itself\n  contains \"# Something\" can no longer produce a second, competing h1\n  next to the page''s own <h1>{title}</h1> — this was a guaranteed\n  conflict whenever an author used a top-level heading in the body,\n  not just a hypothetical.\n- about/page.tsx had no hardcoded heading at all; the entire structure\n  depended on whatever the admin''s Markdown happened to contain. Fixed\n  with a conditional sr-only <h1> that only renders when the content\n  doesn''t already start with its own \"#\" heading — verified against a\n  real render that this produces exactly one h1 either way, not zero\n  and not two (an earlier version of this fix that always rendered the\n  sr-only h1 produced a real duplicate against content that does start\n  with a heading, caught by checking the actual output rather than\n  trusting the diff).\n\nSkip-to-content link: BlogHeaderShell now renders a\nvisually-hidden-until-focused \"Skip to content\" link as the very first\nfocusable element, targeting a new id=\"main-content\" added to <main>\nin all three layouts ((blog), blog/, (blog-admin)).\n\nFocus ring contrast: focus:ring-emerald-500/50 computed to ~2.67:1\nagainst the dark backgrounds it''s used on, under the ~3:1 WCAG\nnon-text-contrast guidance for focus indicators. Bumped to /70\n(12 occurrences across 7 files) — still a soft glow, not a harsh ring,\njust visible enough to meet the bar.\n\ni18n: BlogMobileNav''s hamburger button had hardcoded Portuguese\naria-label strings (\"Abrir menu\"/\"Fechar menu\") instead of going\nthrough next-intl, so an EN/ES-locale screen-reader user heard\nPortuguese for the one thing in the header that wasn''t translated.\nRouted through Navigation.openMenu/closeMenu instead.\n\nVerified: full Vitest suite (45 tests), full Playwright suite\n(13 tests), tsc --noEmit, lint, and a production build all pass. Also\nmanually confirmed via a running dev server against real content: the\nskip link and main#main-content both render, /about renders exactly\none h1, and a real post''s body heading renders as h2 (not h1) next to\nthe post''s own h1 title.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d2fb875d302cd9b49505625c5c0820b50247cf3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/2d2fb875d302cd9b49505625c5c0820b50247cf3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/76f498fd4e41558db80f3397dd201c8faa526705","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d2fb875d302cd9b49505625c5c0820b50247cf3\nparent b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783469574 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783469574 -0300\n\nfix: address remaining medium-severity accessibility findings (#10)\n\nCover-image alt text: posts had no data-model field for it (only\ncoverUrl), so an admin could never supply real alt text for a cover\nimage even when it was meaningful (a diagram, screenshot) rather than\ndecorative. New optional coverAlt field on both post forms, used as\nthe actual alt attribute on the home grid card and the article hero\n(backend column in the paired vertex-api PR); falls back to alt=\"\"\nwhen unset, same as before.\n\nHeading structure risk from user-authored Markdown:\n- blog/[slug]/page.tsx''s ReactMarkdown now remaps every heading level\n  down by one (h1->h2 ... h6 stays h6) via a shared\n  markdownHeadingComponents helper, so a post body that itself\n  contains \"# Something\" can no longer produce a second, competing h1\n  next to the page''s own <h1>{title}</h1> — this was a guaranteed\n  conflict whenever an author used a top-level heading in the body,\n  not just a hypothetical.\n- about/page.tsx had no hardcoded heading at all; the entire structure\n  depended on whatever the admin''s Markdown happened to contain. Fixed\n  with a conditional sr-only <h1> that only renders when the content\n  doesn''t already start with its own \"#\" heading — verified against a\n  real render that this produces exactly one h1 either way, not zero\n  and not two (an earlier version of this fix that always rendered the\n  sr-only h1 produced a real duplicate against content that does start\n  with a heading, caught by checking the actual output rather than\n  trusting the diff).\n\nSkip-to-content link: BlogHeaderShell now renders a\nvisually-hidden-until-focused \"Skip to content\" link as the very first\nfocusable element, targeting a new id=\"main-content\" added to <main>\nin all three layouts ((blog), blog/, (blog-admin)).\n\nFocus ring contrast: focus:ring-emerald-500/50 computed to ~2.67:1\nagainst the dark backgrounds it''s used on, under the ~3:1 WCAG\nnon-text-contrast guidance for focus indicators. Bumped to /70\n(12 occurrences across 7 files) — still a soft glow, not a harsh ring,\njust visible enough to meet the bar.\n\ni18n: BlogMobileNav''s hamburger button had hardcoded Portuguese\naria-label strings (\"Abrir menu\"/\"Fechar menu\") instead of going\nthrough next-intl, so an EN/ES-locale screen-reader user heard\nPortuguese for the one thing in the header that wasn''t translated.\nRouted through Navigation.openMenu/closeMenu instead.\n\nVerified: full Vitest suite (45 tests), full Playwright suite\n(13 tests), tsc --noEmit, lint, and a production build all pass. Also\nmanually confirmed via a running dev server against real content: the\nskip link and main#main-content both render, /about renders exactly\none h1, and a real post''s body heading renders as h2 (not h1) next to\nthe post''s own h1 title.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTZYGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJicQADBR0n6BgBBH6nzn0yzXL3wf\nr5ct/y7caUJBVtovxAKZwSzDba4uhTPCVjZcLpObNlk93G+s4BLCvIFImWgw7A43\nuXlg405irfWKU+HR3qBR/VBDRIpQEQZJFWT6vdqfV70Iw+d6zIx99Y/ZTfyR0kd6\nhPN/kdqwa/+HxJVReUfb3aiNnVk+8aUAJsqt2gH6VboP26ZyAEok0LGukwa8lqtP\nQLTl4NB4K4dk/Kvpmj6b20otwnBRuQT84F1hBsdex+ZH1XokWxv68yYfmtFRzslH\nGpBD7R8V2q3a5B0ylavIn3LRLxpcY/ce2pEJ9UlfLvkZ+lgWUi9j/BN5+bcZsQsJ\naZhlOm1BP7qdKxLSos0/c8UT7WDJlr7iOoxQR5QrjQ7FfdPY3cMI0vRlbp8q6h85\ng7PkMUVjy0n8cJvQ7cI6yhLhAdcIv1F9/G1sSJMPtybk2vDNCh3UIIM5sockYOrI\npDmo6GWF7yXF7ZL12iIBrJfX0jZzfysdPMifNcUb6BDRvE0BhG2zJMJeAaEqFFbF\nL9SPKKMZYKn8QkvTdRS66xVcPWEg4O3xUU28yJSiRDYqz8/CUPLTReMXts41fTlN\nWpg12oAjttlKuN9yX7j1XasQbI0O2ZQ/Pu+TaTQ8cY7F+abRzZQKHeMF1+c7BSN6\nrBlQMDGVzFE5PopHo8Nm\n=HvPL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-08T00:12:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/76f498fd4e41558db80f3397dd201c8faa526705","node_id":"C_kwDOTOZb-9oAKDc2ZjQ5OGZkNGU0MTU1OGRiODBmMzM5N2RkMjAxYzhmYWE1MjY3MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commit/b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c","sha":"b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c"}],"sha":"76f498fd4e41558db80f3397dd201c8faa526705","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/76f498fd4e41558db80f3397dd201c8faa526705"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30626822?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/samuelcsantana","id":30626822,"login":"samuelcsantana","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNjI2ODIy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samuelcsantana","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/commits/b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T23:39:55Z","email":"samuel.ssa89@gmail.com","name":"Samuel Santana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T23:39:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: address critical accessibility gaps across dialogs, forms, and focus (#9)\n\nFull audit findings and rationale summarized below; this covers the\n\"blocks a real user\" tier — screen-reader/keyboard-only users and low-\nvision users specifically.\n\nDialog semantics (ConfirmDialog, LoginModal):\n- New shared src/hooks/useDialogBehavior.ts: moves focus inside on\n  open, restores it to the trigger on close, traps Tab/Shift+Tab\n  within the dialog, and closes on Escape. Covered by 5 real\n  interaction tests (fireEvent-driven, not just \"it renders\").\n- Both dialogs now get role=\"dialog\", aria-modal=\"true\", and\n  aria-labelledby pointing at their heading — previously an AT user\n  navigating in wasn''t told a dialog had opened at all.\n- Backdrop click now closes both (neither did before).\n- ConfirmDialog is reused for every destructive action in the app\n  (delete post/topic/user/comment/own account), so this one hook\n  fixes the same gap in every one of those flows at once.\n\nIcon-only buttons losing their accessible name on mobile:\n- AdminHeaderActions'' sign-out fallback and account-menu trigger, and\n  BlogLoginTrigger, all hide their visible text below the `sm`\n  breakpoint with no aria-label on the button itself — a screen\n  reader announced bare \"button\" for the header''s core auth actions\n  on any phone-width viewport. All three now carry aria-label.\n- AdminHeaderActions'' dropdown also gained role=\"menu\"/\"menuitem\",\n  aria-haspopup, aria-expanded, and closes on Escape (it didn''t\n  before, only click-outside).\n\nKeyboard-invisible admin controls:\n- The home page''s per-post Edit/Delete buttons were opacity-0 until\n  group-hover, with no group-focus-within fallback — opacity:0 doesn''t\n  remove an element from the tab order, so a keyboard-only admin could\n  tab onto a control with zero visual indication anything was focused.\n\nUnlabeled/placeholder-only form fields:\n- TopicRow''s inline rename input had neither a label nor a\n  placeholder — the worst case in the audit, announced as bare \"edit\n  text\". LoginModal''s email/password, CreateTopicForm''s name field,\n  CommentsSection''s textarea, and EditAboutForm''s content textarea\n  (previously a bare <span>, not a real <label>) all get proper\n  label associations now.\n\nErrors that were never announced:\n- Every validation/server error in every form was visual-only — zero\n  aria-describedby/aria-invalid/aria-live in the whole codebase.\n  CreatePostForm/EditPostForm now set aria-invalid + aria-describedby\n  per field (title, slug, content, coverUrl) tied to a matching error\n  id; every standalone error message across LoginModal, TopicRow,\n  CreateTopicForm, EditAboutForm, CommentsSection, and UserRow is now\n  role=\"alert\" (or role=\"status\" for the About form''s success message).\n\nContrast:\n- text-slate-500 computes to 3.1-4.2:1 against the slate-800/900/950\n  backgrounds it was paired with — under WCAG AA''s 4.5:1 minimum for\n  normal text. Replaced with text-slate-400 (6.9-7.9:1) everywhere it\n  was used for real content: timestamps, empty states, footer,\n  profile field labels, the login modal''s divider text, and more —\n  19 occurrences across 12 files, confirmed by grep after the change.\n\nNot in this batch (lower severity, tracked separately): cover-image\nalt text has no data-model field to source it from, user-authored\nMarkdown can produce a duplicate/missing h1, no skip-to-content link,\nfocus ring contrast is a bit under 3:1, and BlogMobileNav''s aria-label\nstrings are hardcoded Portuguese instead of routed through next-intl.\n\nVerified: full Vitest suite (45 tests, including the 5 new dialog-\nbehavior tests), full Playwright suite (13 tests), tsc --noEmit,\nlint, and a production build all pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"76cd85c77ec406e6fa96ac0161c7c1b341715c7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/trees/76cd85c77ec406e6fa96ac0161c7c1b341715c7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/samuelcsantana/vertex-web/git/commits/b7e1b6acd429b96ef387eff6481ca01660a11f1c","verification":{"payload":"tree 76cd85c77ec406e6fa96ac0161c7c1b341715c7b\nparent d2627f3c0b0b39b7aaf546714ad316a2455da5bb\nauthor Samuel Santana <samuel.ssa89@gmail.com> 1783467595 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783467595 -0300\n\nfix: address critical accessibility gaps across dialogs, forms, and focus (#9)\n\nFull audit findings and rationale summarized below; this covers the\n\"blocks a real user\" tier — screen-reader/keyboard-only users and low-\nvision users specifically.\n\nDialog semantics (ConfirmDialog, LoginModal):\n- New shared src/hooks/useDialogBehavior.ts: moves focus inside on\n  open, restores it to the trigger on close, traps Tab/Shift+Tab\n  within the dialog, and closes on Escape. Covered by 5 real\n  interaction tests (fireEvent-driven, not just \"it renders\").\n- Both dialogs now get role=\"dialog\", aria-modal=\"true\", and\n  aria-labelledby pointing at their heading — previously an AT user\n  navigating in wasn''t told a dialog had opened at all.\n- Backdrop click now closes both (neither did before).\n- ConfirmDialog is reused for every destructive action in the app\n  (delete post/topic/user/comment/own account), so this one hook\n  fixes the same gap in every one of those flows at once.\n\nIcon-only buttons losing their accessible name on mobile:\n- AdminHeaderActions'' sign-out fallback and account-menu trigger, and\n  BlogLoginTrigger, all hide their visible text below the `sm`\n  breakpoint with no aria-label on the button itself — a screen\n  reader announced bare \"button\" for the header''s core auth actions\n  on any phone-width viewport. All three now carry aria-label.\n- AdminHeaderActions'' dropdown also gained role=\"menu\"/\"menuitem\",\n  aria-haspopup, aria-expanded, and closes on Escape (it didn''t\n  before, only click-outside).\n\nKeyboard-invisible admin controls:\n- The home page''s per-post Edit/Delete buttons were opacity-0 until\n  group-hover, with no group-focus-within fallback — opacity:0 doesn''t\n  remove an element from the tab order, so a keyboard-only admin could\n  tab onto a control with zero visual indication anything was focused.\n\nUnlabeled/placeholder-only form fields:\n- TopicRow''s inline rename input had neither a label nor a\n  placeholder — the worst case in the audit, announced as bare \"edit\n  text\". LoginModal''s email/password, CreateTopicForm''s name field,\n  CommentsSection''s textarea, and EditAboutForm''s content textarea\n  (previously a bare <span>, not a real <label>) all get proper\n  label associations now.\n\nErrors that were never announced:\n- Every validation/server error in every form was visual-only — zero\n  aria-describedby/aria-invalid/aria-live in the whole codebase.\n  CreatePostForm/EditPostForm now set aria-invalid + aria-describedby\n  per field (title, slug, content, coverUrl) tied to a matching error\n  id; every standalone error message across LoginModal, TopicRow,\n  CreateTopicForm, EditAboutForm, CommentsSection, and UserRow is now\n  role=\"alert\" (or role=\"status\" for the About form''s success message).\n\nContrast:\n- text-slate-500 computes to 3.1-4.2:1 against the slate-800/900/950\n  backgrounds it was paired with — under WCAG AA''s 4.5:1 minimum for\n  normal text. Replaced with text-slate-400 (6.9-7.9:1) everywhere it\n  was used for real content: timestamps, empty states, footer,\n  profile field labels, the login modal''s divider text, and more —\n  19 occurrences across 12 files, confirmed by grep after the change.\n\nNot in this batch (lower severity, tracked separately): cover-image\nalt text has no data-model field to source it from, user-authored\nMarkdown can produce a duplicate/missing h1, no skip-to-content link,\nfocus ring contrast is a bit under 3:1, and BlogMobileNav''s aria-label\nstrings are hardcoded Portuguese instead of routed through next-intl.\n\nVerified: full Vitest suite (45 tests, including the 5 new dialog-\nbehavior tests), full Playwright suite (13 tests), tsc --noEmit,\nlint, and a production build all pass.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqTY5LCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQpUQADfixoAg3pOFdbLS/nXdx8EZ\nTa9j7sYx2UjkduSRE6q28+DsU695lxpXp6HTkX1oOiDV/NlFCyGZOlZPzTm8pxf5\n0MGiqScU4d23kuhI5vGmKiDswX5